eliveries, meetings and decisions so that practical dependencies do not get missed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spend time with teams on site, identify blockers and help find the right person or next action to resolve them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain simple, accurate project trackers, meeting notes, decision logs and status updates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare concise progress updates and raise delays, risks or unclear ownership early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn the business and progressively take on larger projects as your judgement and experience grow.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we are looking for</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">0–3 years of experience in project coordination, operations, engineering, procurement or a related area. Internships, working-student roles, student projects and relevant personal projects all count; extensive professional experience is not required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong bias toward action: you take the next useful step, follow through on details and do not wait to be chased.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity and motivation to learn how a manufacturing business works, including the willingness to ask questions and take feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good organization and clear communication. You can keep several small tasks moving and make sure owners know what is needed from them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A practical, resilient approach when plans change or the first attempt does not work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working on site and collaborating with colleagues across technical and operational teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree, vocational qualification or equivalent practical experience in engineering, business, operations or a related area.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German. English is an advantage.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Desirable experience</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Examples of taking initiative and completing a project, event, improvement or challenging task.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to manufacturing, engineering, construction, logistics or another hands-on environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with task trackers or project tools such as Excel, Jira, Asana, MS Project or similar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coordinating suppliers, quotes, meetings or deliveries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in learning project-management and operational improvement methods.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Benefits and important information:</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer top-decile compensation packages, bonuses and meaningful equity, to attract exceptional aerospace talent. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every employee is awarded stock options in the company, you will directly benefit from your own hard work and success. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive relocation support including flights, shipping and visas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch, dinner and drinks provided everyday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free access to shared company housing</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note, we are a fast paced, hyper-scaling startup. You will need to be comfortable working extended hours with high levels of autonomy, ownership, and flexibility, with contracts structured around a 48-hour working week. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to building an equitable and inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued, has equal access to opportunity, and can thrive. We welcome different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences—and believe our differences make us stronger. <br /><br />Please submit applications in English</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €65K – €75K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li> • €65K – €75K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/stealthrocketrystartup/special-projects-coordinator-germany-111","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1793450413},{"slug":"lead-plant-robotics-engineer-germany-140746","company_name":"Stealthrocketrystartup","title":"Lead Plant Robotics Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Lead Plant Robotics Engineer to develop the manufacturing solutions that allow us to mass-produce solid rocket motors. As the lead, you will own the robotic handling strategy for our pilot plant, from the first layout concept through commissioning and scale-up, and you will lead the robotics team.<br /><br />This is a unique opportunity to define how rockets are built at scale. The pilot plant is the blueprint for the production lines that follow, and the robotic cells you lead will handle containers, motor casings and energetic materials every day.<br /><br />About us<br /><br />We're a Germany-based rocketry startup currently in stealth mode, scaling up rapidly to meet the demand for high-performance, reliable, and scalable solid propulsion technologies for space and defense applications. We are building our first production facility, and are applying our knowledge toward serial production of solid rocket motors.<br /><br />We are working hard to build something truly spectacular.<br /><br />To thrive here you will need to be comfortable working at pace, with the autonomy to make decisions and execute on them quickly. If you're excited by hard technical challenges and want a role where you will make a real difference each day to the future of the company, we may be the place for you.<br /><br />At our company, job titles and career progression are earned, not determined by years of experience alone. They reflect the responsibility you take on and the dedication you bring to each project. If you're ready to rise to the challenge, we'd love to hear from you.<br /><br />Key responsibilities</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the robotics architecture of the pilot plant: robot selection, cell layouts, end-effectors, and handling concepts for buckets, transport boxes, motor casings and carriers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the development of robotic handling solutions for dosing, mixing, casting, curing and demolding stations, including the explosion-protection concept (enclosure, pressure-resistant encapsulation or ATEX-certified equipment).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define robotics requirements for the full line and manage the interfaces with automation, process engineering, ERP/MES and external integrators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the robotics engineering team and external suppliers, including specification, tendering, factory acceptance tests (FAT) and site acceptance tests (SAT).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive cycle-time, throughput and availability targets using offline programming, simulation and data from the pilot line.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the risk assessment and safety concept for robotic cells together with safety engineering (Machinery Directive, ISO 10218, ISO 13849).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we are looking for</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant professional experience (typically 3+ years) designing and commissioning industrial robotic systems, ideally in manufacturing or process environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead-level experience: you have led technical teams or acted as technical authority on a robotic project from concept to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of industrial robot platforms (ideally ABB, Fanuc), including programming, offline programming and simulation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of machine safety (Machinery Directive 2006/42/EC, ISO 10218, ISO 13849) and of structured risk assessment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on engineering mindset: you can move from a concept sketch to a CAD layout, and you can debug a cell on the shop floor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work with autonomy and at pace, and to communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in robotics, mechatronics, mechanical engineering, electrical engineering, or a related discipline; equivalent practical experience may also be relevant.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Desirable experience</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Robotic handling in explosion-protected or hazardous environments (Directive 2014/34/EU, TRGS 720 ff.), or with powders, pastes or chemicals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vision systems, force-torque sensing, or automated quality checks (X-ray or CT integration).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multi-robot coordination, gantry systems, or AGV integration at production scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with manufacturing execution systems (MES) and PLC integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building production capability from zero in a startup or scale-up environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Benefits and important information:</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer top-decile compensation packages, bonuses and meaningful equity, to attract exceptional aerospace talent. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every employee is awarded stock options in the company, you will directly benefit from your own hard work and success. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive relocation support including flights, shipping and visas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch, dinner and drinks provided everyday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free access to shared company housing</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note, we are a fast paced, hyper-scaling startup. You will need to be comfortable working extended hours with high levels of autonomy, ownership, and flexibility, with contracts structured around a 48-hour working week. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to building an equitable and inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued, has equal access to opportunity, and can thrive. We welcome different perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences—and believe our differences make us stronger. <br /><br />Please submit applications in English</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €80K – €100K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li> • €80K – €100K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/stealthrocketrystartup/lead-plant-robotics-engineer-germany-140746","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1793450413},{"slug":"senior-account-manager-nachhaltigkeit-berlin-153902","company_name":"Rootglobal","title":"(Senior) Account Manager - Nachhaltigkeit","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>No previous experience in the sustainability space? Don't worry, we are happy to help you grow into an expert and thought leader at Root! This role requires presence in our Berlin office and both German and English language skills.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>🌎 What we do</h2><h2><strong>We build software that helps companies along the food system get to Net Zero.</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">~31% of global GHG emissions originate from food-related activities. For the first time in history, climate performance has become an overall business performance indicator. Enterprises are mandated by regulatory bodies to disclose their climate performance, which leads to increasing pressure from investors, competitors, retailers, and consumers to <em>prevent and reduce</em> their CO2e emissions. Over the next 10 years, companies have set ambitious reduction targets that need to be met. Enterprise software and new business processes can help.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We raised &gt;€10m in funding, we launched our enterprise product, signed and onboarded some of the largest F&amp;B players in Europe, and put together what we believe is the best-suited early stage tech team in Europe. Will you be the next to join us? 🚀</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>🔭 What you will work on</h2><h3><strong>Your mission</strong></h3><pre class="prosemirrorCodeBlock"><code>Drive customer success as a trusted advisor and account manager for our enterprise customers. Own a portfolio end-to-end from onboarding and tool adoption through retention and ARR growth, co-developing new value propositions and building the trust-based relationships that turn customers into advocates.</code></pre><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><em><strong>Over the next 12 months you will:</strong></em></h3><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow annual contract values of existing enterprise customers</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate our impact into tangible business value for economic buyers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead renewal negotiations and drive upsell opportunities with existing customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expand our reach within global enterprises across new regions, teams, and decision-makers.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support customers' progress along their climate journey</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and nurture strong relationships with clients as their trusted climate advisor and single point of contact, coordinating internal expertise to deliver clear, actionable guidance on sustainability topics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent the customer voice and needs internally to provide input for product development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Educate users and guide them toward measurable progress on their Net Zero journey.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Boost farm-level data collection via the RootOS platform</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboard sustainability managers, farm technicians, and farmers to the platform and guide their data collection efforts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure high data integrity, partner with trusted farm-level data sources, and meet data coverage targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collect, consolidate, and prioritize product feedback.</p></li></ul></li></ol><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>🚀  You might be really good for this role if you</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have 3+ years of experience in customer-facing roles (ideally B2B SaaS, consulting, or startup/scale-up environments) where you built and nurtured strong client relationships end-to-end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ar