<li>Own the critical interfaces between systems and resolve technical conflicts when optimisation within one discipline damages performance somewhere else.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Lead major system-level trades around performance, mass, power, thermal constraints, controllability, reliability, manufacturability and operational capability.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Work closely with GNC and avionics teams to ensure sensing, estimation, control, computing, actuation and vehicle dynamics form a robust closed-loop system.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Challenge designs from first principles rather than accepting assumptions because they are conventional or inherited from previous programmes.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Lead technical readiness for major design reviews, integration milestones and flight tests.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Use test and flight data aggressively, turning unexpected behaviour and failures into design improvements rather than paperwork.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Work directly with Manufacturing and AIT to make sure the vehicle being designed can actually be built, integrated, tested and iterated quickly.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Make difficult technical decisions when information is incomplete, balancing engineering rigour with the speed required to deliver breakthrough capability.&nbsp;</li>
<br><strong>Who you are</strong><br>
<li>An exceptional multidisciplinary engineer who naturally thinks at system and vehicle level rather than only within a single subsystem.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Deeply technically credible, with a strong foundation in areas such as Systems Engineering, GNC, avionics, flight controls, vehicle architecture or complex aerospace system design.&nbsp;</li>
