<li>Able to understand a difficult technical problem quickly, identify the assumptions that actually matter and drive the team towards an answer.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Experienced making significant engineering trade-offs across multiple disciplines rather than optimising one component in isolation.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Comfortable moving between first-principles technical discussion and major programme-level decisions without losing depth.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Willing to get personally involved when a problem matters. You do not need a large team, perfect information or an established process before you can make progress.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Able to distinguish engineering rigour from engineering bureaucracy.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Confident challenging exceptional specialists in their own disciplines while remaining open enough to change your own mind when the evidence demands it.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Calm when things go wrong, intellectually honest when something is not understood and relentless about finding the real answer.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Motivated by the opportunity to build sovereign European defence capability and comfortable working on systems where the consequences of engineering decisions genuinely matter.&nbsp;</li>
