&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ripple/director-global-sdr-operations-london-406947","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793451321},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-london-94198","company_name":"Getscope","title":"Senior Software Engineer","description":"<h2>Our Mission:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope automates the data collection that's slowing down the physical world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standards are vital for the safety of our infrastructure. Spending hours manually documenting them is not.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dave is an inspector. Today he’s climbing through one of Europe’s biggest chemical plants, looking for the corrosion that could shut the whole site down, with a notebook and pen in hand. Tomorrow, he’ll spend even longer on the part of the job he hates: turning those scribbles into a report.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the AI-native data collection layer for the 2 billion field workers like Dave. Scope radically simplifies how inspectors collect data in the field, make decisions, and produce reports. Along the way, we’re building the largest dataset on the condition of the built world and the decisions experts make about it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a $2T market and we’re just getting started. We're growing rapidly, and already work with 7 of the top 10 companies in the space. Our customers inspect facilities and products for companies including AstraZeneca and SpaceX.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We take pride in our talent density, and have assembled a best-in-class team: acquired and future founders, people from institutions like Imperial, Carnegie Mellon and Oxford, and from firms like Palantir, Goldman Sachs and Flexport .</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since launching from Entrepreneurs First in 2024, we've raised an oversubscribed $20m round led by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.indexventures.com/">Index Ventures</a>, the firm behind Figma, Revolut and Wiz, with over 100 unicorns backed to date.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real product ownership.</strong> You’ll go on site with inspectors, decide what matters, design it, ship it, and see whether it worked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The hard, interesting problems in AI.</strong> Field data is messy: voice notes, photos, video, half-finished sentences recorded in a chemical plant with no signal. Turning that into a report an expert will sign is a context-engineering problem nobody has solved well yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A small team that ships fast</strong>. We ship to production every day and put changes in front of inspectors within days, not quarters. Ideas go from a site visit to a live feature in a single sprint. If something doesn’t land, we learn why and iterate quickly. There are no layers of sign-off between you and the user.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> <strong>Redesign the mobile app</strong> for how inspectors actually work: gloves on, no signal, one hand holding on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> <strong>Build the systems </strong>that takes voice notes, photos, videos and proactively finishes reports without being annoying</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineer how we feed context to AI models</strong>: how to store, fetch and select standards, reports, media, user intention</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evolve our workflow builder</strong>: something between Retool, Webflow and n8n for inspections</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design the architecture behind the product</strong>: how unstructured data flows through the system, how AI is integrated, how offline and online behaviour stay seamless, and how we keep the product simple as it becomes more powerful.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re deeply technical.</strong> You’re a little bit sad that AI tooling creates more distance between you and the code, and you still like knowing how things work underneath.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re a manager of one.</strong> We believe great teams are made up of highly agentic people who care more about shipping results than collecting badges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ve got the scar tissue.</strong> You have 5+ years of experience and know which technical decisions matter, and which ones don’t.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ve shipped real applications.</strong> Ideally mobile, ideally with Expo or React Native. You care about the details that break in the real world: offline, flaky networks, error states.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re curious about AI as an engineering problem.</strong> You’re interested in getting messy real-world inputs into a model and getting something reliable back out, not just in calling an API.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Interview process</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An initial call with our talent team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative technical exercise with an engineer, usually in Typescript or Python.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An Interview with a cofounder - Jonny (CEO) or Jakob (CTO).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onsite Product Interview - Meeting more people on the team and getting a feel of what it would be like to work here.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Compensation and benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re in the office five days a week, so we’ve made it a great place to be.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">£120k–£150k base + significant equity, so you have a real stake in what you’re building</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">33 days’ holiday (including bank holidays, which you can take at your discretion.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bupa private medical: £0 excess, pre-existing conditions covered, digital GP, plus Bupa dental</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fresh meal prep delivered every week, a stocked fridge, and team lunch out every Friday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working late? Dinner’s on us, and so is your Uber home</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full visa sponsorship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">New MacBook and whatever tools you need</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible parental leave, including adoption leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular team events and off-sites</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £120K – £150K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £120K – £150K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/getscope/senior-software-engineer-london-94198","tags":["Engineering and Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793450414},{"slug":"customer-operations-specialist-europe-london-486188","company_name":"Plasma","title":"Customer Operations Specialist - Europe","description":"<h1><strong>About Plasma</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plasma is building the primary account for global money.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Money used to belong to a country. Increasingly, it belongs to a person or business moving through many countries. People and businesses now earn, spend, save, hire and invest across borders.  Traditional banks cannot serve this new world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first product, Plasma One, is a global money account: a place to receive, hold, send funds in seconds, earn yield and spend with a card in the local economy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Underneath is the Plasma network, built from first principles for stablecoin payments. Stablecoins make dollars faster, cheaper and more reliable to move.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity is to become where all global money lands first: where income arrives, balances grow, payments move, businesses operate, and new financial products are built.</p><h2></h2><h2><br /><strong>The Team &amp; </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://x.com/Plasma/status/2067634709727719601?s=20"><strong>Our Story</strong></a></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a global team of founders, operators and engineers, obsessed with building the best products. We work at the cutting edge of financial innovation, using stablecoins to create tools for consumers and businesses.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate with trust, clarity, and ambition: own your craft, move with urgency, contribute beyond your lane, back your teammates, debate rigorously, and keep raising the bar for what great means.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><em><strong>Customer Experience </strong></em></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plasma is scaling its customer-facing operations across international markets, and we’re growing the Customer Experience Team to match. You’ll join an established team and take ownership of coverage for the CET time zone, making sure our customers get great support when they need it most.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work across the full customer journey, from first contact through to resolution. Because we’re still building out our playbook, your input will directly shape the processes, standards, and team culture as we grow. You won’t just follow the process; you’ll help refine it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some flexibility in working hours &amp; weekend shifts will be needed to support coverage and the occasional busy period. We’re looking for a hard-working self-starter who thrives in a fast-moving startup environment and is committed to the mission alongside the rest of the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><em><strong>The role</strong></em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the customer experience day-to-day:</strong> Be the first person our customers reach when something goes wrong or they need help. You will handle inbound queries across chat, email, and support tooling, and take accountability for the quality and speed of every response.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the right hand of the Ops lead:</strong> Work directly alongside the Head of Operations to build out processes, identify gaps, and support decisions as we scale the team internationally. This is not a back-office support role. You will be involved in how we think about operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the foundations:</strong> We are early. Many of the processes, templates, and escalation paths do not exist yet. You will create them. From response frameworks to internal guides, you will help lay the groundwork the team will rely on as we grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support international team scaling:</strong> As we hire Ops team members in new markets, you will help onboard them, share knowledge, and maintain consistency in how we deliver for customers across regions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Spot problems before they become patterns:</strong> Track issues across the customer base, flag recurring themes to Product and Engineering, and help prioritise fixes that actually move the needle for customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work across teams:</strong> Collaborate with Compliance, KYC, and Product to make sure the customer experience is joined up, especially during onboarding and verification flows where things can go wrong quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent the customer internally:</strong> Your proximity to customer feedback is valuable. Use it. Bring customer insight into internal conversations and push for improvements that matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be Flexible with Shift Rotation: </strong>Most weeks you’ll work the normal Mon-Fri, however team members currently rotate weekend shifts which means that you may be required to work a weekend shift once every 6 weeks. You’ll then be able to take those days worked off the following week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><em><strong>The Bar</strong></em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1 to 3 years of experience</strong> in customer operations, customer success, or a support role, ideally within fintech, payments, or crypto. We will consider strong candidates from outside these sectors if the fit is right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Someone who takes ownership.</strong> You do not wait to be told. When something is broken or missing, you fix it or flag it. You hold yourself to a high standard even when no one is watching.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear and direct in how you communicate.</strong> You can write a helpful, professional response under pressure and explain a complex situation simply. You know the difference between being thorough and overcomplicating things.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competent English Language </strong>- our team communicates in english so being competent with the language is a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable with ambiguity.</strong> This is an early-stage company. Processes will change, priorities will shift, and some days you will be figuring things out as you go. You see that as interesting rather than frustrating. Preferably, you have worked at a fast-paced tech company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuinely curious about crypto.</strong> You do not need deep technical knowledge, but you need to understand the basics of how stablecoins and digital assets work and be motivated to learn more. Our customers live in this space.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organised under pressure.</strong> You can manage a queue, prioritise effectively, and keep quality high when things are busy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative by default.</strong> You work well with people in different functions, different time zones, and different levels of seniority. Building the team abroad means working with people you may never meet in person, and you are good at that.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><em><strong>Nice to have</strong></em></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience in a startup or scale-up</strong> where you had to build or rebuild processes, not just follow them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exposure to Intercom, Zendesk, Freshdesk</strong>, or similar support tooling in a live production environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Any familiarity with KYC or compliance workflows</strong> as they relate to customer onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience supporting or managing a small team</strong>, even informally, or helping onboard new colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An interest in how stablecoin and DeFi products work</strong> and the customer challenges they crea