al.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🎯 New-logo hunter:</strong> You generate your own pipeline through outbound and win new customers rather than relying on expansion or inbound.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📈 Track record:</strong> You have consistently hit or exceeded quota over the past two to three years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧭 Structured selling:</strong> You use a methodology such as MEDDPICC and navigate technical evaluations, procurement, legal and security reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📍 Location:</strong> You are based in the United Kingdom or Ireland and you already have the right to work there. This role covers the UK&amp;I territory and involves regular travel to customers in the region.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice-to-haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ Technical product background:</strong> You have sold developer tools, cloud infrastructure, data, AI or automation platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🤝 Partner-led deals:</strong> You have worked deals with system integrators or cloud partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 Open source or PLG exposure:</strong> You understand how community adoption turns into enterprise revenue.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join us?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will close the largest deals in our portfolio and shape how n8n sells to the world’s biggest organisations, with a product technical teams already use and love. You will work closely with Solutions Engineers, Partnerships, Customer Success and Product, and leadership will listen to what you learn in the field. n8n is growing at an exceptional pace, backed by a vibrant community and a remote-first culture built on autonomy, experimentation and high talent density. Apply now and help us bring AI-powered automation to the global enterprise.<strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>n8n is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We can sponsor visas to Germany; for any other country, you need to have existing right to work.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Our company language is English.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>You care about diversity and inclusion? We do too! Check out our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/Diversity-inclusion-and-belonging-n8n-c1bec2fff536422d868b1a438d990e35?pvs=21"><em>Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging initiatives at n8n</em></a><em> (</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/n8n/Diversity-inclusion-and-belonging-n8n-c1bec2fff536422d868b1a438d990e35"><em>https://www.notion.so/n8n/Diversity-inclusion-and-belonging-n8n-c1bec2fff536422d868b1a438d990e35</em></a><em>).</em></p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Location disclaimer:</strong> If you see multiple job postings for the same role, it is most likely because we're hiring remotely for this role and posting in different locations to make sure every potential candidate can see the role. Please apply to the location you're the most likely to work from in the future. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation</strong> 💸 – We offer fair and attractive pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership</strong> 💪 – Our core value is to “empower others,” and we mean it—you’ll get a slice of n8n with equity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work/life balance</strong> 🏖️ – We work hard but ensure you have time to recharge:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> 30 days of vacation, plus public holidays wherever you are.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US:</strong> 20 vacation days, 8 sick days, plus public holidays wherever you are.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; wellness</strong> 🩺 –</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> We provide benefits according to local country norms.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US</strong>: Multiple low-premium, low-deductible medical plans with coverage for individuals and families—plus a no-cost premium HDHP option with a pre-seeded HSA—along with dental and vision coverage.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Future planning</strong> 💰 –</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> We provide pension contributions according to local country norms.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US:</strong> 401(k) retirement plan with a 4% employer match.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial security</strong> 🛡️ –</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Europe:</strong> We provide benefits according to local country norms.*</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>US: </strong>Company-paid short-term and long-term disability insurance, plus life insurance to support you and your loved ones.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career growth</strong> 📈 – We hire rising stars who grow with us! You’ll get €1K (or equivalent) per year to spend on courses, books, events, or coaching to level up your skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A passionate team</strong> 🤩 – We love our product, and we prove it with regular hackathons where we see who can build the coolest thing with it!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first</strong> 🌏 – Our team works remotely across Europe, with regular off-sites for team bonding. Some roles, like sales in the US, are hybrid—please check the job description.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Giving back</strong> 🤝 – We're big fans of open source, and you'll get $100 per month to support projects you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transparency</strong> 🙏 – We all know what everyone’s working on, how the company is doing—the whole shebang.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*Country and/or State specific details provided in your employment agreement.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/n8n/large-enterprise-account-executive-uki-remote-uki-united-kingdom-260290","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1793450414},{"slug":"director-of-engineering-risk-and-compliance-london-354393","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Director of Engineering - Risk and Compliance","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role overview | Context</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> built its name serving the world's largest enterprises. We're now growing into many more types of customer: businesses of every size, including self-serve, startups integrating straight from our docs, and platforms (software companies, payfacs and marketplaces) that onboard thousands of sellers through our APIs. As our product range grows, that takes us from thousands of customers to millions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At that scale, the decision about who we work with, and on what terms, can't be a manual review at the end of a sales process. It has to be a product. It decides how quickly a good business goes live, how much it costs us to serve them, and how confident our regulators and scheme partners are in us. We're looking for a senior Engineering leader to own that decision.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This team decides which businesses we can work with and on what terms. It covers business verification, screening, underwriting, ongoing monitoring and financial crime. It's a shared platform that serves every one of our businesses. Its users are our customers (directly, or through the platforms they sign up with) and, internally, our Risk, Compliance and Financial Crime teams and the analysts who run reviews and investigations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Much of what we have today was built segment by segment and market by market, for a smaller number of large customers. The next chapter is one opinionated, configurable decisioning platform. Enterprise, platform and SMB customers should all run on the same foundations, with the right depth of checks and the right terms for each. That way a new product, segment or market doesn't mean rebuilding our controls, and this team isn't on the critical path for every launch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role overview | Risk, Verification &amp; Compliance</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The remit covers:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Risk decisioning:</strong> underwriting, risk tiering, exposure limits, reserves and settlement terms, and when to restrict or offboard, re-assessed across the customer lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business verification:</strong> company, ownership, document, bank account and website checks, run once for every segment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial crime:</strong> sanctions and PEP screening, AML and transaction monitoring, and the controls, audit trails and reporting behind our regulatory obligations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Decisioning platform:</strong> the shared infrastructure that runs these checks automatically for every market and customer type.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll partner closely with the teams that own onboarding and identity verification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role overview | Remit and Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be comfortable building and scaling critical platforms in a regulated environment, where correctness, auditability and availability matter as much as speed. You'll balance two goals that are often in tension: making it fast and easy for good businesses to work with us, and keeping bad actors out and the business compliant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a change role. You'll assess what we have, set a clear direction, and move us from segment-specific, analyst-led processes to an automated decisioning platform, without pausing the business while you do it. You'll do this in close partnership with Product, Risk, Compliance, Financial Crime and Legal, and with the leaders of the businesses that depend on the platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll directly lead an established team of engineers and managers of varying seniorities. Amongst other duties, you'll have impact across:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Setting the technical vision and strategy for Risk, Verification &amp; Compliance. That includes deciding what we build once and share, and what each segment, product or market configures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building a decisioning platform that automates the decisions that don't need a human, safely, and sends the rest to the right analyst with the context they need. Our automation rate sets our cost to onboard and to serve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Making risk dynamic across the customer lifecycle. New businesses start on terms that match the signals we see: limits, reserves and settlement speed. Those terms relax automatically as the business trades well, and we act quickly when the signals change. This starts with simple rules and evolves into machine learning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Making decisions explainable, so that customers, partners and our own analysts understand why a decision was made and what happens next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Giving Risk and Compliance the dials. Acceptance criteria, early-life controls and policy should be configuration that can be changed, tested and measured by cohort, not a code change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping our financial crime controls ahead of growth. Screening and monitoring have to scale from large enterprises to a very large base of smaller businesses, through new channels, payment methods and products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading the design and delivery of verification, screening, underwriting and monitoring systems that are accurate, auditable and highly available.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Representing Engineering in regulatory, audit, scheme and partner conversations where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing and developing a high-performing team of individual contributor (IC) Engineers and Engineering Managers, providing guidance, support and career development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Striving for best practice on hiring, coaching and enablement, and being a magnet for top talent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role overview | Desired Background, Core Competencies</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ideal candidate for the role will bring:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading multi-level engineering organisations (EMs and ICs) through growth and change, with a track record of developing leaders, not just hiring them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of transforming critical platforms while the business kept running: multi-year re-architecture, migrations, or consolidating several systems into one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and operating mission-critical decisioning or rules platforms at scale. Ideally these served several customer segments, products or markets from a shared foundation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a regulated environment (financial services, payments or similar), where compliance, auditability and risk are part of the engineering problem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep technical understanding of cloud-native, distributed and data-heavy systems, including how to run ML models safely in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional collaboration skills, with a proven ability to partner with senior cross-functional stakeholders, particularly in Risk, Compliance, Financial Crime and Legal, and to make clear trade-offs in a complex stakeholder landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, domain knowledge in KYB, AML and financial crime, underwriting, fraud or merchant risk. Experience with self-serve or high-volume onboarding, or with platforms and their sub-merchants, is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Humility, low ego and an ideal ambassador for our mission, values and operating principles.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you feel that you don't meet all the requirements but think you might still be right for the role, please consider continuing in the process. We're always keen to build relationships with leaders who resonate with our mission and values.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/director-of-engineering-risk-and-compliance-london-354393","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793450413},{"slug":"2027-strategic-finance-analytics-graduate-programme-london-268259","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"2027 Strategic Finance Analytics Graduate Programme","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>’s #NextGen Strategic Finance Analytics Graduate Program you’ll work alongside experienced professionals, gaining hands-on experience and a comprehensive introduction to digital payments and technology. The program offers an extensive learning experience through technical training, professional development workshops, and direct access to industry experts. You'll be part of a global Early Careers, Graduate community, with regular networking events, mentoring opportunities, and social activities designed to build connections and accelerate your growth and leadership potential. By the end of the scheme, you’ll be equipped with the knowledge, experience, and confidence to make a lasting impact at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a> and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How you’ll make an impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">During the programme, you may:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse commercial and business performance in order to help the business assess where it is creating value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage AI tooling as a force multiplier to build and automate reusable analytical workflows and agents to create insights from financial data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate directly with Data Engineering and Data Science to support the development and enhancement of our core financial data models, and the context layer that enables AI agents to leverage that data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Craft executive-style deliverables, which may include decks, models, written documents or AI-powered apps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with your manager to translate ambiguous requests from leadership, Finance and cross-functional stakeholders into clear, decision-ready insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive continuous reporting improvements, standardisation, and simplification whilst documenting definitions and limitations - leaving no room for approximation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work with Finance and Data partners to scope requirements and support the delivery of key initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a curious, analytical and innovative individual, either due to graduate in summer 2027 or having graduated within the last 12 months, who is excited to dive into the world of Finance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll bring:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a quantitative or business discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical mindset - You’re comfortable working with numbers, identifying the underlying patterns and drawing sound conclusions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent verbal and written communication skills - You have the ability to adjust your style to suit different perspectives and seniority levels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial curiosity - You want to dive into the details to understand how merchant, product, and commercial dynamics affect financial performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence with data tools - You have a clear aptitude and willingness to learn data tooling. Python and SQL experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional attention to detail - You rigorously validate data, pressure-test assumptions, and transparently communicate analytical limitations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payments or financial knowledge is a bonus, but not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early Careers experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll receive:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dedicated onboarding and payments-focused training.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional skills workshops and leadership sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentoring from experienced colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Networking and community events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunities to work on meaningful, business-critical projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular feedback and transparent performance conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Potential progression into a permanent role, subject to performance, readiness, headcount availability and business requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eligibility</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Graduated within the last 12 months or due to graduate by the programme start date, depending on the selected pathway.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Available to work full-time for the duration of the programme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to work from the stated programme location and meet applicable right-to-work requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/2027-strategic-finance-analytics-graduate-programme-london-268259","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793450413},{"slug":"senior-specialist-account-management-london-230518","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Senior Specialist, Account Management","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>The Mission:</u></strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are seeking a visionary and results-oriented Senior Specialist, Account Management to nurture and maintain long-term relationships with our most strategic Enterprise accounts within the United Kingdom.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the business advisor and main point of contact to some of our most important accounts. You will act as the voice of our product and ambassador of our brand, delivering expertise, education, and mentorship to our merchants. The key for success here will be the ability to use your business savvy knowledge and the required gravitas to effectively communicate and influence at all levels to achieve mutually beneficial scenarios and promote our value proposition. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ideal candidate is an independent, high-achieving individual, able to stand out in an ambitious environment and excel through self-motivation and personal drive. If you are eager to join a thriving, fast-paced environment this is the role for you to make a difference. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>How you’ll make an impact</u> </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Grow a portfolio of existing enterprise merchants by identifying expansion opportunities, cross/upselling Checkout’s value add services, performance improvements, and other levers to increase our share of wallet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Crafting and executing on merchant specific account development plans, outlining clear opportunities for growth and paths to success. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Building high touch, consultative, and nurturing relationships with our merchants through regular and open communications, both face-to-face and virtual.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Delivering expertise, education, and guidance to merchants. Act as their payment consultant as they craft and complete a comprehensive, global payments strategy. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Negotiate win-win pricing structures by growing a thorough overview of a merchant's revenue drivers to deliver the best, sustainable outcomes for both merchant and Checkout.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Tracking merchant project deliverables and ensure merchant activities are updated within SalesForce, Clari, and other CRM tools.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Understanding the intricacies of our products, services and partner networks thoroughly to leverage this against our merchants’ growing needs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Collaborating with various teams (e.g. Sales, Legal, Integration, Support) across the company to ensure an outstanding merchant experience and bring the voice of the customer to our internal stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Data-based decision making - not afraid of diving into numbers to ensure merchants have confidence in our ability to provide meaningful and metric-driven insights. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Drive a culture of cross-team learning through active knowledge sharing whilst contributing to improving ways of working, impacting not just ‘what’ we do but ‘how’ we do it. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Qualifications</u> </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Experience: 3+ years’ commercial experience in a B2B Account Management or Relationship Management role in the FinTech and/or Payments industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Commercial Acumen: Proven track record of driving and exceeding revenue targets and managing strategic account portfolios. Experience in negotiating and pricing strategy deals specific to the UK market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Payments Knowledge: Good knowledge of today’s major e-commerce and payments, technologies, players and major future trends.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">- Customer Obsession: Customer driven and able to establish a robust relationship with assigned customer base.<br />- Multifaceted approach adapting to changing requirements with the ability to balance multiple opportunities concurrently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/senior-specialist-account-management-london-230518","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793450413},{"slug":"manager-gtm-engineer-london-72900","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Manager, GTM Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, we create marketing that moves people to choose our products, builds a brand where great marketers want to work, and fuels the growth of our business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a GTM Engineer to join Marketing and help transform how we work internally. You’ll design and build AI-assisted workflows, agents and integrations that reduce manual effort, improve how information moves across the team and give marketers more time to focus on high-value work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marketing Operations Team owns our marketing technology and tools, and the automation that supports go-to-market execution across our channels. This role works alongside Marketing Operations, with a different starting focus: improving the internal processes, workflows and systems that help Marketing plan and deliver its work. The aim is to 10x our impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on technical role in a marketing team. You’ll spend around 70% of your time building: understanding how work gets done, finding where it is manual or breaking down, and shipping practical solutions. You’ll partner closely with Marketing Operations to make sure what you build fits our existing tools and standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work across Marketing, in close partnerships across Marketing Operations, Commercial AI Transformation and the AI Centre of Excellence. You’ll bring a clear technical point of view on what is scalable and reliable, while making sure the systems you build are useful to the people who need them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How You’ll Make an Impact</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Find the problems worth solving</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with teams across Marketing to understand their processes and the work behind their requests. Map workflows, identify manual effort, duplicated work, missing context and avoidable errors, then prioritise opportunities based on their potential value. You’ll use your creativity and judgement rather than simply build to a ticket.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Build AI-assisted workflows and integrations</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and ship agents, automations, skills and integrations that make internal marketing work easier. You might use Claude Enterprise, Copilot Studio, Clay, MCP connectors, coding agents or other tools across our marketing stack. Work with Marketing Operations when a solution involves our marketing technology or channel tools.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Make internal marketing work more efficient</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build workflows that help teams do the work behind marketing more efficiently, from briefing, research and insight gathering to planning, content development and hand-offs. Connect information and tools so people spend less time on repetitive coordination and more time on work that needs their expertise. Partner with Marketing Operations where workflows touch marketing technology or channel execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Build systems people can rely on</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design beyond the individual task. Consider the data, context, tools, users, hand-offs, controls and feedback loops a workflow needs to work well. Identify where information is missing, where an agent needs better direction or where teams need support to use and improve the system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Help marketers build with AI</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work alongside marketers to show what is possible and help them use AI with confidence. Create reusable patterns, skills, playbooks and guardrails so teams can solve more problems themselves and repeat good practice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Test, learn and improve</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prototype and test workflows, learn from how people use them, and improve or retire them based on the results. Identify design, security, privacy, brand and scale risks early, and follow our AI governance and review processes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Keep up with the tools</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay curious about new models, coding tools, connectors and agent patterns. Be able to explain which tools are right for a particular job and why, whether you’re comparing Claude, ChatGPT, coding agents or emerging platforms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You build things</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve made working automations, prototypes, integrations, agents, internal tools or products, and enjoy taking a messy problem through to something people can use. Your job title matters less than what you’ve built and the value it creates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You use AI hands-on</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use LLMs to get work done, not just to talk about what they could do. You’re comfortable prototyping with AI coding tools, testing different approaches, debugging and improving the result. You can show us something you’ve built with Claude, Codex, ChatGPT or another LLM platform, at work or in your own time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You have sound technical judgement</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can reason about systems, APIs, data flows, permissions and failure modes. You understand the difference between a promising demo and a dependable workflow. You don’t need a traditional software engineering background, but you do need to be comfortable working directly with technical tools and making sensible implementation choices.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You understand marketing and GTM</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand how demand generation, growth, customer marketing, marketing operations, sales and revenue processes connect. You’re familiar with concepts such as campaign briefs, segmentation, ABM, lead scoring, MQLs, MQAs, pipeline, attribution and lifecycle stages. You’re interested in the business outcomes behind the work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You’ve worked across marketing or RevOps tools</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve built or supported workflows across platforms such as Salesforce, HubSpot, Asana, Clay or similar tools. You can think across a stack rather than optimise one tool in isolation, and you’re comfortable with connectors, APIs, webhooks or MCP-style integrations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You know how to design useful workflows and agents</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can give a workflow the context it needs, choose the right tools, define hand-offs, involve people at the right points and make outputs easy to review. You understand that an agent’s performance depends on its data and operating environment as well as the model.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You prioritise for value</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can judge which problems are worth solving, which should remain manual and where a simpler answer will work better. You balance speed, quality, risk, maintainability and commercial impact, and can make a clear case for what to build next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You measure and improve your work</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable defining success measures, tracking usage and output, and deciding what to improve, stop or scale. You care about measurable gains in productivity, quality, speed or business impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You think in systems</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You look for the process behind the immediate pain point. When a spreadsheet is difficult to use, for example, you’re curious about the data, decisions and hand-offs that created it, and what would make the process work better. You can hold the bigger picture while working through the details needed to ship.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You communicate clearly and bring people with you</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can explain technical ideas to marketers, commercial leaders, Product, Engineering, Security, IT and Operations in a way that helps them make decisions. You listen well, communicate simply and influence through your work and judgement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You’re curious and self-starting</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable with ambiguity and motivated to learn. You’ve taught yourself new tools, built something outside your formal remit or pursued a technical interest in your own time. A personal project, prototype, automation, community contribution or other example could show us how you learn.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You use AI responsibly</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand that marketing systems need to be accurate, secure, explainable and aligned with our brand and company standards. You know when people need to review an output, when data should not be used and when an experiment is not ready to scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might come from marketing technology, marketing operations, growth engineering, RevOps, automation engineering, product, full-stack engineering or another technical role close to commercial teams. What matters most is your curiosity about marketing, your judgement about what is worth improving and your ability to build practical solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/manager-gtm-engineer-london-72900","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793450413},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-agentic-search-web-rendering-chromium-244360","company_name":"Nebius","title":"Senior Software Engineer (Agentic Search) – Web Rendering (Chromium)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a rapidly evolving world, trust in AI depends on AI agents being grounded in fresh, verified real-world data. Search is the foundation that makes this possible. We are building an agent-native search platform designed specifically for AI systems rather than human users. Our product provides programmatic, low-latency, and observable search APIs that AI agents use to retrieve, filter, and reason over real-world information at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to work on the rendering infrastructure of a novel search engine tailored for agentic AI consumption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will focus on loading modern web pages in a browser that we patch and build ourselves, so that content is rendered completely and reliably at a cost that works across billions of pages. You will work inside Chromium to remove what we do not need, make the rest faster and cheaper, and keep our build current as Chromium moves. Your work ensures that high-quality content is consistently available to the indexing and retrieval systems downstream.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, your responsibility will be to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Change Chromium in its heavy core (Blink, the V8 integration, the compositor, the network service) to cut CPU, memory and startup cost per page&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strip Chromium down for agent workloads: skip what nobody needs, such as image and media decoding, web font downloads, and rasterization and GPU work where no one needs pixels, while keeping what page scripts depend on to run correctly (style, layout, animation frames, observers), and work out what breaks, or renders differently, when you do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the browser compatible with the web: make sure that what we remove does not change how the sites we load behave or render&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Profile and tune fleets of browsers: the process model, memory per renderer, startup, isolation and crash handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the production system around it: how browsers are launched, pooled, recycled and monitored&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have 5+ years of experience building production systems, and are an expert in several of the following areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inside the browser&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong C++ in a large, performance-critical codebase, ideally Chromium, Blink or V8, or a comparable browser engine (Rust is a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chromium architecture: the process model, Mojo IPC, the rendering pipeline (DOM, style, layout, paint, compositing), and the network service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building, debugging and shipping custom Chromium builds: the build system, tracing, crash analysis, and maintaining patches across releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance and systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Profiling CPU, memory and I/O for browser fleets, with tools such as perf, tracing and flame graphs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux process isolation and resource management, concurrency, and memory management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have run browsers in production, or built the infrastructure that does, and can describe where the time and memory went&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have experience with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to Chromium, Blink, V8, Firefox, WebKit or another browser engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building or maintaining a patched browser that you wrote the patches for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Browser instrumentation, including the Chrome DevTools Protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working familiarity with how modern frontend frameworks render (SSR, CSR, streaming, hydration)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems, Kubernetes, and Go or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The kind of problems you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cut the cost of loading a page in half. Where do CPU and memory go, and what would you change in the browser?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn off the GPU and image decoding for agent workloads. What breaks, and what changes in how pages load and render?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A page runs a script that never yields. How do we detect and stop it without help from the page?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chromium ships a new version. How do we bring a large set of patches forward in days, not weeks?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide when a page is finished, for pages with analytics beacons, long polling and endless scrolling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We conduct coding interviews as part of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
