 management skills with the confidence to push back, calibrate and advise senior hiring leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort managing a varied req load across functions and seniority levels, and prioritising with sound judgment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High agency, high ownership and strong attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of hiring bar-raising talent in competitive markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in a fast-changing, 0 to 1 environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong sourcing discipline and the ability to build pipeline without relying on inbound or agencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A builder mindset: you improve the system while delivering the work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in, or willing to relocate to, London, and comfortable working from our London office.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Makes You Stand Out</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have helped build early teams in new international markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have recruited for frontier AI, developer tools, infrastructure, cloud or enterprise software companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have hired across both technical and G&amp;A roles, and can switch between them easily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience partnering with regional stakeholders, founding country leaders and/or G&amp;A leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable moving between strategic talent mapping and hands-on execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care deeply about quality, not just speed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know how to close candidates who have multiple options.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our Commitment</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunity.</strong> Cognition is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected characteristic under applicable law. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for candidates with disabilities throughout the hiring process - please let us know if you need any. Cognition also considers applicants with criminal histories consistent with the SF Fair Chance Ordinance and similar local laws.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data Privacy and Arbitration:</strong> By submitting your application, you agree to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://cognition.com/documents/Cognition-Global-Applicant-and-Job-Candidate-Privacy-Notice.pdf"><u>Global Applicant and Job Candidate Privacy Notice</u></a>. For US applicants, by submitting your application, you agree to the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://cognition.com/documents/Cognition-Applicant-Arbitration-Agreement.pdf"><u>Applicant Arbitration Agreement</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cognition/recruiter-europe-london-291784","tags":["General & Administrative"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793428828},{"slug":"remote-lead-engineer-air-343548","company_name":"Uforce","title":"Lead Engineer, Air","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE is looking for a <strong>Lead Engineer, Air</strong> to take hands-on technical ownership of our first Western-facing air product, turning operational lessons from Ukraine into a reliable, manufacturable system that customers can test, deploy and reorder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your initial focus will be one product. You’ll bring engineering, manufacturing, supply chain and field teams together around a controlled design and a clear delivery plan, resolving the reliability and integration challenges that stand between today’s product and repeatable production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on technical leadership role, not a management-only position. You’ll stay close to the hardware, own system-level engineering decisions and ensure that changes are proven through testing and reflected in what we build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our air portfolio expands, there is potential to grow into broader technical leadership, including Chief Engineer, Air. Progression will depend on business need and demonstrated performance, rather than a fixed promotion timetable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Establish product ownership and a delivery plan.</strong> In your first 30 days, assess the current design, customer requirements and test evidence with engineering, manufacturing and field teams. Identify the highest-priority risks and agree a 90-day plan with clear owners, milestones and acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Create a controlled technical baseline.</strong> By day 60, establish practical requirements, configuration records, bills of materials, interface definitions and change control so teams know what has been approved, built, tested and deployed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead end-to-end systems integration.</strong> Own technical trade-offs across airframe, propulsion, power, avionics, flight control, communications, navigation, payload interfaces and ground systems, drawing on specialist expertise where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve reliability and demonstrate performance.</strong> During the initial three to five months, establish a failure-reporting and corrective-action process, address priority failure modes and verify improvements through repeatable ground and flight testing against agreed requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prepare the product for repeatable production.</strong> Partner with manufacturing and supply chain on design for manufacture, component qualification, approved substitutions and supplier risks. Release a production package covering drawings, BOM, assembly requirements, inspection and acceptance tests, supported by a costed BOM and cost-reduction priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enable credible customer trials and delivery.</strong> Define approved configurations, test plans and readiness criteria. Validate capability claims, document operating limits and provide clear engineering input on delivery feasibility, support needs and technical risks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Connect operational experience to product development.</strong> Work closely with Ukrainian product experts and international teams to preserve field knowledge, manage configuration differences and translate operator and customer feedback into prioritised product changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build a foundation for portfolio growth.</strong> Identify reusable architecture, components and engineering practices, recommend capability and resource needs, and review the scope for broader ownership with leadership as the portfolio develops.</p></li></ul><h2>Required Skill</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on UAS engineering ownership:</strong> Experience leading delivery of a complete air vehicle or substantial integrated UAS product, with clear evidence of your own technical decisions and their impact on flight performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems integration judgement:</strong> The ability to reason across mechanical, electrical, flight-control, communications, navigation and software interfaces, and recognise when specialist depth is needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prototype-to-production experience:</strong> Meaningful involvement in taking an aerial product into repeatable production, including design for manufacture, configuration control and production testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliability and test discipline:</strong> A track record of diagnosing flight or field failures, identifying root causes and proving corrective actions through repeatable testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional technical leadership:</strong> The ability to set priorities, coordinate engineers and specialist partners, and drive delivery through influence as well as formal authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cost and component judgement:</strong> Practical understanding of how design decisions affect availability, qualification, unit cost, manufacturing quality and applicable sourcing requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational awareness:</strong> Understanding of how GNSS denial, jamming, communications resilience and operator feedback influence UAS design and testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Startup execution:</strong> Comfort working close to hardware, making decisions with incomplete information and balancing delivery speed with appropriate engineering control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear communication and ownership:</strong> The ability to distinguish demonstrated capability from development goals, explain limitations and escalate technical, safety or resource risks early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel regularly to engineering teams, manufacturing sites, test ranges and customers.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience working with Ukrainian UAS teams, products or operators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience adapting products for Western defence customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with applicable NDAA, Blue UAS and export-control requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting customer trials, military qualification or airworthiness activity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with payload integration or payload-release systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coordinating engineering and manufacturing across countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of growing from hands-on product ownership into broader technical leadership.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/remote-lead-engineer-air-343548","tags":["Hardware"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom | Remote","created_at":1793428828},{"slug":"people-operations-generalist-london-161454","company_name":"Goodstack","title":"People Operations Generalist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’ve been looking to join a fast-growing startup with a bold vision of <strong>a world where doing good is built into everything we do</strong>, then you’ve found the right place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by General Catalyst, the same investors behind Stripe and Airbnb, we’re building something truly extraordinary.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission at Goodstack is to <strong>revolutionize how the world does good 🌎.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a fast growth, AI-native social impact startup, we power global change through technology. We enable companies to seamlessly integrate positive impact into what they do through a unified platform while supporting nonprofits in gaining access to cutting-edge technology and finding new funding streams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global brands, including <strong>Google, OpenAI, TikTok, LinkedIn, HSBC, Atlassian and Twilio</strong> - as well as thousands of nonprofits, including the Red Cross, Cancer Research, and Oxfam - use Goodstack to make a difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In 2025 alone, we facilitated <strong>$5 billion in donations</strong> to good causes. But this is just the beginning. We're building the world’s leading platform that powers donations to nonprofits globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To keep our momentum and deliver consistently high value to our partners, we need incredible people to help us on our journey – <strong>we need you 🫵</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Join us as People Operations Generalist to </strong>help us build a People function that is simple, dependable and ready to scale.</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Goodstack is growing quickly across multiple countries, and we need someone to take ownership of the day-to-day operations behind our employee experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with the Head of People &amp; Culture, taking responsibility for the operational side of the function so that our people, managers and teams get the support they need.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who's brilliant with detail, takes ownership from start to finish, spots problems early, and enjoys finding simpler ways of working.</p><h2><strong>As People Operations Generalist, your mission will be to:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own day-to-day People operations across the employee lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare contracts, amendments, and employment documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run smooth onboarding, employee-change, and offboarding processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintaining accurate HRIS and employee data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinating our EOR platform and international employee administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preparing payroll inputs and administering employee benefits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting immigration, sponsorship and right-to-work administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as the first point of contact for routine employee People queries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinating performance, progression and compensation-cycle administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintaining People policies, templates and internal documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Producing recurring People data and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identifying opportunities to simplify and automate People processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting engagement and employee-experience initiatives.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>After 3 months, success will look like:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Operational</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">100% accurate contracts/employee documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboarding ready before Day 1.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payroll inputs completed accurately/on time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">HRIS data maintained accurately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Routine employee queries resolved in a timely manner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">EOR/immigration deadlines proactively tracked.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Leverage for the Head of People</u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Materially reduce the amount of routine People Ops execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recurring People reporting produced without manual assembling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People processes documented and repeatable.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>This role is a perfect match for you if you:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience running People/HR operations in a fast-moving organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are highly organised and genuinely strong at getting the details right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly and know when something needs escalating.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can independently manage recurring processes and deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable working across HRIS, payroll, benefits and employee documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a good baseline knowledge of UK employment practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable supporting employees across multiple countries/EOR arrangements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Look for the simplest effective solution rather than adding process for its own sake.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle confidential information with excellent judgement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable working in an environment where priorities change quickly.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus if you have knowledge or love of:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building automations that enable teams beyond your function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connecting with people to understand their motivations and how we can build the best culture where work = professional fulfilment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being curious and an active learner for your craft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tea and smoothie drinking 🫖</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>🇬🇧 What you can expect upon joining our team</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Salary reviews and share options becoming an integral part of our growth and share in the company's success</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💝 Goodstack’s Workplace Giving</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⚕️ Vitality Plus - Private health insurance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌞 £250 Brighten your day annual budget</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤓 £1000 Learning &amp; development annual budget</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 Goodstack library</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌯 Tasty Tuesday! Office lunch is on the company</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏃🏿‍♀️ Slow run club Wednesday</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⭐️ Paid days off to volunteer for non-profit causes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎤 Paid days to attend conferences</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥳 Paid day off on your birthday!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 25 days annual leave, plus paid public holidays</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💙 Paid sick leave</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧘🏽 Paid wellness leave</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🪁 Parental leave</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧸 Workplace nursery scheme</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧓🏽 Pension (with tax-efficient salary sacrifice option)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚴🏾 UK cycle-to-work scheme</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌳 Ecologi carbon offsetting</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⚖️ Flexible working hours</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🖥️ WFH budget upon joining</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏡 You're always welcome to pop in more often if you enjoy the buzz of being in the office. It's a warm, friendly space right in the heart of London</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🙌 … and so much more</p><h1><br /><strong>About us</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2017, Goodstack has been at the forefront of creating a future where good will be built into everything we do. From daily commutes to weekend activities or grocery shopping, we envision a world where creating positive change is seamlessly integrated into our everyday lives. In this future, the depth and breadth of impact we can make through everyday actions will expand dramatically – benefiting both businesses and the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Businesses are expected to deliver on both profit and purpose and those that don’t are falling behind. We’re here to make it easy for any company, anywhere in the world, to integrate good into what they do. Doing this empowers everyone – companies, employees, consumers, and communities – to contribute to positive change and take meaningful action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Let's do this! 💜</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>OUR PLEDGE TO DIVERSITY, EQUITY &amp; INCLUSION</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We take pride in our diverse and growing team representing 20+ nationalities across 5 continents 🌍! Our continued expansion provides us with opportunities to embrace and celebrate different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences, essential to our success. We actively seek and welcome applicants from all walks of life, regardless of race, religion, colour, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A team that represents the world that we are trying to support is a wiser, more knowledgeable and stronger one. We’re excited for you to bring your experience, yourself and your special </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://goodstack.io/blog"><strong>lemon twist</strong></a><strong> to Goodstack to propel us forward in striving to create a better world for us all.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://goodstack.io/careers"><strong>Careers Page</strong></a> for more details!</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/goodstack/people-operations-generalist-london-161454","tags":["People & culture"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"🇬🇧 London","created_at":1793428828},{"slug":"3d-computer-vision-research-engineer-geospatial-visual-localization-london-21403","company_name":"Niantic Spatial","title":"3D Computer Vision Research Engineer, Geospatial Visual Localization","description":"<h2><strong>About Niantic Spatial</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI has learned from almost everything online, but it still struggles with the physical world, where 99.5% of economic activity happens. It doesn’t know where things are, how spaces fit together, or what changes over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That’s one of the biggest unsolved problems in AI, and it’s the one we’re solving at Niantic Spatial. We build spatial AI models and services so people and machines can reason, learn and act safely in the physical world. We turn camera imagery, video, sensor data and archives into accurate, AI-readable representations of real places that robots can train in and machines can use to know exactly where they are.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In physical AI, mistakes have real consequences. That’s why we build AI grounded in measured reality, not guesswork, so the people and machines relying on it can trust it to get things right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team built some of the world’s most widely used maps. Now we’re building something bigger: a living, measured record of the real world that machines can query, learn from and use to understand how places change over time. If you want to help AI understand the world we actually live in, come build with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Research Engineer to help develop our Geospatial Visual Localization technologies, which allows people and robots to accurately localize themselves anywhere on the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an end-to-end applied research role. You will develop new approaches to open problems alongside our researchers in 3D vision and machine learning, and publish your work at leading conferences. You will help build and train large models on large-scale multi-modal datasets, including our proprietary collection of 30 billion posed images and ship them into production, to be used by people and robots from all over the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team works with heterogeneous captures from phones and other handheld devices, 360 cameras, vehicles, and drones, as well as aerial and satellite imagery, LiDAR, and external geographic data. Your focus will be to improve accuracy and robustness across urban and rural locations, cameras, seasons, weather, and capture quality. The system must remain reliable with noisy GPS, in GPS-denied environments, and with outdated reference maps. Each pose estimate comes with an uncertainty that our customers rely on, and keeping it well calibrated across these conditions is part of the work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, implement, and evaluate novel visual localization algorithms, combining 3D vision and deep learning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train large models on multi-modal data at scale, and build the benchmarks that measure their accuracy and robustness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop robust solutions for difficult real-world conditions: noisy or denied GPS, changing appearance, varying capture quality, large geographic extents, and imperfect reference maps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work side-by-side with leading researchers in visual localization, 3D computer vision, and mapping, as well as engineering and product teams, to identify the highest-impact problems and turn research into end-to-end solutions that operate at production scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate results clearly through technical writing, design reviews, internal presentations, and publications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong grounding in 3D computer vision, deep learning, robotics, photogrammetry, or a closely related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience with multi-view geometry and related problems, such as camera pose estimation, monocular depth estimation, SfM, SLAM, georeferencing, point-cloud registration, or sensor fusion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of transformer models for 3D vision, such as vision foundation models, feed-forward 3D reconstruction, or multi-view and multi-modal attention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of geospatial data and coordinate reference systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to formulate ambiguous real-world problems, choose appropriate mathematical or learning-based tools, and evaluate solutions rigorously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python skills and experience training deep learning models at scale, with libraries such as PyTorch, NumPy, and SciPy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software engineering skills, with the ability to turn research prototypes into reliable, scalable, and maintainable systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking an algorithm from research idea and experimental prototype through evaluation, benchmarking, and deployment on real-world data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and verbal communication and the ability to collaborate across research and engineering disciplines.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A PhD in computer vision, robotics, machine learning, photogrammetry, geodesy, remote sensing, or a related field, or equivalent research or industry experience. A PhD is not required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong publication record or substantial active involvement in the research community, especially at venues such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, ICLR, SIGGRAPH, SIGGRAPH Asia, 3DV, ICRA, RSS, or related conferences and journals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with aerial or satellite imagery, GNSS/GPS, IMUs, LiDAR data, geodesy, mapping systems, or large-scale spatial data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of technical leadership, mentorship, or successful cross-functional delivery.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Base salary: Competitive market rate. Compensation also includes an annual bonus, equity, and a comprehensive benefits package.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Location &amp; Work Model</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our London office, with three days per week in office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Inclusive Application</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know the strongest candidates don't always tick every box. If you're excited about this role and believe you could do it well, we encourage you to apply even if your experience doesn't match every qualification listed - you may be exactly who we're looking for.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Niantic Spatial is an equal opportunity employer. Individuals seeking employment at Niantic Spatial are considered without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion, creed, age, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding or related medical conditions), marital status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, military or veteran status, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, or any other protected category under applicable laws. Niantic Spatial will also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories in accordance with applicable laws. Please contact your recruiter if you want to request an accommodation for the job application or interview process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Candidate Privacy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">I understand that by submitting my job application, the information I provide as part of that application will be used in accordance with Niantic Spatial's Privacy Notice for Job Applicants and Candidates <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.nianticspatial.com/applicant-privacy-notice">https://www.nianticspatial.com/applicant-privacy-notice</a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/niantic-spatial/3d-computer-vision-research-engineer-geospatial-visual-localization-london-21403","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793428828},{"slug":"infrastructure-software-engineering-platform-build-london-jj-mack-265667","company_name":"Fractile","title":"Infrastructure Software Engineering – Platform & Build","description":"<h1><strong>About Fractile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile was founded in 2022 on the bet that, eventually, the world’s most capable AI systems would be limited in their impact by the time taken to produce useful outputs. We bet everything on the logical conclusion: that the only way to truly unlock this latent value, to make speed viable at scale, was to radically re-invent the hardware that we run our frontier AI models on. Ever since, we have been building chips and systems that tackle this problem: how to efficiently generate output at thousands of tokens per second, while handling the complexity and capacity challenges of operating large models at very long contexts.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The workloads that push to the limits of the current frontier are already transformational; it is the technical and economic limits on inference speed that are constraining progress. The defining work of the 21st century will be marked by the engine of inference delivering immense and diffuse chains of intellectual inquiry, in drug discovery, in software engineering, in materials discovery, in any field where progress is driven by deep reasoning and intelligence to resolve complex problems. <br /><br /></p><h3>The Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Infrastructure Platform Engineer you will be a core part of our technical team working alongside the hardware, software and research teams to solve cutting-edge problems in AI hardware, ranging from verification to simulation, alongside the best of the best (DeepMind, Apple, Meta…).</p><h3>About the Software organisation at Fractile</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Infrastructure sits within the Software organisation at Fractile, which is responsible for developing a full software stack for our groundbreaking AI inference systems. That's everything from ML compilers, device drivers and systems firmware, application level runtime and ecosystem integrations, ML and compute libraries, great developer tooling and a full portfolio of simulators, through to datacenter scale workload deployment solutions. At Fractile, we know that a fantastic software stack is a critical and central part of any AI inference solution and it sits at the heart of everything we're doing.</p><h3>About the team and role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Infrastructure team is responsible for the core platform and systems at Fractile. We build, scale, and optimize the mission-critical systems that power our entire engineering org, including our multi-language Bazel monorepo and CI pipelines. From hardware design and verification to kernel development and ML compilers, we enable all Fractile engineers to ship fast and reliably.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team brings both deep build system expertise and an SRE mindset: reliability, build performance, debugging CI failures systematically, and giving the engineering organisation clear visibility into how our infrastructure is performing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Infrastructure Platform Engineer, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the CI infrastructure end-to-end: create, maintain and debug reproducible multi-language CI pipelines, and optimize CI performance across large compute clusters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain infrastructure observability, alerting, runbooks, and incident response workflows for Fractile's infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our infrastructure as code, automating provisioning of hybrid cloud and on-prem resources from a single source of truth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale and maintain Fractile's Bazel monorepo as we continue growing across Python, C++, Rust, SystemVerilog, and ML workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the infrastructure and platform experience for every engineer at Fractile.</p></li></ul><h3>About you</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring deep infrastructure and build systems expertise alongside an SRE mindset. You are systematic in how you approach fault isolation and root cause analysis, and you apply metrics-driven thinking to build reliability and developer productivity. You thrive on variety (ML, compilers, kernel drivers, simulators, hardware verification) and you understand that your work becomes the foundation every engineer at Fractile builds on. You take that responsibility seriously.</p><h3>Key Requirements</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in software, platform, or infrastructure engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years hands-on experience working with CI/CD for large-scale products, including monitoring, debugging performance and resolving pipeline failures at scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years working with build systems, preferably modern cross-language build systems with an emphasis on correctness, high performance and extensibility, such as Bazel, Buck, Pants, Please, etc.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with infrastructure as code (Terraform / OpenTofu, or Pulumi)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with monitoring and observability tooling (Prometheus, Grafana, or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge and practice of DevOps / SRE principles: SLOs, alerting design, incident management, and on-call practice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong proficiency in at least one systems or scripting language used for tooling (Python preferred; Go or Rust also relevant), with a track record of shipping well-tested, maintainable developer tooling that other engineers rely on: CLIs, CI integrations, build and release automation</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary: A competitive salary reflective of your experience and the specialist nature of the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity &amp; Ownership: meaningful equity so everyone shares in the value creation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benefits: Private Medical, Dental and Vision, Contributory Pension, 25 Days holiday plus bank holidays and Life/Critical Illness Insurance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diverse &amp; fun office: we believe the hardest problems get solved by the broadest range of minds. We are committed to Equal Employment Opportunity through attracting and retaining a diverse team and building an inclusive environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile is seeking to increase the clock speed of global progress, one chip at a time. We’ve recently raised $220M from investors including Founders Fund and Accel and our most important work lies ahead. Join us!</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Export controls</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our work involves technologies subject to UK, US and other international export control regulations. Certain roles may require additional eligibility checks to ensure compliance with applicable law. We'll be transparent about this throughout the hiring process.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fractile/infrastructure-software-engineering-platform-build-london-jj-mack-265667","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London - JJ Mack","created_at":1793428827},{"slug":"developer-experience-devex-london-jj-mack-78476","company_name":"Fractile","title":"Developer Experience / DevEx","description":"<h1><strong>About Fractile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile was founded in 2022 on the bet that, eventually, the world’s most capable AI systems would be limited in their impact by the time taken to produce useful outputs. We bet everything on the logical conclusion: that the only way to truly unlock this latent value, to make speed viable at scale, was to radically re-invent the hardware that we run our frontier AI models on. Ever since, we have been building chips and systems that tackle this problem: how to efficiently generate output at thousands of tokens per second, while handling the complexity and capacity challenges of operating large models at very long contexts.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The workloads that push to the limits of the current frontier are already transformational; it is the technical and economic limits on inference speed that are constraining progress. The defining work of the 21st century will be marked by the engine of inference delivering immense and diffuse chains of intellectual inquiry, in drug discovery, in software engineering, in materials discovery, in any field where progress is driven by deep reasoning and intelligence to resolve complex problems. <br /><br /></p><h3>About the Software organisation at Fractile</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Developer Experience sits within the Software organisation at Fractile, which is responsible for developing a full software stack for our groundbreaking AI inference systems. That's everything from ML compilers, device drivers and systems firmware, application level runtime and ecosystem integrations, ML and compute libraries, great developer tooling and a full portfolio of simulators, through to datacenter scale workload deployment solutions. At Fractile, we know that a fantastic software stack is a critical and central part of any AI inference solution and it sits at the heart of everything we're doing.</p><h3>About the team and role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Developer Experience team at Fractile helps shape how our customers interact with the Fractile inference accelerator. We work across the company to identify, create, and present information on how the system is being used, as well as providing the tooling to help optimise our customers' usage of the system, while keeping a shallow learning curve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a member of the Developer Experience team you will need to understand the current state of development for inference hardware. You will need to be able to identify what will work well for engineers wanting to identify potential opportunities for performance improvements, while knowing what tooling will fit into an existing LLM engineer's workflow with the minimal amount of disruption and effort.</p><h3>About you</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone who is self-driven and capable of identifying tooling opportunities, designing those tools, and delivering them in a way which will fit in with an LLM engineer's existing toolset. You will have worked in this area before, possibly as an FDE or at a company that provides inference services using their own models, and have the ability to develop new tools that are designed to be functional and easy to learn and use.</p><h3>Key Requirements</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with inference frameworks such as JAX and/or PyTorch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of software development in Python, Rust, C/C++, or a similar language</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience monitoring and optimising code written in CUDA, ROCm, OpenCL, or similar</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience 