 missions :</strong> Vous êtes prêt(e) à vous investir pleinement dans les tâches qui vous sont confiées, en respectant les procédures et en cherchant toujours à améliorer la qualité du service.</p></li><li><p><strong>Volonté d'apprendre et d'évoluer :</strong> Vous aimez relever des défis et êtes ouvert(e) à l'apprentissage continu.</p></li><li><p><strong>Attitude professionnelle :</strong> Votre sérieux et votre souci du travail bien fait sont des atouts majeurs.</p></li><li><p>Assiudité et ponctualité : sont indispensables pour occuper ce poste</p></li></ul><h2>Avantages</h2><ul><li><p>Mutuelle</p></li><li><p>Transport en commun remboursé à 50%</p></li><li><p>Dimanche et jours fériés majorés à 25%</p></li><li><p>Primes sur objectif incluant la qualité et l'assiduité pouvant aller jusqu'à 250€ brut/mois</p></li><li><p>Evolution par échelon : 100€ d'augmentation sur le salaire si vous validez l'échelon et ce dès les 18 mois de présence.</p></li></ul><p><strong>N'attendez plus pour faire de cette annonce votre prochain défi professionnel. Rejoignez-nous et contribuez à un service de qualité au sein d'une équipe dynamique et respectueuse. Votre expérience, votre savoir-faire et aussi votre savoir être (très important) seront des atouts précieux pour notre entreprise !</strong></p><p>Tu as envie d’en savoir encore plus clique sur ce lien :</p><p>https://www.linkedin.com/company/taxi-lyonnais1/mycompany/?viewAsMember=true</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/gtl-taxi-lyonnnais/tele-conseillerere-tele-operateur-trice-centraliste-bron-97054","tags":["Customer Service"],"job_types":["Cdi - contrat à durée indéterminée","professionnel / expérimenté"],"location":"Bron","created_at":1793435445},{"slug":"responsable-qualite-cdd-6-mois-renouvelable-h-f-boulogne-billancourt-461030","company_name":"Sogeclair","title":"Responsable qualité CDD 6 mois- renouvelable (H/F)","description":"<p>Les missions du Responsable Qualité sont&nbsp;: </p><ul><li>Organiser et maintenir le système de management de la qualité et superviser sa déclinaison à tous les niveaux de l'entreprise</li><li>Définir et mettre en œuvre le plan de communication sur la politique et le programme qualité</li><li>Assurer la bonne compréhension et l'application des procédures et démarches qualité à travers les formations et l'assistance méthodologique</li><li>Identifier et analyser les problèmes qualité et proposer des actions correctives</li><li>Promouvoir les plans d'amélioration de la performance, la culture d'amélioration continue et les meilleures pratiques auprès des collaborateurs</li><li>Définir et suivre les outils de gestion de la qualité (système documentaire, indicateurs…)</li><li>Assurer la veille normative et réglementaire</li><li>Préparer les démarches de certification ou d’accréditation spécifiques (ISO 9001)</li><li>Participer à l'implémentation du système de management de la qualité fournisseur</li><li>Organiser et superviser des audits qualité internes et externes<br><br><strong>**Remplacement de congé de maternité, CDD de 6 mois renouvelable, entrée en fonction souhaitée : 1er décembre**</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>Compétences techniques </strong></p><ul><li>Connaitre les méthodes et les outils propres à la Qualité.</li><li>Connaître les normes, standards et procédures Qualité</li><li>Mettre en place et piloter le dispositif de contrôle du respect des procédures et des méthodes d’assurance qualité (plan d'audit, formation, …)</li><li>Piloter des projets de certification</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Aptitudes professionnelles </strong></p><ul><li>Autonomie</li><li>Organisation et rigueur</li><li>Capacité d’adaptation à un environnement multi-entités et multi métiers.</li><li>Être force de proposition</li><li>Capacité de communication et d’animation</li><li>Maitrise de l’anglais niveau professionnel</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><em>Le Groupe SOGECLAIR est convaincu que la diversité et l’inclusion sont des éléments essentiels de sa performance et s’engage à recruter sans discrimination.</em></p><p>Dans un souci de lisibilité, le masculin est utilisé dans cette annonce, mais nous encourageons les candidatures de toutes les personnes, sans distinction de genre, d’origine, de handicap ou de toute autre caractéristique.</p><p></p><p><strong>Notre processus recrutement :</strong></p><p>📞 Un rapide entretien téléphonique de pré-qualification</p><p>🤝 Un entretien technique et RH</p><p>💻 Optionnel : un second entretien ou test de personnalité</p><p>🏁 Welcome aboard !</p><h3>Benefits</h3><p>Work @Sogeclair ✨ :</p><ul><li>Un environnement de travail international et multiculturel 🌎</li><li>Des perspectives de mobilité interne</li><li>Un apprentissage permanent : Sogeclair Academy 🎓</li><li>Un package de rémunération : RTT, mutuelle, pack mobilité durable, politique cooptation, TR etc.</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/sogeclair/responsable-qualite-cdd-6-mois-renouvelable-h-f-boulogne-billancourt-461030","tags":["Quality Assurance","Automotive","Sogeclair Simulation"],"job_types":["Temporary","mid-senior"],"location":"Boulogne-Billancourt, France","created_at":1793434815},{"slug":"quantum-software-engineer-massy-300160","company_name":"Quandela","title":"Quantum Software Engineer","description":"<p>Quandela is a global leader in quantum computing, designing, building, and delivering cutting-edge quantum solutions for research and industry. Its offerings include a very energy-efficient quantum computers for data centers, full-stack quantum computing solutions accessible via the cloud, and algorithm access services for academic and industrial customers. Following a pragmatic, step-by-step roadmap, Quandela has been deploying industrial-grade systems since 2023 while developing future generations of fault-tolerant quantum computers capable of scaling through the integration of thousands of photonic components. Quandela is committed to making quantum computing accessible to all in order to address the most complex industrial and societal challenges. Learn more at: <a href="http://www.quandela.com/" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">Quandela | Leading Photonic Quantum Computing Solutions</a> </p><p></p><h3><strong>Description of the Project </strong></h3><p>We are looking for a <strong>Quantum Software Engineer</strong> to develop the future software stack for controlling utility-scale quantum computers. At the interface of the theory and engineering teams, this ambitious project aims to develop internal tools to streamline the operation of logical quantum circuits on Quandela’s spin-photonic quantum computers.</p><p>This position requires a strong understanding of quantum computing protocols on real hardware, strong software engineering skills and proficiency with AI tools.</p><p></p><h3><strong>Your Key Responsibilities: </strong></h3><ul><li>Develop a new compilation stack translating high-level quantum circuits into hardware-aware pulse schedules optimized for our photonic quantum computers.</li><li>Drive long-term architectural strategy, technical roadmap, and cross-organizational alignment.</li><li>Contribute to the development of a digital twin, receiving hardware instructions to simulate the behavior of our future QPUs.</li><li>Stay up to date with the latest developments in quantum software.</li></ul><h3>How You’ll Grow: </h3><ul><li>3 months. By the end of the first quarter, you are expected to have a grasp over Quandela’s roadmap and specific approach to quantum computing. You understand how user operations are currently compiled to machine instructions and how that is expected to evolve</li><li>6 months. By the end of the first semester, you have a firm understanding of Quandela’s technology and are already a key contributor to the compiler codebase for the near future</li><li>12 months. You have a long-term vision over the quantum software’s activities, and are the owner of one or more work packages for strategic projects.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><h3><em>What we're looking for:&nbsp;</em></h3><ul><li>Master’s, or PhD in Quantum related field.</li><li>2/4+ years of relevant experience in quantum software, quantum hardware automation, or related topics.</li></ul><p><strong>Must-have:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>A good understanding of photonic-based quantum computing.</li><li>Strong proficiency in python.</li><li>Experience working at the interface of software, experimental hardware, and theory teams in the industry or academia.</li><li>Collaborative mindset, able to serve as a bridge between various teams.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Important, but you can grow here:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Proficiency in at least one system language (C++ or Rust)</li><li>Exposure to the quantum computing frontends and related ecosystem (e.g. cirq, qiskit, openqasm, cuda-q).</li><li>Hands-on experience with quantum photonic systems.</li><li>Familiarity with compilation mechanisms such as LLVM or compilation to microcode.</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><h3></h3><ul><li>Competitive salary, flexible based on your experience </li><li>Profit-sharing &amp; company savings plan</li><li>100% health coverage (Alan)</li><li>50% transport reimbursement or sustainable mobility bonus</li><li>Meal vouchers (Swile), Gymlib fitness support</li><li>Childcare assistance &amp; referral bonuses (€1,000–€2,000)</li></ul><p></p><h3>What we offer: </h3><ul><li>A meaningful role with real ownership, from day one</li><li>A team eager to collaborate and grow with you</li><li>A hybrid work model (3-4 days/week onsite in Massy, 1 day in Paris or 1 to 2 days remotely)</li><li>Daily exposure to the entire quantum stack — from high-level APIs to low-level firmware, and everything in between.<br> </li></ul><h3><strong>Process </strong></h3><ul><li>Talent Acquisition Interview (30' - 45')</li><li>Hiring Managers Interview (45')</li><li>Use Case (a live use case or one to be prepared at home and presented afterward)</li><li>Meeting with the teams </li><li>2 to 3 reference check</li><li>Offer </li></ul><p><em>(This process is provided for guidance only and may evolve depending on the roles)</em></p><p></p><p>At Quandela, we believe that the strength of our team is the plurality of experiences, perspectives, and journeys. We are committed to building a respectful, inclusive, and welcoming work environment. All applications are welcome.&nbsp;</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/quandela/quantum-software-engineer-massy-300160","tags":["Information Technology","Computer Hardware","IT & Software"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Massy, France","created_at":1793434814},{"slug":"photonic-integrated-circuit-designer-intern-h1-2027-massy-137651","company_name":"Quandela","title":"Photonic Integrated Circuit Designer Intern (H1/2027)","description":"<h3><strong>About Quandela </strong></h3><p>Quandela stands as a global leader in quantum computing, driven by groundbreaking technology and a strategic vision for scaling quantum solutions. The company’s unique ability to offer both hardware and software solutions, along with its commitment to build energy efficient datacenters and scalability, positions it to play a key role in the next wave of innovation, and in many strategic and sovereign industrial sectors.</p><p>Join Us at the Forefront of Quantum Computing Innovation 🚀</p><p></p><h3><strong>Description of the Team</strong></h3><p>The internship will be conducted in the Photonic Integrated Circuits (PICs) department ofQuandela. The PICs team works on the production and development of the optical processors of Quandela quantum computers, having in mind performance and scalability.</p><p>In detail, the team members carry out electromagnetic and thermal simulations to estimate the performance of the integrated components, prepare PICs layouts to be fabricated in collaboration with external foundries, and take care of both the characterization and the packaging of the fabricated devices.</p><p></p><h3><strong>Your Key Responsibilities</strong></h3><p>Depending on your experience and the duration of the internship, your work may involve deepening the understanding of existing building blocks, exploring new functionalities or tools, or developing advanced modeling approaches for testing. In particular, the goal of this internship will be to either bridge the gap between fabrication and design, or to evaluate new architecture for quantum processing unit (QPU).</p><p>In this role you will be using standard electromagnetic simulations and/or circuit modelling by means of commercial software like Lumerical FDTD, FDE, EME or free-tools (gdsfactory, tidy3d, meow, sax..).</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Enrollment for the whole duration of the internship in a MSc in Physics, Telecom/Electronics Engineering, Photonics, Quantum Technologies or related fields. <strong>This position is only valid with an Internship Agreement.</strong></li><li>Minimal duration is 5 months. Shorter internship will not be accepted.</li><li>Ideal starting date late Summer 2026.</li><li>General knowledge of integrated photonics modelling and layout</li><li>Python, Git, Lumerical, simulation tools (FDTD, mode solver, EME..)</li><li>Great skills in data analysis</li><li>Capability of working in a team</li><li>Strong communication skills in English and French</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Swile Card (meal vouchers) 🍴🛒</li></ul><ul><li>50% participation in transportation costs&nbsp;🚆</li></ul><ul><li>Possibility of remote work&nbsp;💻</li><li>Internship Allowance between €1,200 and €1,400 per month 💰</li></ul><ul><li>1,5 days off per month, cumulative 🧳</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What we also offer</strong></p><p>A challenging and innovative work environment at the heart of quantum computing.&nbsp;</p><p>A diverse and collaborative company culture.&nbsp;</p><p>Opportunities for professional growth and skill development.&nbsp;</p><p>At Quandela, we believe that the strength of our team is the plurality of experiences, perspectives, and journeys. We are committed to building a respectful, inclusive, and welcoming work environment. All applications are welcome.&nbsp;</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/quandela/photonic-integrated-circuit-designer-intern-h1-2027-massy-137651","tags":["Computer Hardware","Products"],"job_types":["Full time","internship"],"location":"Massy, France","created_at":1793434814},{"slug":"lead-ai-engineer-paris-425434","company_name":"mirakllabs","title":"Lead AI engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mirakl:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2012, Mirakl has been at the forefront of marketplace innovation, empowering every business to compete in the platform economy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, Mirakl’s operating system combines an enterprise marketplace solution (Mirakl Platform) that enables retailers and B2B organizations to launch, scale, and operate marketplaces and dropship, AI-powered multichannel selling (Mirakl Connect), retail media (Mirakl Ads) and an agentic commerce infrastructure (Mirakl Nexus).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With dual headquarters in Boston and Paris, Mirakl helps a global ecosystem of 450+ marketplaces (B2C and B2B) and a network of over 100k third-party marketplace sellers. Brands like Macy’s, Decathlon, Carrefour, Asos, and Airbus Helicopters use Mirakl to grow their businesses in new and remarkable ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mirakl.com&quot;&gt;www.mirakl.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
