st, measure its results, and apply what you learn to future campaigns.</p><p>Work location: Our company operates on a remote-first model. This role can be performed remotely from anywhere in Europe. Fluent English and German are a must. Occasional travel to our office in Neuchâtel, Switzerland, or to team events may be required.</p><h3><u>Core Responsibilities</u></h3><ul><li>Identify, assess, and recruit creators across relevant platforms and markets.</li><li>Develop campaign concepts that balance Hilo’s brand goals with measurable commercial outcomes.</li><li>Forecast likely reach, engagement, traffic, and acquisition outcomes to guide creator selection and budgets.</li><li>Negotiate fees, deliverables, timelines, and content usage rights, including rights to use creator content in paid campaigns.</li><li>Manage partnerships end to end, from briefing and content review through publication and reporting.</li><li>Build and nurture long-term relationships with creators and brand ambassadors to drive sustained awareness, trust, and advocacy.</li><li>Collaborate with paid media teams to amplify high-performing creator content across paid social and other relevant channels.</li><li>Set clear goals, track brand and performance metrics, and compare results with initial estimates.</li><li>Use campaign data and audience insights to improve creator selection, content formats, and investment decisions.</li><li>Work across marketing and product to align campaigns with Hilo’s priorities and approved health claims.</li><li>Build repeatable processes that support growth across the US, UK, Germany, and other markets.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><u><strong>Background &amp; Experience</strong></u></p><ul><li>At least 2 years of hands-on influencer or creator marketing experience, including managing partnerships from start to finish.</li><li>A data-driven mindset: you can estimate campaign outcomes, assess performance, and turn findings into better decisions.</li>