u if you want to lead a strong engineering team through its next phase of growth and own the result.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You report to the Director of Product Engineering and work closely with the other product team leads, product management, and the go-to-market organization (project managers, customer success, and sales). The team is organized in subteams, each with its own lead, and you are the person who keeps them aligned.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead and grow the team</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run regular 1:1s, ensure growth of the engineers in your team, review progress, and make promotion and ranking decisions together with engineering leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach and develop subteam leads, and set up the subteam structure as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep a distributed team connected and productive: clear working agreements, transparent planning, and a culture where people raise problems early.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hire</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own hiring for the team end to end: define the profiles, screen candidates, run interviews, review coding challenges, and close offers together with Talent Acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep a high bar while hiring at pace (our current target is around two new engineers per month), and make sure every new joiner has an onboarding plan and a buddy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the roadmap and priorities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the quarterly roadmap and run monthly planning with product owners and product management, prioritizing by customer impact, revenue, and strategic value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance enterprise go-lives, automation improvements, platform migration, developer experience, operations, and new products, and say no when something does not move the product forward.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate early and clearly when priorities conflict, and communicate decisions to the go-to-market organization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver for strategic enterprise customers</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take responsibility for the engineering side of large enterprise go-lives: requirements engineering, solution design, test and fix cycles, and go-live readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with project managers and, where needed, with customer stakeholders and their IT teams, and give clear, regular engineering updates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close gaps in the product rather than per customer, so the next enterprise customer arrives on a platform that already handles their case.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have led an engineering team of 8+ people for at least two years, ideally in B2B SaaS, and you have grown a team through hiring rather than only inheriting one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong backend engineering background and can still read, review, and discuss production code and system design with senior engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have hired many engineers yourself, you know what a high bar looks like, and you can run a structured interview process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have delivered complex software for enterprise customers, including demanding go-lives, and you are comfortable in a room with customer stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prioritize ruthlessly, communicate trade-offs clearly, and can hold a position with engineers, sales, and executives while keeping the relationship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You develop people: you give direct feedback, set measurable goals, and help engineers grow into leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take ownership, surface problems early, ask for help when you are stuck, and hold your team to the same standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in English. German is a strong plus, since many of our customers and colleagues are in the DACH region.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll get</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A real mandate.</strong> You own the invoice team end to end: people, hiring, roadmap, and delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact you can measure.</strong> Automation rates and go-lives on our largest accounts are directly visible to customers and to the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A strong team.</strong> Engineers from serious academic and industry backgrounds who care about doing the work well, with subteam leads already in place.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A smooth handover.</strong> The current team lead moves into a new role in engineering leadership and stays available to support your start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Room to grow.</strong> As a fast-growing, global AI company, BLP keeps creating new leadership opportunities.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/blp-digital-ag/team-lead-invoices-zurich-420009","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1793418028},{"slug":"ai-product-concept-designer-interior-stylist-home-decor-part-full-time-switzerland-324141","company_name":"Jobgether","title":"AI Product Concept Designer & Interior Stylist – Home Décor (Part-/Full-time)","description":"<div>
