rience in landing new clients, retaining existing customers, and driving account expansion for early-stage enterprise products in a dynamic, entrepreneurial setting.<br /><br /><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute sales strategies to target enterprise customers, focusing on building and maintaining a robust pipeline that drives long-term growth.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the entire sales cycle, from prospecting and initial outreach to contract negotiations and closing deals, while consistently meeting or exceeding revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with internal teams, including product, marketing, and customer success, to ensure a seamless sales experience and alignment on customer needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify customer pain points and align our solutions to address these, delivering customized product demos and presentations tailored to their specific business needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and nurture relationships with C-level executives and key decision-makers within target accounts, establishing yourself as a trusted advisor and ensuring customer satisfaction and retention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead account planning efforts by researching potential customers, understanding industry trends, and developing strategies to win new business and grow existing accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and manage sales activities and results, accurately forecasting opportunities and keeping detailed records of interactions and progress in CRM systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay updated on industry trends, competitor offerings, and market changes to position our product effectively and maintain a competitive edge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to business growth initiatives, providing feedback to product and marketing teams to influence product development and go-to-market strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Kong with professionalism, acting as a brand ambassador at industry events, conferences, and customer meetings.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in enterprise sales (&gt;1k employees), with a proven track record of closing complex deals in a SaaS, cloud, or enterprise software environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success in selling to large enterprises, particularly to senior-level executives and across multiple departments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong consultative selling skills, with the ability to understand customer needs and present compelling solutions that drive business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and negotiation skills, capable of managing high-stakes conversations and building lasting relationships with stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A results-driven mindset, with a passion for meeting and exceeding sales goals and revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with CRM platforms (e.g., Salesforce) and leveraging data to forecast accurately and track sales metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of open-source software, APIs, or infrastructure software is highly advantageous.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment, taking ownership of your sales territory and adapting to changing market dynamics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical and strategic thinking, with a knack for identifying business growth opportunities and devising plans to capitalize on them.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-JM3</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Kong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kong Inc., the AI Connectivity Company, is building the connectivity layer of AI. Trusted by the Fortune 500® and AI-native startups alike, Kong’s unified API and AI platform enables organizations to secure, manage, accelerate, govern, and monetize the flow of intelligence across APIs and AI traffic — on any model, any cloud. For more information, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.konghq.com">www.konghq.com</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/kong/enterprise-account-executive-switzerland-bern-381717","tags":["All Cost Center"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Switzerland","created_at":1793364015},{"slug":"certification-engineer-nyon-344048","company_name":"Eh Group","title":"Certification Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About EH Energy Engineering</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">EH Energy is developing cutting-edge fuel cell technology for heavy-duty mobility and large-scale stationary power applications. Our uniquely redesigned product delivers a significantly more compact fuel cell system with high power density and lower production costs. In response to the challenges of climate change and the global shift toward decentralized energy, EH Energy provides high-performance, cost-effective fuel cell solutions to our clients and partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To support our rapid growth and bring our systems to global markets, we are seeking a Certification Engineer. In this critical role, you will take full ownership of our product compliance roadmap, bridging the gap between innovative engineering and strict global regulations. You will lead hazard and risk assessments, define certification strategies across international markets (EU, North America, marine), and interface directly with notified bodies and classification societies to ensure our fuel cell systems are safe, fully compliant, and market-ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role <strong>requires a full-time, on-site presence at our office in Nyon, Switzerland</strong>. We are <strong>unable to offer remote or hybrid arrangements</strong>, so candidates should be based locally or <strong>prepared to relocate</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Certification strategy and project management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify applicable directives, regulations, harmonised standards and class rules early in the development cycle and translate them into design requirements (EU, North America, marine)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Select and manage notified bodies, NRTLs, classification societies and test laboratories, own budgets, schedules and contracts for certification work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and witness type tests, factory acceptance tests (FAT) and site acceptance tests (SAT)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Safety engineering and risk analysis</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead risk assessments to ISO 12100 and hazard studies (HAZID, HAZOP to IEC 61882)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead design and process FMEA (IEC 60812) for stacks, balance of plant, containers and fuel processing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run explosion-protection assessments: hazardous area classification (IEC 60079-10-1), ventilation and gas detection concepts, and equipment selection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specify and verify safety functions to ISO 13849 (PL) and IEC 61508, including safety requirement specifications and validation reports</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance and technical documentation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compile and maintain technical construction files, CE Declarations of Conformity, type-approval dossiers and certification reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review user, installation, operation and maintenance manuals, safety instructions and labelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the standards register and assess the impact of new or revised standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage certification change control: assess design changes for impact on existing certificates</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration and continuous improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the internal authority on certification scope: ensure in-service conformity of series production with certified designs, and support procurement and supply chain on material and packaging compliance (e.g. RoHS, packaging regulations).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support design reviews and supplier qualification, including component certificates (ATEX, PED, electrical)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Standards and regulatory scope</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role covers, but is not limited to, the frameworks below. Working knowledge of most is expected; deep expertise in several is required</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">IEC 62282 series, CSA/ANSI FC 1:2021, ISO 16110-1 and Machinery Regulation (EU) 2023/1230</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Required qualifications</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s or bachelor’s degree in mechanical, electrical, chemical, process or safety engineering, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in product certification, compliance or safety engineering for complex electromechanical or process equipment (energy, gas, process, machinery or marine)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience with hydrogen or fuel cell systems and the IEC 62282 series, CSA/ANSI FC 1 or ISO 16110</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of taking products through CE marking and third-party certification with notified bodies or NRTLs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience leading FMEA, HAZOP and risk assessments, and documenting them to auditor standard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid knowledge of ATEX / IECEx, hazardous area classification and explosion-protection concepts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience specifying and validating safety functions to ISO 13849 and/or IEC 61508</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent technical writing: clear, structured, audit-ready technical files and manuals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English, written and spoken</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Preferred qualifications and personal profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marine type approval with a classification society (DNV, LR, BV, ABS) or IGF Code projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with fuel processing, reformers or fire equipment, and with pressure equipment under PED</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Certified functional safety qualification or ATEX/IECEx competence certification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with North American codes (NEC, NFPA) and UL/CSA certification</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigorous and structured, with a strong safety mindset and an eye for detail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pragmatic: finds compliant solutions that keep development moving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident communicator with engineers, auditors, authorities and customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-driven in a fast-growing, scale-up environment; comfortable owning topics end to end</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date: Immediately</strong></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/eh-group/certification-engineer-nyon-344048","tags":["Engineering Services"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Nyon","created_at":1793364015},{"slug":"recruiting-hr-operations-manager-nyon-220263","company_name":"Eh Group","title":"Recruiting & HR Operations Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a hands-on, resourceful Recruiting &amp; HR Operations Manager to help us attract, hire, and support exceptional talent as we grow. This role will primarily focus on full-cycle recruiting, partnering closely with hiring managers and leadership to understand business needs, build talent pipelines, and deliver an efficient, high-quality candidate experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">While recruiting will be the priority, this role will support onboarding, employee lifecycle administration, and day-to-day HR operations for our Swiss-based team when time allows. Reporting to the Fractional HR leader based in the US, you will help build scalable, consistent people practices while providing responsive support to employees and managers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an individual contributor role for someone who enjoys quick execution to make an impact, owning the details, building relationships, and balancing multiple 