{"data":[{"slug":"content-creator-video-social-mit-ceo-fokus-all-genders-b2b-saas-fur-kmu-berlin-7562","company_name":"mika","title":"Content Creator Video & Social mit CEO-Fokus (all genders) B2B SaaS für KMU","description":"<p>Buchhaltung ist für die meisten Gründerinnen und Gründer ein Blackbox-Posten: teuer, langsam, und am Ende weiß niemand genau, wofür er zahlt.<br>mika ändert das. Wir bauen KI-gestützte Buchhaltung, die Unternehmen selbst in die Hand nehmen können, ohne Steuerberater dazwischen. Belegerfassung, Klassifizierung, E-Rechnung, Validierung und Meldungen laufen automatisiert, statt im Monatsrhythmus über einen externen Schreibtisch zu wandern.<br>Wir sind 30 Personen, betreuen rund 900 Kunden und haben unsere Seed-Runde frisch abgeschlossen.<br><br><strong>Worum es geht</strong><br>Unsere CEO und Mitgründerin hat auf LinkedIn eine starke Personal Brand aufgebaut. Sie spricht auf Bühnen, co-hostet einen Podcast und ist eine der lauteren Stimmen zu Unternehmertum und KI. Jetzt soll das auch auf Instagram, TikTok und ggf. YouTube funktionieren, und zwar so, wie es auf diesen Kanälen funktioniert, nicht als Kopie von LinkedIn. Dafür suchen wir dich.<br><br><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></p><ul><li><p>Du produzierst Video- und Visual-Content für die Kanäle unserer CEO: Short-Form-Videos, Podcast-Schnipsel, Visuals</p></li><li><p>Du begleitest sie auf Veranstaltungen und machst dort Content: Talks, Backstage, Gespräche, Stimmung</p></li><li><p>Du baust ihre Kanäle auf Instagram, TikTok und ggf. YouTube aus, mit einer eigenen Logik für jeden Kanal</p></li><li><p>Du entscheidest mit, welche Inhalte über die CEO laufen und welche über mika</p></li><li><p>Du filmst, schneidest und schreibst selbst, von der Idee bis zum fertigen Post</p></li><li><p>Du beobachtest Trends und reagierst schnell darauf, nicht erst drei Wochen später</p></li><li><p>Du produzierst auf Deutsch und auf Englisch</p></li></ul><p><strong>Was du mitbringst</strong></p><ul><li><p>Du hast schon Kanäle aufgebaut, idealerweise für dich selbst oder für eine Gründerin oder einen Gründer, und kannst das mit Zahlen und Beispielen zeigen</p></li><li><p>Du weißt, warum ein Video auf TikTok anders funktioniert als auf Instagram oder YouTube, und baust Content entsprechend</p></li><li><p>Du filmst und schneidest sicher, mit dem Handy genauso wie mit der Kamera</p></li><li><p>Du schreibst gut, auf Deutsch und auf Englisch (min C1)</p></li><li><p>Du bist schnell, arbeitest selbstständig und brauchst keine Briefings für jeden Post</p></li><li><p>Du wohnst in Berlin oder ziehst her, denn ohne Präsenz vor Ort geht der Job nicht</p></li><li><p>Du reist gern und bist 1–4 Mal im Monat auf Events in Deutschland dabei</p></li></ul><p><strong>Was dich erwartet</strong></p><ul><li><p>Du arbeitest direkt mit der CEO und hast echten Einfluss darauf, wie sie und mika nach außen wirken</p></li><li><p>Du baust etwas auf: Du übernimmst keinen fertigen Redaktionsplan, du entwickelst die Kanäle selbst</p></li><li><p>Du bist auf Bühnen, Events und hinter den Kulissen eines schnell wachsenden KI-Startups dabei</p></li><li><p>Du hast viel Freiraum bei Formaten und Ideen, solange sie funktionieren</p></li></ul><p><strong>Bewerbung</strong><br>Schick uns statt eines langen Anschreibens 3–5 Links zu Kanälen oder Videos, die du aufgebaut oder produziert hast, und schreib in zwei Sätzen dazu, was deine Rolle dabei war.<br><br><em>Bei mika schätzen wir Vielfalt und arbeiten an einem Umfeld, in dem alle im Team ihr Bestes geben können. Bau mit uns die Zukunft der Finanzen für kleine Unternehmen.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mika/content-creator-video-social-mit-ceo-fokus-all-genders-b2b-saas-fur-kmu-berlin-7562","tags":["Social Media Manager"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793376070},{"slug":"software-qa-engineer-ii-kassel-hesse-363426","company_name":"Axon","title":"Software QA Engineer II","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Axon and be a Force for Good.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Axon’s RF sensors detect and locate drones so public safety and critical infrastructure teams can protect airspace. You will own the test strategy and independent verification approach for RF sensor capabilities — spanning regression, integration, and real-world validation — so those systems are trustworthy in the lab and in the field. You will work closely with RF Engineering at the intersection of software, hardware, and real-world RF, helping turn technical evidence into confident product decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based out of our Kassel, Germany office and follows a hybrid schedule. We rely on in-person collaboration and ask that team members work onsite Tuesdays through Fridays, with the flexibility to work remotely on Mondays, unless there is an approved workplace accommodation. We believe that connection fuels innovation, and our in-office culture is designed to foster meaningful teamwork, mentorship, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the test strategy and independent verification approach for RF sensor software from design through release, adding rigor through regression, integration, and real-world validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and own test strategies spanning feature, regression, integration / interface, system, and field validation. Combine automated coverage with targeted manual validation based on risk and technical feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop in-depth functional tests for individual components of the RF sensor software, and keep those tests maintainable as the product evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reproduce, isolate, and characterize issues on real sensor hardware and in test environments; capture clear reproduction steps, logs, and environment details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain hardware-backed automated regression tests and supporting test tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and improve development and test systems and test hardware so environments stay stable, observable, and ready for daily use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with RF Engineering and independently verify behavior in realistic environments and across system interfaces. Execute system, release, field, and acceptance testing with release stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document test results and defects clearly, and contribute to software design reviews and after-action reviews for the work you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge with the wider team, give actionable feedback, and support newer engineers and interns through pairing, reviews, and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use approved agentic AI tools regularly to design tests, analyze results, and draft documentation and review AI output against quality, security, and performance standards before you rely on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree or vocational qualification in electrical engineering, computer science, embedded systems, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience testing software that runs on or with hardware (embedded products, devices, sensors, or similar systems), including independently owning the test and quality approach for that work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RF, embedded, sensor, or similarly hardware-integrated systems, with the technical aptitude and curiosity to develop deep expertise in RF sensor technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and maintaining automated tests or test tooling, ideally in Python pytest, with the ability to independently support hardware-backed regression testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in Linux-based systems (SSH, Networking).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, quality-focused working style: you Join Forces with others, Own It on the quality of the work you take on, and speak up with candor when something is unclear or broken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It’s a plus if you have experience with drones or hardware-in-the-loop / continuous integration test setups and an interest in supporting others as they grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement? That&#39;s ok. At Axon, we Aim Far. We think big with a long-term view because we want to reinvent the world to be a safer, better place. We are also committed to building diverse teams that reflect the communities we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they check every box in the job description. If you’re excited about this role and our mission to Protect Life but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification listed here, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above job description is not intended as, nor should it be construed as, exhaustive of all duties, responsibilities, skills, efforts, or working conditions associated with this job. The job description may change or be supplemented at any time in accordance with business needs and conditions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Some roles may also require legal eligibility to work in a firearms environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We collect personal information from applicants to evaluate candidates for employment. You may request access, deletion, or exercise other CCPA rights at&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; ----- target=&quot;_blank&quot; ----- ----- via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://privacyportal.onetrust.com/webform/0efc1702-9321-4119-bc9d-a06c3a1d3e4e/ca57cc26-a159-4193-9f6e-58ffe3fd2509&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://privacyportal.onetrust.com/webform/0efc1702-9321-4119-bc9d-a06c3a1d3e4e/ca57cc26-a159-4193-9f6e-58ffe3fd2509&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Axon Privacy Web Form&lt;/a&gt;. For more information, please see the Your California Privacy Rights section of our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.axon.com/candidateprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.axon.com/candidateprivacypolicy&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Axon’s mission is to Protect Life and is committed to the well-being and safety of its employees as well as Axon’s impact on the environment. All Axon employees must be aware of and committed to the appropriate environmental, health, and safety regulations, policies, and procedures. Axon employees are empowered to report safety concerns as they arise and activities potentially impacting the environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer that promotes justice, advances equity, values diversity and fosters inclusion. We’re committed to hiring the best talent — regardless of race, creed, color, ancestry, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship status, marital status, disability, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances — and empowering all of our employees so they can do their best work. If you have a disability or special need that requires assistance or accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please email &lt;a ---------- &lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;Please note that this email address is for accommodation purposes only. Axon will not respond to inquiries for other purposes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Phishing alert:&amp;nbsp; Axon will never ask you to pay for any part of the hiring process, including training, equipment, or background checks. We do not make job offers via text message, WhatsApp, or instant messaging platforms without a formal interview process.&amp;nbsp; All legitimate job openings are listed on our official careers page at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.axon.com/careers&quot;&gt;https://www.axon.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;If you receive a suspicious offer or outreach from an email address that is not ----- or if you are asked for sensitive personal information (bank details, Social Security Number) prematurely, please ignore the message and report it to &lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/axon/software-qa-engineer-ii-kassel-hesse-363426","tags":["2024 Dedrone R&D"],"job_types":[],"location":"Kassel, Hesse","created_at":1793375719},{"slug":"permitting-and-regulatory-compliance-manager-darmstadt-135867","company_name":"Focused","title":"Permitting and Regulatory Compliance Manager (f/m/d)","description":"<h1>About Focused Energy</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focused Energy is building the future of clean energy through laser-driven inertial fusion. Backed by our $240M Series A, the largest fully secured Series A in the global fusion industry, we are scaling rapidly across multiple geographies. Based in Germany and the US, we have brought together the top scientific and engineering minds using proven technologies to unlock fusion power at commercial scale. Focused Energy is working to realize game-changing scientific innovation that promises to deliver a clean, sustainable, and abundant source of power globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Your Role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own Focused Energy's permitting and regulatory pathway across our regulated technical facilities, from early feasibility through construction, commissioning, and handover to Operations. You will build and run the integrated permitting strategy under the direction of the Senior Project Manager / Programme Director, and act as our primary contact with competent German authorities. Your work will ensure regulatory requirements shape design, procurement, and construction decisions, with a particular focus on the Biblis site transition and the evolving German fusion regulatory framework.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What You'll Do</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain the integrated permitting strategy, including authority mapping, submission schedules, permit and conditions registers, and regulatory-risk forecasts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead coordinated engagement with municipal, district, Hessian state, and federal authorities, aligning submissions and commitments with the approved project strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own permitting coordination for the Biblis nuclear-site transition, including RWE decommissioning interfaces, existing licences, radiation-protection arrangements, and handover evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate application readiness with Engineering, architects, fire-safety and structural specialists, and the Prüfstatiker, and track reviews to closure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the German fusion legal framework and translate permit conditions and regulatory changes into project requirements, schedules, and risk responses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate material risks and options to the Senior Project Manager / Programme Director, and hand ongoing permit obligations to Operations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Who You Are</h1><h3>Must-Haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience in German construction and public permitting, including building applications, authority consultations, and partial approvals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of Hessian procedures and the Hessische Bauordnung.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of radiation-protection licensing and nuclear-site interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coordinating fire-safety and structural-checking processes with specialists and consultants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to explain regulatory risk and options clearly to non-specialists, including project managers and agency counterparts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, both written and spoken.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice-to-Haves</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tritium or comparable regulated-facility experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multi-agency permitting for novel or regulated technical facilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building reusable permitting playbooks or standards across projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working alongside RWE, licence holders, or other site owners on decommissioning or site handover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with EU or German energy and nuclear regulatory frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentoring capability through example and playbook-building, without formal line management.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What We Offer</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Technology &amp; Mission: Be part of a cutting-edge company working on groundbreaking research in clean energy and scientific discovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Career Development: We invest in our people. This is an opportunity to join an early, growing company at the forefront of new technology, where you’ll have the opportunity to develop and grow your career.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative Culture: Work with great people in a dynamic, international environment with top-tier scientists, engineers and professionals passionate about solving global challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership: Take ownership from day 1 and drive impact by making decisions, solving challenges and shaping the future of our company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your Success is our Success: We offer a competitive salary and company ownership in the form of stock options, giving you a direct stake in our success and ownership in what we build together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vacation Days: We support your work-life-balance by granting you 30 days of vacation per year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Snacks and Drinks: Our office fridges are never empty. Enjoy our healthy snacks and drinks. Our Darmstadt office even offers a canteen with delicious lunch options daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement Plan: If you decide for a private pension plan, we will finance 20% on top of your monthly contributions, plus loyalty incentives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equipment: We offer state-of-the-art Windows or Apple Laptops. In addition, you will receive a keyboard, mouse and headset so you are fully equipped from day 1.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events: We organize regular events to foster team bonding, encourage collaboration, and build a strong, supportive company culture. Connect with colleagues across departments, share ideas, and have fun together, both in and outside of the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mobility with NAVIT: We partner with NAVIT to support your flexible commuting needs - whether it’s a public transportation ticket, taxi rides or car-sharing you choose what fits your lifestyle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fitness with Wellhub: We care about your health. Get access to a wide range of gyms, fitness studios and wellness services across Europe through our partnership with Wellhub.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Focused Energy is an equal opportunity employer committed to creating an inclusive environment. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, Focused Energy will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation offered will be determined by factors such as location, level, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Certain roles may be eligible for incentive compensation, equity, benefits. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/focused/permitting-and-regulatory-compliance-manager-darmstadt-135867","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Darmstadt, DE","created_at":1793374823},{"slug":"public-funding-coordinator-darmstadt-159775","company_name":"Focused","title":"Public Funding Coordinator (f/m/d)","description":"<h1><strong>About Focused Energy</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focused Energy is building the future of clean energy through laser-driven inertial fusion. Backed by our $240M Series A — the largest fully secured Series A in the global fusion industry — we are scaling rapidly across multiple geographies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Germany and the US, we have brought together the top scientific and engineering minds using proven technologies to unlock fusion power at commercial scale. Focused Energy is working to realize game-changing scientific innovation that promises to deliver a clean, sustainable and abundant source of power globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Your Role</strong><br />We are looking for a dedicated <strong>Public Funding Project Coordinator (f/m/d) </strong>to coordinate the full lifecycle of publicly funded projects in Germany and the EU, from opportunity assessment and application through financial administration, reporting, and close-out. Working closely with Technology &amp; Engineering, Global Corporate Affairs, Finance, and project partners, you will translate funding requirements into clear plans and keep budgets, documentation, and deadlines on track. This is a hands-on, AI-first role for someone who combines financial rigor with practical project coordination, resolves issues early, and improves the tools and processes that make funding delivery reliable. <br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What You’ll Do</strong><br /><strong>Funding Opportunities &amp; Applications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own</strong> the end-to-end coordination of assigned public funding projects, from opportunity assessment and application through financial administration, reporting and close-out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead</strong> the consolidation of funding applications, translating requirements into clear workplans, responsibilities, and deadlines when the company decides to pursue an opportunity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enable</strong> informed funding decisions by maintaining a transparent opportunity pipeline with clear information on eligibility, deadlines, and required inputs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial Administration &amp; Compliance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive</strong> timely payment requests and financial reporting by bringing together accurate inputs from Accounting, technical project owners, and project partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ensure</strong> eligible expenditure is tracked and reconciled, and that compliance risks or budget deviations are identified and escalated early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build</strong> and maintain complete, audit-ready project records, including funding conditions, supporting evidence, reporting obligations and correspondence.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Coordination &amp; Process Improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner</strong> with Finance, Technology &amp; Engineering, Global Corporate Affairs, project partners and funding bodies to resolve questions and keep milestones on track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve</strong> workflows, templates and data quality, establishing well-organized project information and using data- and AI-enabled tools where appropriate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Practical experience in public funding administration</strong>, including assessing new funding opportunities, preparing funding applications, payment requests, reporting, financial documentation, or related grant-management activities. Around five years of relevant experience would be helpful, but we value hands-on capability over a fixed number of years or a particular qualification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with German federal or state funding programmes, particularly those supporting research, innovation or industrial development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of funding conditions, eligible-cost requirements and audit-ready documentation, with the ability to translate these into practical project plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, hands-on working style: you manage multiple deadlines, maintain accurate records and follow through on missing information without needing to be chased.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence working with spreadsheets and financial or project data, including consolidating inputs and checking information for accuracy and completeness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, with the ability to explain funding requirements clearly to colleagues, project partners and funding bodies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership and sound judgment: you resolve routine issues independently, communicate risks early, and collaborate effectively across teams without formal authority.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Nice to have</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a public-funding consultancy, research organization, public administration, or a startup or scale-up environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with financial or ERP systems such as NetSuite and an interest in improving workflows through data and AI-enabled tools.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Technology &amp; Mission: Be part of a cutting-edge company working on groundbreaking research in clean energy and scientific discovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Career Development: We invest in our people. This is an opportunity to join an early, growing company at the forefront of new technology, where you’ll have the opportunity to develop and grow your career.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative Culture: Work with great people in a dynamic, international environment with top-tier scientists, engineers and professionals passionate about solving global challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership: Take ownership from day 1 and drive impact by making decisions, solving challenges and shaping the future of our company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your Success is our Success: We offer a competitive salary and company ownership in the form of stock options, giving you a direct stake in our success and ownership in what we build together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vacation Days: We support your work-life-balance by granting you 30 days of vacation per year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Snacks and Drinks: Our office fridges are never empty. Enjoy our healthy snacks and drinks. Our Darmstadt office even offers a canteen with delicious lunch options daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement Plan: If you decide for a private pension plan, we will finance 20% on top of your monthly contributions, plus loyalty incentives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equipment: We offer state-of-the-art Windows or Apple Laptops. In addition, you will receive a keyboard, mouse and headset so you are fully equipped from day 1.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events: We organize regular events to foster team bonding, encourage collaboration, and build a strong, supportive company culture. Connect with colleagues across departments, share ideas, and have fun together, both in and outside of the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mobility with NAVIT: We partner with NAVIT to support your flexible commuting needs—whether it’s a public transportation ticket, taxi rides or car-sharing you choose what fits your lifestyle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fitness with Wellhub: We care about your health. Get access to a wide range of gyms, fitness studios and wellness services across Europe through our partnership with Wellhub.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Focused Energy is an equal opportunity employer committed to creating an inclusive environment. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, Focused Energy will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation offered will be determined by factors such as location, level, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Certain roles may be eligible for incentive compensation, equity, benefits. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/focused/public-funding-coordinator-darmstadt-159775","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Darmstadt, DE","created_at":1793374823},{"slug":"product-designer-berlin-371892","company_name":"Knowunity GmbH","title":"Product Designer","description":"<h1>TL;DR</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a world-class product designer who’s obsessed with craft &amp; excited about AI. You’ll join +60 builders shipping one of Europe’s biggest consumer AI products, shaping how millions of students learn.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Why Knowunity?</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building the <strong>#1 AI learning companion</strong> for 1 billion students. A future where every student on the planet can access, enjoy &amp; benefit from the highest quality education. Since founding Knowunity straight out of high school in 2020, we've been committed to revolutionising how students learn.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Millions of students already use our AI learning companion weekly. We <strong>just raised €27m</strong> - Europe’s largest education round in the past three years. The AI learning market is at an inflection point, finally enabling true personalisation at scale, and we're determined to build the first AI learning unicorn in this space.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join an elite team of <strong>+60 hands-on builders</strong> serving 1 billion students worldwide. If we execute on our product vision, you will have built something generational that transforms education globally. This is your chance to build a generational company that shapes how an entire generation learns.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Why now?</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design is the single highest-leverage investment at Knowunity right now. You’ll be at the center of that shift.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve <strong>built a product millions of students love</strong>, powered by an engineering team that ships &amp; learns extraordinarily fast. Now we’re <strong>going all-in on craft</strong>. The kind of UI excellence, motion design, and systematic thinking that turns a loved product into a world-class one.<br />We just brought on a <strong>new Head of Design</strong>. We’re building a design system from the ground up. And we’re <strong>working with Ragged Edge</strong> (the agency behind the <strong>Transferwise</strong> &amp; <strong>Granola</strong> rebrands) <strong>on a major brand evolution</strong>.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You won’t be maintaining someone else’s vision. You’ll be shaping it from the start.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Who you are</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your portfolio matters more than your years of experience. Show us work that moved metrics &amp; delighted users:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Craft-obsessed: </strong>The details are the design. You push back until the bar is raised.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI enthusiast</strong>: From prototyping to research to shipping. You see AI tools as a multiplier, not a threat.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems thinker:</strong> You care about scaling quality across a product, not a pretty Figma library. Code-first design systems, AI-powered design reviews, whatever works at speed &amp; scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Simplifier:</strong> Education is messy. AI is unpredictable. You turn complicated user journeys into experiences that feel obvious.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Biased to action</strong>: You move fast by default. Prototypes over presentations, experiments over endless debate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder</strong>: You like getting your hands dirty. Bonus if you’ve shipped a side project end to end, or opened a merge request.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team-first</strong>: Direct feedback, no preciousness, no territory. Engineers prototyping features? More builders means better outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curious</strong>: New tools, new patterns, new ways of thinking. You stay up to date &amp; experiment continuously because you want to, not because someone told you to.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What you'll do</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise the bar on everything students see, touch &amp; feel. Make the Knowunity product undeniably world-class.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set the standard</strong>: UIs students want to screenshot &amp; details they feel, but can’t name. Your work is the reference point.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale it</strong>: Curated references, stellar components &amp; sharp reviews. Make it easy even for vibe-coding PMs to hit the standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pioneer AI-native design</strong>: AI changes how we research, ideate, ship, as well as what we ship. You’ll figure out both, from AI-assisted workflows to AI-native product experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Idea to production, fast</strong>: Work directly with C-level &amp; engineering. Concept on Monday, shipped on Wednesday, live for a million students on Thursday.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What we offer</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not for everyone. Everything for the right ones:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact at scale:</strong> Your work reaches millions of students daily. Future generations will know what you build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Elite team, real ownership:</strong> +60 exceptional people. Direct access to C-level &amp; founders. You own entire areas from conception to delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation &amp; equity:</strong> Competitive salary paired with meaningful equity in a company with genuine unicorn potential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong> 28 days annual leave, 40 days work from anywhere, personal development budget, mental health support, Urban Sports Club, monthly retail vouchers, team &amp; company events.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Next steps</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Click “Apply for this job” and submit your CV and LinkedIn profile. We move fast.</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro call</strong>: Get to know each other, see if there’s mutual excitement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5 minute Loom</strong>: walk us through something you’re proud of. A feature you shipped, an app you vibe-coded. Your pick.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep-dive call</strong>: Unpack your Loom case with our head of design/CPO, discuss your experience &amp; perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On-site day</strong>: Meet our CEO, CPO &amp; the team. Work together, get a real feel for the culture. We’ll cover travel.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage applications from exceptional talent regardless of traditional background requirements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Knowunity is an equal opportunity employer committed to diversity and inclusion. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of nationality, ethnic origin, religion, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or marital status. Please don't include photos or age in your application.</em></p><h2></h2><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/knowunity-gmbh/product-designer-berlin-371892","tags":["Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793374817},{"slug":"remote-b2b-marketing-india-26630","company_name":"ElevenLabs","title":"B2B Marketing - India","description":"<h2>About ElevenLabs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is an AI research and product company transforming how we interact with technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in January 2023 with the first human-like AI voice model. Today, we serve millions of users and thousands of businesses - from fast-growing startups to large enterprises like Deutsche Telekom and Meta. Our investors are some of the world's most prominent, including Andreessen Horowitz, ICONIQ Growth and Sequoia. We've raised $781M in funding and our last valuation was $22B - multiples of 11, always.<br /><br />We have expanded from voice into three main platforms:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents enables businesses to deliver seamless and intelligent customer experiences, with the integrations, testing, monitoring, and reliability necessary to deploy voice and chat agents at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenCreative empowers creators and marketers to generate and edit speech, music, image, and video across 70+ languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAPI gives developers access to our leading AI audio foundational models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything we do is the result of the creativity and commitment of our team - builders doing the best work of their lives. We are researchers, engineers, and operators. IOI medalists and ex-founders. If you want to work hard and create lasting positive impact, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual team offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring your entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia, Italy and Cancún</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a senior B2B Growth Marketer to build and scale demand generation for ElevenLabs in India. This is a hands-on, in-country role focused on generating enterprise pipeline, growing our brand with technical buyers, and creating programs that become benchmarks for B2B marketing in AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work will shape how Indian businesses discover, evaluate, and adopt ElevenLabs. The goal is to build repeatable marketing engines that make ElevenLabs the top choice for every enterprise.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build integrated B2B marketing campaigns end to end across India's priority industries from strategy and messaging through execution and measurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Localize and execute programs across ABM, content, events, webinars, partner/customer marketing, executive branding, product launches, and outbound - choosing the right channel for the problem rather than owning a single function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adapt global campaigns and messaging for the Indian market, and feed local insights (buyer behavior, competitive dynamics, regulatory context) back to the global team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with local sales and the global product marketing, growth, and design teams to keep messaging consistent and execute high-impact campaigns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own pipeline generation and campaign performance for the market, using data to measure results, run experiments, and continuously improve what works.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5 to 7 years of experience at a high-growth technology company - you've built and scaled B2B demand generation programs that created measurable enterprise pipeline, and you know what moved the needle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership Pedigree: You have implemented growth and marketing projects from start to finish and held yourself accountable for the ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of the Indian market: its enterprise buyers, media landscape, and business culture, ideally with an existing network.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work well without much process. This role spans multiple marketing functions and needs someone who sets priorities, spots opportunities, and moves quickly as our first marketer in the market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relentless commitment to excellence — a high bar for quality, clarity, and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about AI, follows the technology ecosystem closely, and has exceptional judgment on what makes marketing stand out.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Remote</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/elevenlabs/remote-b2b-marketing-india-26630","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1793374816},{"slug":"influencer-marketing-manager-berlin-188594","company_name":"Taxfix","title":"Influencer Marketing Manager (d/f/m)","description":"<h2>Our story:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every year millions of people are either filing their taxes in fear or giving up on their tax refund altogether. We're working on fixing that. Our intuitive app enables anyone, regardless of education or background, to file their taxes with newfound confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spread across Germany, Spain and the UK, the team at Taxfix Group with its brands Taxfix and Steuerbot, is a compassionate group of solution-finders. We speak our minds openly, and with over 400 professionals, including tax experts, developers, and IT security experts, we're rich in ideas and voices. The group has facilitated more than 3.5 billion euros in tax refunds for its customers since its founding in 2016.<br /></p><h2>The opportunity: </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're now growing our consumer business and building new services for self-employed people and freelancers. To support that, we're looking for an Influencer Marketing Manager to run creator campaigns for Taxfix and Steuerbot.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most people find taxes stressful. Hearing from a creator they already trust that they got money back in one evening is more convincing than an ad. That's why creators are a big part of our marketing. We run the channel in-house with a significant yearly budget and use it both to bring in new users and to build trust in our brands. The hard part is doing both at once: getting new users at a good cost while keeping the content credible for the creator's audience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role reports to the Influencer Marketing Lead and focuses at first on our two German brands, Taxfix and Steuerbot.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run and scale creator campaigns from start to finish: find creators, reach out, negotiate, brief them, review content, take it live and report on results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate deals that make sense for both sides. Push back on first prices and agree on terms like view guarantees or performance-based pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build long-term relationships with creators and their managements, and decide how we work with them across both brands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run frequent hypothesis-driven experiments. We put strong emphasis on asking the right questions, good experiment design, and generating actionable data and interpretations. You own large parts of creator and influencer experimentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You continue to expand our creator database and context layer, allowing you to work very data and insight driven, and enabling AI agents to work alongside or for you equipped with the right data and context.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate the repetitive parts of your job with n8n, Claude Cowork/Code and GitHub, so research, scoring and reporting run on their own and you can spend your time on higher value work with creators, negotiations, content and strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Seasonal campaign planning across multiple platforms, formats and creator sizes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2–4 years of hands-on experience running influencer campaigns on TikTok, Instagram and YouTube, at a brand or an agency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re highly curious about the creator economy and thrive on turning complex, ambiguous challenges into practical solutions in a high-agency role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re an effective and confident negotiator who always strives to get the best deal and who’s not shy to walk away from a deal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re highly analytical and very comfortable with processing and critically interpreting data sets, with an eye for detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are on the path of becoming an AI builder with first basic to advanced workflow automations or other agentic solutions under your belt with measurable impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re experienced in general in how to work with LLMs and agentic solutions effectively, including when to critically review their outputs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator and relationship builder with both, internal stakeholders and external managements and creators. You’re fluent in German and English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you come from performance marketing, growth, affiliate or creator operations and have worked with creators, apply anyway. We'd like to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What your first 90 days look like</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A creator pipeline where you can explain why each creator is on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working relationships with the creators and managements you book.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two structured experiments, with read-outs that say what failed as clearly as what worked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">One recurring task automated, with the hours it saves measured.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Taxfix? </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A chance to do meaningful, people-centric work with an international team of passionate professionals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holistic well-being with free mental health coaching sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A monthly allowance to spend on an extensive range of services that you can use and roll over as flexibly as you like.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee stock options for all employees—because everyone deserves to benefit from the success they help to create.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 annual vacation days and flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A generous learning budget to support your personal and professional development and guidance from our internal L&amp;D experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad for up to six weeks every year. Just align with your team, and then enjoy your trip.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of opportunities to socialise as a team. In addition to internal meetups, our international team hosts regular get-togethers—virtually and in person when possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free tax declaration filing, of course, through the Taxfix app—and internal support for all personal tax-related questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a four-legged friend in your life? We’re happy to have dogs join us in the office.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Excited? So are we. Check out our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/taxfix/life/8684512c-424f-44de-8d07-6e6b516e3319/?viewAsMember=true"> <u>Life at Taxfix</u></a> page on LinkedIn to get a glimpse of our culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Taxfix, we believe that incredible things happen when you have a wealth of perspectives and experiences. We're proudly committed to equal employment and development opportunities no matter your gender, race, religion, age, sexual orientation, colour, disability, or place of origin. To help mitigate any potential unconscious biases, we ask that you refrain from including your picture, age, or marital status on your CV. Let your experiences speak for themselves.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not sure if you meet all the requirements for this role? Please apply anyway. You might bring something special to the team that we hadn't considered previously.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/taxfix/influencer-marketing-manager-berlin-188594","tags":["Performance Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793374816},{"slug":"senior-staff-product-engineer-berlin-288747","company_name":"Cortea AI","title":"Senior/Staff Product Engineer (m/f/x)","description":"<h1>About us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re <strong>Cortea</strong>, a Berlin startup <strong>transforming audits with AI</strong>. Manual, document-heavy audits waste expert time while demand keeps rising. Our <strong>AI-powered software and specialized AI agents</strong> remove the repetitive work so auditors can focus on judgment. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top-tier VCs with &gt;15m funding, with a working product and paying customers, we’re rapidly scaling.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value <strong>first-principles thinking, speed, trust, and kindness</strong>. We build side by side <strong>in our Berlin office</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an <strong>experienced engineer who's happy anywhere in the stack</strong> and turns complex audit workflows into product auditors rely on every day. You pick up whatever a problem needs, from the data model to the interface to the agents behind it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A lot of what we build has no reference implementation. You're <strong>comfortable wading into something nobody has solved yet</strong> and shipping a first version that actually works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our engineering team is a <strong>small, flat group of builders</strong>: strong ICs who open a laptop when they see a problem instead of scheduling a meeting. Everyone owns real product and architecture decisions, and that's exactly what we want more of.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the interfaces auditors work in, partnering with design to turn complex flows into something that feels effortless</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve the agents at the core of the product, plus the harnesses and eval pipelines around them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the long-running workflows behind the product reliable and debuggable, so failures surface fast instead of silently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI heavily in your own workflow to move faster, without ever shipping output you can't stand behind</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the how in RFCs and technical discussions with other engineers, and partner with product on the what</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Qualifications</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll fit here if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have 5+ years shipping production web applications across the stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write production APIs and model the data behind them so it holds up under multi-tenancy and load</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are strong on the frontend and can build genuinely complex UI</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get how LLM agents actually work: agents, harnesses, tool use, and measuring quality with evals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep up with where AI is moving and bring the latest tools into how you work to make yourself faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring a strong product mindset and real ownership of outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make architectural decisions, weigh trade-offs, and build things other engineers can extend</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable with ambiguity and work things out from fundamentals when there's no established answer</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice-to-haves that are a plus:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building agents, harnesses, or eval pipelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data-dense or workflow-heavy B2B products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scaling multi-tenant systems as data and traffic grow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Audit, finance, compliance, or another domain where being wrong is expensive</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Early-stage startup or fast-moving engineering environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>No one checks every box. If you ship across frontend, backend, and data and own what you build, let's talk.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our tech</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">React, TS, Tailwind, TanStack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python, Postgres, Temporal, Kafka, Redis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GCP, Azure, k8s</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GitHub, Linear, Slack, Notion</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High impact &amp; growth:</strong> Front-row seat to scaling an AI startup with real ownership from day one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mission-driven culture:</strong> First-principles thinking, bold ideas, and a supportive team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Attractive compensation:</strong> competitive salary + meaningful equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal development:</strong> Learning budget for courses and conferences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True Berlin startup environment:</strong> Central Berlin office, team lunches, retreats, flexible vacation</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Interview process</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Call</strong> — Intro to Cortea with our Founders Associate Liza</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second Call</strong> — Technical interview with our Member of Technical Staff Jendrik</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Third Call</strong> — Deep dive into our culture with our Co-Founder Philipp</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On-site Half-Day (Berlin) </strong>— Meet the team and work on a real problem together</p></li></ul><h2></h2><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/316125b8-3855-479e-a082-a30caf346d45/1ddbeed3-b4e6-4a47-8872-d5cfeee3e842/image.png" /></div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cortea-ai/senior-staff-product-engineer-berlin-288747","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793374816},{"slug":"ai-engineering-manager-munich-362730","company_name":"Dataguard","title":"AI Engineering Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<h2><strong>YOUR JOB</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do you want to build AI that goes beyond impressive demos and actually works at scale? As our AI Engineering Lead, you’ll take on the harder challenge: turning ambitious ideas into trusted, production-ready technology. You’ll lead a specialist team, shape the architecture behind our AI ambitions and play a defining role in how AI transforms DataGuard.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>WE PROTECT THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE DATA</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a fast-growing security and compliance tech company with a clear purpose: we protect the people behind the data. With over 200 team members worldwide and with offices in Munich, Berlin, London, Stockholm, and Vienna, we help more than 4,000 global customers get certified fast and build a strong and scalable risk posture. With AI-powered automation, self-serve capabilities, and additional tailored expert advice, we offer our customers a seamless security and compliance experience to stay ahead of the rapidly evolving security landscape and challenges like the surge in cyber-attacks.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the target architecture for DataGuard’s AI technology and guide the transition from early-stage solutions to reliable, scalable production systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and develop our three-person AI functional team, setting clear technical direction, priorities and meaningful development paths</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand the DataGuard product ecosystem and identify where AI can create genuine customer and business value across the platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define robust engineering standards for validation, reliability, observability, testing, security, documentation and controlled releases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Engineering, Product, Data Operations and selected business teams to deliver high-value AI initiatives without creating unsupported or unscalable solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance architectural depth with pragmatic delivery, making thoughtful trade-offs while maintaining momentum in an ambitious scale-up environment</p></li></ul><h2></h2><h2><strong>WHAT YOU'LL GET IN RETURN</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The proper tools and capacities to build up and lead an ambitious, international team with diverse skill sets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy the freedom and trust to bring in and execute your ideas with a quick pace, autonomy, and the ability to make impactful decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gain strategic insights into management topics with the opportunity to actively contribute, working closely alongside leadership and executive peers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapid development opportunities, attractive performance bonuses, and the opportunity to strengthen your leadership skills and business expertise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Step into a stable, forward-looking role within a dynamic scale-up poised to shape the fast-growing Security &amp; Compliance industry</p></li></ul><h2></h2><h2><strong>THE QUALITIES YOU'LL NEED FOR A SUCCESSFUL CAREER AT DATAGUARD</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent academic background in computer science, machine learning, mathematics or a related quantitative field</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience taking AI/ML systems from prototype to reliable, scalable production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent architectural judgement and the ability to make clear, pragmatic technical trade-offs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a specialist team while remaining technically credible and hands-on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High engineering standards across testing, observability, security and release quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator who can turn complex AI topics into clear decisions across technical and business teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>LAST BUT NOT LEAST. FROM THE BOTTOM OF OUR HEARTS:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No matter your origin, ethnicity, gender identity, religion or individual requirements; at DataGuard, all that counts is the person you are. As Guards and Guardettes, we are united not only by our dedication, but also by our shared belief in our purpose: Protect the people behind the data. Convince us with your personality and your skills – and together we will make great things happen. We are looking forward to meeting you!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-DNI</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/dataguard/ai-engineering-manager-munich-362730","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1793374816},{"slug":"deployment-strategist-public-sector-emea-396796","company_name":"TRM Labs","title":"Deployment Strategist, Public Sector (EMEA)","description":"<h2>Build a Safer World.</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM Labs provides AI-powered intelligence solutions that help public and private sector agencies investigate and disrupt crime. TRM's platforms enable investigators to trace illicit activity, build cases, and construct operating pictures of threat networks. Leading agencies and businesses worldwide rely on TRM to make the world safer and more secure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an EMEA Public Sector Deployment Strategist, you will own the post-sale experience for a portfolio of public sector customers across the region, including law enforcement agencies, regulators, and government teams working some of the most complex cases in crypto-related crime. You will own onboarding, adoption, outcomes and the relationship across all TRM products, including Ardence, our newest and fastest-moving product. Your mandate is not just to manage accounts. You will define what success looks like for each customer, prove it with usage and outcomes, and enable the renewals and expansion that follow alongside our Account Directors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The impact you will have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboard and activate your EMEA Public Sector accounts across all TRM products, with a clear onboarding path and measurable hands-on-keyboard usage for every account in your portfolio</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI to build production CS workflows that pull from ChurnZero, Salesforce, Gong, and product usage telemetry to auto-generate account health summaries and QBR drafts — compressing hours of reporting prep into minutes so you can spend your time on the work that actually requires human judgment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and track adoption benchmarks across the portfolio — hands-on-keyboard usage, consumption rates, and account-specific success metrics — and surface at-risk accounts before renewal decisions are made</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop new use cases with investigators and analysts that deepen usage across TRM products, including Ardence, and feed what you learn back into onboarding and enablement for the wider team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run executive business reviews and QBRs with senior stakeholders at public sector agencies and regulators across EMEA — building the trust and credibility that turns TRM from a vendor into a mission-critical partner</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with ADs, who own the commercial motion, to enable renewals and expansion: bring account health, adoption evidence, and a structured path to proving value for every customer with an expiring or at-risk contract, and take accountability for the GRR and NRR outcomes that adoption drives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close the feedback loop between customers and Product — synthesize adoption blockers, feature gaps, and new use case opportunities into prioritized, actionable input that informs the roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work as one team with EMEA colleagues across languages and time zones, sharing the playbooks, workflows, and account plans that work so coverage is consistent across the region</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in customer success, deployment, or post-sale roles with proven accountability for GRR, NRR, and adoption outcomes — you have the track record, not just the title</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Domain credibility in law enforcement, public sector, cyber, national security, financial crime, or blockchain intelligence — you can walk into a room of investigators and earn their trust in the first meeting, not the fifth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguity — you have worked in fast-changing product environments, can ship a working v1 without waiting for a perfect playbook, and can point to the specific outcomes it drove; Ardence is still evolving and your accounts may shift as it matures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production AI fluency — you have built real, repeatable AI workflows (not just experiments) that synthesize data from multiple sources into outputs that run consistently and have measurable results; you can show the workflow, explain the data logic, and articulate where human judgment stays in the loop</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High level of independence — you set your own agenda, operate without needing constant direction, and ship v1 before you have all the answers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong executive presence — you can run a QBR with a senior government or public sector stakeholder and command the room through substance, not just polish</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in the UK or Europe and comfortable working with customers across EMEA; additional European languages are a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Team:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The EMEA Public Sector team supports law enforcement, government, and regulatory customers working on complex cases involving crypto-related financial crime, cyber threats, and national security risks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join the EMEA Deployment Strategy team, which covers the region by geography and language (DACH and Eastern Europe, the UK, and SPLATAM), alongside Customer Experience. This is a net-new seat that adds coverage across our accounts, with high autonomy and meaningful influence on how we serve the region</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The broader TRM CS organization operates distributed, not distant — async-first communication through Slack, strong documentation, and intentional synchronous time for key decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work directly with the Head of EMEA Deployment Strategy and the Head of Customer Success, with close day-to-day collaboration with the AD team and Product</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Operating Rhythms:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a globally distributed team, members may observe different timezones. However, most of the team will overlap between the hours of 7am-5:00 pm PST for meetings and collaboration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Customer success Team is fully remote, thriving on asynchronous communication and collaboration through Slack channels and detailed documentation. We hold weekly Customer Syncs, bi-weekly health syncs, join our associated POD calls, and regularly engage with our customers. As experts in our craft, we focus on providing support, driving value, and building meaningful relationships with our customers as trusted advisors. We are on the front lines of TRM, ensuring our customers get the most out of the product and bringing valuable insights back to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moves fast and iterates — v1 ships before it is perfect, and feedback is expected to be direct and specific</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On-Call Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">End-to-End Ownership: While there is no formal hourly rotation, you will be the primary lead for your area and responsible for customer success. This requires a high degree of agency and a commitment to seeing mission-critical tasks through to resolution, including the flexibility to handle urgent needs outside of standard hours or on weekends when they arise.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learn about TRM Speed in this position:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 30 days of joining, you have met every account in your portfolio and shipped a working onboarding and adoption plan for your first 2–3 accounts — not a slide deck, but a live document with measurable adoption benchmarks that the account team is already using to set customer expectations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 6 weeks, you share a draft success metrics framework at 50% complete with the account team and key customers to validate direction — getting real signal on what drives credit consumption before investing further in building out the full playbook</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within 60 days, you identify the highest-impact use case or adoption play for your portfolio — presenting a concrete recommendation to leadership on what to prioritize and why, grounded in actual account data</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Application Instructions</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re interested in joining TRM, we encourage you to apply directly. Every application is reviewed by our Talent team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before applying, review the job description carefully and highlight the experience and impact that best demonstrate the required qualifications. Please also provide thoughtful and accurate answers to the application questions, as these will be used to evaluate your skills and qualifications for the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you send your resume directly to someone at TRM, we can’t guarantee it will reach the appropriate hiring team. Applying directly is the best way to ensure your application will be considered.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Interviewing with TRM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is designed to understand how you think, solve problems, and deliver impact, while allowing you to evaluate TRM. Most interview processes include a case study, an AI skills assessment, and a Leadership Principles interview.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruiter Intro:</strong> Qualifications, motivations, and alignment with the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager:</strong> Deep dive into your relevant experience, skills, and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Round:</strong> 1–2 interviews focused on the skills most critical to the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Round: </strong>Hands-on case study. This is usually a panel-style session where we go deeper into your craft, problem-solving, and alignment with TRM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>References:</strong> Former colleagues who can provide insight into your work and impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congrats! Your recruiter will present the offer and compensation details.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Welcome to TRM:</strong> We're excited to build a safer world with you!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your recruiter will share your specific interview plan and preparation guidance along the way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>AI Fluency at TRM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI fluency is a baseline expectation at TRM.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe AI meaningfully changes how top performers operate. We expect every team member to use AI to accelerate and reimagine their craft, not just automate surface tasks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TRM, AI fluency means you are among the top 10 percent of operators in your function in how you apply AI to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accelerate repeatable workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structure and solve problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve output quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increase speed and leverage</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be evaluated on applied AI fluency during the interview process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Life at TRM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building a safer world. That promise shows up in how we work every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM moves FAST. We are a high-velocity, high-ownership team that expects clarity, follow-through, and impact. People who thrive here are energized by hard problems, experimentation, and continuous feedback. If something takes months elsewhere, it will ship here in days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work sits at the intersection of AI, national security, and fighting crime. The problems are complex, the stakes are real, and the environment evolves quickly. The pace and intensity of the work reflect the importance of the mission. As a result, the way we operate requires a high level of ownership, adaptability, collaboration, and creative problem-solving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TRM, you should expect:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Priorities and targets to change quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operating with a high degree of ambiguity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A high level of personal ownership and accountability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaboration across teams and functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frequent, high-touch communication</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creative problem-solving and out-of-the-box thinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pace that rewards urgency, adaptability, and outcomes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This environment is energizing for people who enjoy building, solving hard problems, and making progress in situations that are not always fully defined. It also requires thriving in ambiguity, adjusting course as new information emerges, and maintaining focus and positivity in a fast-moving and intense environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We also recognize that this style of operating is not for everyone. If you are primarily optimizing for predictability or a consistently balanced workload, we encourage you to use the interview process to pressure-test whether this environment is truly the right fit. We want teammates who thrive here, not just survive here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are excited by meaningful problems, motivated by ambitious goals, and energized by working alongside mission-driven colleagues, there is a good chance you will find TRM to be an exceptional place to grow and contribute. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Leadership Principles</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire and grow against three leadership principles. They’re the standards for how we operate, treat each other, and make decisions.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact-Oriented Trailblazer: We put customers first and move with speed, focus, and adaptability. We treat every plan like an experiment – test, ship, measure, and iterate quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master Craftsperson: We care deeply about our craft. We balance speed with high standards, own outcomes end‑to‑end, and invest in getting better everyday.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inspiring Colleague: We add clarity and energy, not noise. We bring humility, candor, and a one‑team mindset — giving and receiving feedback to make the team stronger.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h2><strong>Join our Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At TRM, we care deeply about our craft. We are looking for individuals who want their work to matter, who experiment with speed and rigor, and who take pride in building a safer world for billions of people. If you’re excited by TRM’s mission but don’t check every box, we encourage you to apply — we hire for slope, judgment, and the will to learn fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">TRM is a Series C company with $220M in total funding, backed by Goldman Sachs, Bessemer, Y Combinator, Thoma Bravo, and others. Headquartered in San Francisco, TRM operates as a distributed-first company with hubs in Los Angeles, San Francisco, New York, Washington D.C., London, and Singapore. </p><h3></h3><h2><strong>Privacy Policy and Additional Information</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your application, you agree to allow TRM Labs to process your personal information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.trmlabs.com/policies/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We collect the information you provide (such as your resume, work history, and contact details) solely for the purpose of evaluating your candidacy for current and future roles at TRM.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Because our hiring cycles for certain positions may span 24 to 36 months, we retain your personal information for up to 36 months from the date of your application. After that period, your data is deleted unless a different retention period is required or permitted by law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or another jurisdiction with applicable data protection laws, you have the right to access, correct, or request deletion of your personal data at any time before that period ends. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:dec