s for CI/CD, release strategies, and Infrastructure as Code.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Integration:</strong> Define architecture and integration patterns for APIs, events, and batch interfaces.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Security:</strong> Incorporate security, monitoring, resilience, high availability, and regulatory requirements into the architecture.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Data &amp; AI:</strong> Translate data and AI strategies into concrete architecture components and integration patterns.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Technical Sparring:</strong> Support Development, Infrastructure, Security, and business teams with technical decisions.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="wp-block-heading" style="text-align:start;"><strong>Your profile</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><p><strong>Education:</strong> A completed degree in IT or a comparable qualification provides the foundation for this role.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Architecture:</strong> Several years of experience as a Solution, Cloud, or Enterprise Architect in complex IT environments.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Hands on:</strong> Practical programming experience and a strong technical understanding are essential.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Cloud:</strong> Very good knowledge of modern cloud, network, and identity architectures, ideally complemented by Azure experience.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Technology:</strong> Experience with microservices, APIs, CI/CD, Infrastructure as Code, and modern platform architectures.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Industry:</strong> Experience in banking, insurance, investment, or a comparable financial environment, combined with experience in modern cloud or SaaS environments.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>Communication:</strong> Excellent English skills and the ability to communicate complex technical decisions clearly and effectively.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="tex