&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take it live.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Coordinate User Acceptance Testing, resolve what testing surfaces, and upskill super users so the customer is proficient and self-sustaining after go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own adoption, not just delivery.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;A technically correct solution that nobody uses is not a successful project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Document what you built&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— requirements, scope and configuration — so the project team, the customer and our Continuous Services colleagues can work with it after handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work across disciplines&lt;/strong&gt;: with Technical Consultants on the data model, interfaces and the customer&#39;s ERP landscape, and with Project Managers on scope, effort and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within RELEX&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge and develop implementation best practice across industries (grocery, DIY, home goods, pharma, wholesale and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge with the team as both a trainer and a participant, and support colleagues who are earlier in their journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our global teams on international projects and bring practices between regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tooling actively in your daily work — we expect curiosity here and give you room to experiment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Around 2+ years of relevant experience&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;in supply chain or retail planning, demand and inventory planning, or in implementing / consulting on planning software. A degree in supply chain management, business, engineering, mathematics or computer science is a good foundation — but we care more about what you have actually done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured thinking and comfort with ambiguity.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Many customer requirements arrive without a ready-made answer. You break them down, work with data, and arrive at a defensible recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication that works across levels&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— from super users in a training room to senior stakeholders in a steering committee, including the conversations where the message is not what the customer hoped to hear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business-fluent German and English.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Both are used daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willingness to travel&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;depending on the project phase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical affinity&lt;/strong&gt;: SQL, scripting, or an interest to pick these up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additionally, for the Senior level:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of consulting or implementation experience, including&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;demonstrable ownership of a workstream or a smaller project end-to-end&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— scope, risk, timeline and completion, not just your own tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable effort estimation for standard and custom requirements, supporting scoping and SOW discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching and mentoring less experienced colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in front of senior customer stakeholders, including steering committees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a supply chain planning system, either as a user or as an implementer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and tracking KPIs or building a value case&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We’re bold thinkers and kind teammates, growing fast but staying grounded. Our Nordic roots and global outlook shape a culture of friendliness, creativity, and collaboration, all powered by openness and shared wins. We care deeply about doing the right thing - and doing it together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility in how and where you work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Room to thrive&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;in a fast-growing global company with a good market position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical benefits that support work, family, wellness, and everyday life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse, inclusive, and supportive work culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work that meaningfully reduces waste and improves sustainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership, autonomy and flat hierarchies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two paid volunteering days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are a global community of different cultures, voices, and experiences. We celebrate what makes us unique and connect through what we share, in an authentic and safe environment. Together we shape the future, and each other.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;If you feel this is the opportunity you don’t want to miss, you can apply by sending your resume through the application form as soon as possible. Please note that we cannot process any applications through email.   &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Apply today and be part of the future. Be RELEX!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www.relexsolutions.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/relex-greenhouse-banner-bottom.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1280&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/relex/senior-supply-chain-consultant-wiesbaden-421781","tags":["Operations EMEA and APAC"],"job_types":[],"location":"Wiesbaden","created_at":1793364924},{"slug":"gtm-lead-germany-berlin-397650","company_name":"Parallel","title":"GTM Lead Germany","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Parallel, we build AI agents to help healthcare facilities automate their administrative processes and unlock additional revenue, starting with medical coding.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Today, up to 25% of healthcare spending is lost in manual, repetitive administrative work. Legacy software hasn’t helped, it’s made things slower, more complex, and more frustrating for care teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe AI agents can change that. Our technology combines Large Language Models with system-level automation to handle real work inside existing hospital tools. No integrations, no disruption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first agent automates coding workflows and frees up time for medical staff to focus on patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in 2024, are backed by top investors (Index, Frst, Y Combinator, Hexa, Kima Ventures, Better Angle), and we’re just getting started.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The future of healthcare isn’t just digital — it’s automated. Come help us build it !</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Context</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Germany is one of Europe's largest healthcare markets, and its hospitals face the same pressure we solve in France: rising administrative load, staff shortages and revenue lost to incomplete coding.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Germany GTM Lead, you are our first hire in the country. You will report directly to Paul Lafforgue, CEO and co-founder, and work closely with Chris, our CTO, and the product team in Paris. You will own everything from the first prospecting call to the first signed contracts, shape the local product and build the German team from zero.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> 2 to 3 months of onboarding in Paris, then based in Germany with regular trips to Paris. Office in Munich or Berlin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team:</strong> none at first. Around 5 people in H1 2027, around 12 by the end of 2027.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Your mission</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take Parallel from zero to a validated, repeatable market in Germany by the end of 2027: 2 to 3 flagship hospitals as paying customers, 2M€ ARR and a local team of around 15.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Outcomes</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First customers:</strong> build the pipeline with Paul, book your own first meetings (your calendar starts empty), sign the first pilots and turn them into paying contracts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>German go-to-market:</strong> pick the segment to win first (private groups, public or university hospitals), adapt the pitch to the German healthcare context, test our success-based pricing, including in public tenders, and build visibility through networks, trade shows and customer references.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Local product:</strong> run the feedback loop between German hospitals and the product &amp; tech team, and bring in local medical expert(s) to validate usage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>German team:</strong> hire a team growing from 0 to around 12 across sales, ops, engineers and set up the office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth story:</strong> report on Germany's progress to the leadership team and investors, and, if we acquire a local company, contribute to due diligence and lead the integration of the acquired team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Who you are</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">A builder who wants to open a market, not run one. This job is for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a native German speaker, with your schooling and career in Germany, and fluent in English, our working language with headquarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 5 to 10 years of experience, including at least 2 years in a quota-carrying B2B sales role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have lived at least one 0-to-1 experience: you founded a company, joined a startup of fewer than 50 people or launched a new market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy being on the ground: meeting customers, travelling and opening doors yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable with ambiguity and an empty playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are credible with hospital leadership (CEO, CFO, chief medical officer) as well as with physicians.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can convince first hires to join a company that nobody in Germany knows yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are open to about 3 months of regular trips to Paris, with a long-term base in Germany.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong> you know the German healthcare system, or you have already launched a business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong> you have hired and managed a team, or worked on M&amp;A or the integration of an acquired team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Our values</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to Win:</strong> we are not here just to participate, ship something “good enough”, or enjoy the startup ride. We want to win. That means caring deeply about outcomes, moving fast and being willing to put in the intensity required when it matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High Trust, High Standards:</strong> trust is our default. If you joined us, it's because we believe you can own your scope and make good decisions. We don't want a company built on approvals, control and micromanagement. But trust comes with responsibility. The more freedom we give, the higher the standard we expect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low Ego, Hands-On:</strong> no one at Parallel is above doing the work. Titles, seniority and past achievements don't exempt anyone from getting their hands dirty. Everyone should be willing to step into the arena when needed. Leadership means taking responsibility, not creating distance from execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Don't Take Yourself Too Seriously:</strong> we are extremely serious about our mission. We don't need to be extremely serious about ourselves. Building a company is intense. We want Parallel to remain a place where people enjoy spending time together, laugh, celebrate and bring energy to the people around them. High standards and good vibes are not opposites. We want both.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1>Hiring process</h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screening call (40 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical case + Q&amp;A with Paul, CEO (video call, 45 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Presentation of your written practical case (video call, 1h30)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business case in Paris (half a day)</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Why should you join us?</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A rare opportunity:</strong> open Parallel's first international market as employee #1 in the country, with a direct line to the CEO and the room to build the team, the playbook and the office your way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A product that already works:</strong> you start with a live product, around 800 customer references in France and local CTO in Germany ready to adapt it with you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real-world impact:</strong> every hospital you sign gives clinical staff time back from paperwork to improve patient care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Package &amp; perks:</strong> competitive salary and meaningful equity, health insurance, top-quality equipment and a public-transport contribution.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We care about who you are, not just what's on your CV.</strong><br /><br />If you're drawn to what we're building but don't meet every requirement, we still want to hear from you. Studies show that women in particular tend to apply only when they meet 100% of the criteria. If that's you, please don't let that hold you back. We'd love to receive your application.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/parallel/gtm-lead-germany-berlin-397650","tags":["New Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1793364018},{"slug":"instrumentation-development-embedded-engineer-munich-323677","company_name":"Proxima Fusion GmbH","title":"Instrumentation Development Embedded Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proxima Fusion is Europe’s fastest-growing fusion company and the continent’s best-funded fusion player, as well as the first spin-out from the Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics (IPP). Backed by over €650M and powered by a growing team across Munich, Zurich, and Oxford, we are developing the hardware and infrastructure needed to deliver the world’s first commercial stellarator fusion power plant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our concept advances the most mature fusion technology out there, the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator, through two next-generation machines: Alpha and Stellaris. Our work combines stellarator optimization, advanced computation, machine learning, and high-temperature superconducting magnets to unlock higher-performance designs that were previously out of reach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turning these designs into a functioning fusion power plant requires excellence and ownership across every discipline, from physics and engineering to software, manufacturing, law, and business functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY JOIN PROXIMA FUSION</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will get to work on some of the most complex tech challenges to bring abundant, safe, clean energy to the world.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get to join and learn from an exceptional selection of accomplished and driven individuals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do your life’s best work and enjoy the journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get to show that big things are possible in Europe when you assemble the best talent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>YOUR IMPACT</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Instrumentation Development Embedded Engineer, you will own the development of high-speed control and protection systems for the Alpha fusion demonstrator, focusing on FPGA-based solutions for plasma heating hardware protection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work across the full development lifecycle, from writing and verifying HDL code to developing software-in-the-loop and hardware-in-the-loop testing, integrating embedded software and electronics, and establishing robust development and deployment pipelines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also help establish Proxima’s FPGA development capability beyond plasma heating, defining reusable architectures, development workflows, testing methodologies, and HDL best practices that can be adopted across other systems.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT YOU WILL DO</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, implement, and maintain HDL-based control and protection systems, starting with plasma heating system protection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish end-to-end FPGA development workflows, CI/CD pipelines, and SIL/HIL test environments integrated with plant design frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop embedded software, firmware, and low-level drivers to interface FPGAs with sensors, actuators, and other control systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate across RF, controls, electronics, and systems teams to define system interfaces, ICDs, and verification plans.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in Electronics, Embedded Systems, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong proficiency in HDL (VHDL, Verilog, SystemVerilog) and software scripting (Python, C/C++).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience integrating FPGAs with hardware peripherals, board-level electronics, and communication interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with modern software development practices (Git, CI, code review, automated testing).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Systems-thinking approach with strong debugging skills spanning HDL, embedded firmware, and physical hardware.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-speed digital interfaces (multi-gigabit serial links, LVDS, SerDes, RF/instrumentation links) and PCB-level signal integrity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">FPGA+processor platforms and MPSoCs (e.g., AMD/Xilinx Zynq UltraScale+).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Precision timing and synchronization (IEEE 1588 PTP, White Rabbit)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Network protocols (Ethernet).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real-time signal processing, fast protection systems, and high-speed data acquisition in fusion or industrial environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">HDL design methodologies and techniques for reliable radiation-hardened systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Schematic comprehension and custom PCB development.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>INTERVIEW PROCESS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter Interview (30-60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Screening (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Panel (3x60 min)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />*This role sits at "L2" of our framework, please inquire during the recruitment process for further information.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Proxima Fusion, our mission is bold: making limitless clean energy a reality. To get there, we need a high-performing, diverse team that brings different perspectives, challenges assumptions, and builds together with purpose. We know that diversity of thought and experience leads to better ideas, stronger execution, and a more resilient team. We don’t look at how you identify, what you look like, who you choose to worship or what ethnicity you are. We care about what you can bring to the table.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/proxima-fusion-gmbh/instrumentation-development-embedded-engineer-munich-323677","tags":["Stellarator Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1793364014},{"slug":"business-development-associate-munich-429548","company_name":"Proxima Fusion GmbH","title":"Business Development Associate","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proxima Fusion is Europe’s fastest-growing fusion company and the continent’s best-funded fusion player, as well as the first spin-out from the Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics (IPP). Backed by over €650M and powered by a growing team across Munich, Zurich, and Oxford, we are developing the hardware and infrastructure needed to deliver the world’s first commercial stellarator fusion power plant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our concept advances the most mature fusion technology out there, the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator, through two next-generation machines: Alpha and Stellaris. Our work combines stellarator optimization, advanced computation, machine learning, and high-temperature superconducting magnets to unlock higher-performance designs that were previously out of reach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turning these designs into a functioning fusion power plant requires excellence and ownership across every discipline, from physics and engineering to software, manufacturing, law, and business functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY JOIN PROXIMA FUSION</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will get to work on some of the most complex tech challenges to bring abundant, safe, clean energy to the world.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get to join and learn from an exceptional selection of accomplished and driven individuals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do your life’s best work and enjoy the journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get to show that big things are possible in Europe when you assemble the best talent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>YOUR IMPACT</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proxima will sell fusion electricity in the late 2030s. Proxima's Business Development team finds and executes business opportunities on the way there: inorganic (acquisitions, minority stakes and joint ventures in businesses synergetic with Proxima) and organic (new product lines built from Proxima assets). You will own opportunities along our Business Development playbook, from market scan to a clear go/no-go from leadership, with an initial focus on inorganic deals. You will work directly with the Business Development Lead and the Head of Business Operations, within the CFO organization, and alongside engineering, finance, legal, and supply chain teams.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT YOU WILL DO</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the front of the deal funnel:</strong> Build market reports, competitive landscapes, and company mappings that shape where Proxima invests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive clear decisions</strong>: Build decision memos and business cases that lead to a go/no-go from the leadership team and board, pulling in our engineers to ground the analysis in technical reality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run deal workstreams</strong>: Lead expert calls, reference checks and data room screening.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strengthen the function</strong>: Contribute roadmap and communication, and systematically deploy AI tools to speed up research, screening, and drafting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Source new opportunities</strong>: Attend conferences and industry events, and feed new ideas into the pipeline, including organic ones over time.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deal execution experience</strong>: 2-3 years in tier-1 strategy consulting, private equity, venture capital, or a fast-paced startup, ideally with exposure to industrials, energy, or advanced manufacturing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical fluency</strong>: STEM degree (engineering, physics, mathematics or similar), or a demonstrated ability to work fluently with technical teams on technical topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Standalone problem-solving and judgement</strong>: You take an ambiguous question, structure it, run the analysis, and come back with a recommendation, without waiting to be told how.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Modeling and writing craft</strong>: Strong market modeling and memo-writing skills; you can build a valuation, a business plan, and a two-page decision document that leadership actually reads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear communication</strong>: Fluent in English (written and spoken), comfortable in front of founders, suppliers, and senior stakeholders; German is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Startup mindset:</strong>