ctly with our CTO, Christopher Klabunde. We have plenty of ideas and are looking for someone who enjoys building things, thinks for themselves and cares about quality.</p><h2>What you will work on</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Android development:</strong> Build new features for our device software and app, improve existing workflows and create an intuitive, reliable user experience.</p></li><li><p><strong>Connected systems:</strong> Work on interfaces between the app, device software and backend, helping make data flows and error handling reliable.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hands-on prototyping:</strong> Turn ideas into working prototypes, try them on our rowing machines and develop promising approaches with the team.</p></li><li><p><strong>Quality from the start:</strong> Write understandable, maintainable code, take part in reviews and tests, and fix problems thoroughly.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI-assisted development:</strong> Use AI tools for ideas, coding, testing and debugging. Understand and verify their output before it becomes part of the product.</p></li></ul><h2>Your role as Scrum Master</h2><p>Alongside your technical work, you will help our projects move forward as a team. As Scrum Master, you will coordinate collaboration within our software team and with external development agencies, working closely with CTO Christopher Klabunde. This role does not include line-management responsibility.</p><ul><li><p>Bring internal developers and external partners into a shared plan, with clear responsibilities, next steps and acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p>Prepare and facilitate agile discussions, such as sprint planning, short daily check-ins, reviews and retrospectives, adapted to the needs of our projects.</p></li><li><p>Track dependencies, milestones and open decisions, raise obstacles early and help the team resolve them.</p></li><li><p>Help bring everyone’s work together so it can be tested as a complete product and prepared for reliable releases.</p></li></ul><p>If you already have Scrum Master or project coordination experience, bring it with you. If you are new to the role, Chris and the team will support you as you grow into it. A Scrum Master certification is welcome, but not required.</p><h2>What you bring</h2><ul><li><p>Programming fundamentals and an interest in native Android development with Kotlin or Java. Android experience is welcome; if you are new to it, tell us how you learn and why it interests you.</p></li><li><p>The ability to explain how you approach a technical problem. Personal apps, learning projects, university work, internships and student jobs all count alongside professional experience.</p></li><li><p>An interest in writing reliable, maintainable software and learning how to test it well.</p></li><li><p>Openness to AI-assisted app development and a willingness to question and check the results.</p></li><li><p>Initiative, a collaborative approach and the desire to learn an existing product and gradually take ownership.</p></li><li><p><strong>Good spoken and written English is required.</strong> You need to discuss technical topics confidently with the team. <strong>German is not required, but it is a strong advantage.</strong></p></li><li><p>The ability to work regularly on site in Königs Wusterhausen, where we develop and test directly on the devices.</p></li></ul><p>A degree in computer science or a related subject, relevant vocational training, or equivalent knowledge provides a good foundation.</p><h2>Experienced or just starting out? We would like to meet you</h2><p>Already have several years of experience? Great – bring your ideas and a fresh perspective. New to this field or looking for your first professional role? That is welcome too. If you are excited about our product, have a technical foundation and learn quickly, we would like to hear from you.</p><p>Whichever stage you are at, it is our job to help you settle into the team and provide the knowledge, tools and support you need to succeed. You will get to know our product and ways of working alongside Chris and the team. We will match your initial tasks and responsibilities to your experience and help you grow from there.</p><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul><li><p>Experience with Firebase as an app backend, for example user authentication, data storage or server-side logic.</p></li><li><p>Experience in iOS development, ideally with Swift or SwiftUI.</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Git, automated testing, CI/CD, API integration or connecting software to devices.</p></li></ul><h2>What we offer</h2><ul><li><p>A real product you can try out yourself, with a direct impact on how our customers train.</p></li><li><p>A company of around 25 people, a small software team and close collaboration with CTO Christopher Klabunde.</p></li><li><p>Room for your ideas and professional growth, with responsibilities that develop with your skills.</p></li><li><p>A permanent, full-time position: 40 hours per week and 28 days of annual leave.</p></li><li><p>€50,000–€65,000 gross per year, depending on your relevant skills and experience.</p></li><li><p>A workplace in Königs Wusterhausen near Berlin, with one or two days of working from home per week by agreement.</p></li></ul><h2>Working near Berlin</h2><p>Our office is at Zur Heide 10, Königs Wusterhausen. The town has direct S46 S-Bahn and regional train connections to Berlin; you can cycle from the station to our office. Regular on-site work matters because development, testing and teamwork happen around the actual rowing machines. This is a hybrid role based in Germany.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Send us your CV in English or German. No formal cover letter is needed. A GitHub link or an app you have worked on is welcome, but optional.</p><p>We will start with a short online conversation, followed by a closer look at your experience, learning approach and the work at AUGLETICS.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"ur