 varied range of certification activities, with scope to take ownership of broader operational improvements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and coordinate certification programs, including client considerations and audit time calculations, and improve how milestones, dependencies and follow-up activities are managed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review applications and shape project plans, identifying device codes, required assessments and assessor competence requirements, while streamlining routine checks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare certificates following approved certification decisions and coordinate surveillance and renewals, simplifying administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Streamline certificate transfers by coordinating next steps with customers and outgoing certification bodies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Triage medical device change notifications and coordinate the appropriate specialist review, improving how changes are categorised and routed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep customers and colleagues informed of progress, outstanding actions and next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with product and engineering to improve procedures and automate routine workflows, so your work increasingly focuses on the most complex customers and cases.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Required qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years’ experience in operations, project delivery, or a related discipline. You’ve owned detailed projects or workflows from planning through completion, meeting agreed deadlines and communicating complex information clearly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical background. A degree or equivalent in Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics, or another analytically demanding subject, or comparable achievement through technical work, research or independent projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of solving difficult problems independently. You can explain an unfamiliar problem you tackled, how you broke it down, the decisions you made and the result you achieved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An eye for detail. Experience reviewing detailed documents or data for completeness and accuracy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in healthcare, certification or another regulated industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of medical technology and the role of certification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Interview process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductory call with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sarahburley/">Sarah</a> — 20 minutes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nadinecaballero/">Nadine</a>/<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sasharanasinghe/">Sasha</a> — 45 minutes. Review a case study, prioritise actions and suggest an improvement. All relevant process rules will be provided.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sarahburley/">Sarah</a> — 45 minutes. Review a case study, prioritise actions and suggest an improvement. All relevant process rules will be provided.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tirion-h-evans/">Tiri</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-dewar-78758992/">James</a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jamie-cox-01458b3a/">Jamie</a> — 20 minutes each. Values and working style interviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">References and offer.</p></li></ol><hr><p>Compensation: £60K – £70K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £60K – £70K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/scarlet/certification-program-manager-london-274065","tags":["Tech Ops"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK - London Office","created_at":1793396420},{"slug":"work-at-scarlet-london-252419","company_name":"Scarlet","title":"Work at Scarlet","description":"<h2><strong>We pull medical technology from the future to solve human health.</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scarlet is authorised to assess and certify medical devices. We combine clinical, technical and regulatory expertise with AI agents and software so rigorous certification can keep pace with product development at the world’s most ambitious technology companies, without lowering the safety bar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers have cut a year or more from their certification timelines for new AI-enabled medical devices and shortened product-update cycles from months to weeks. You’ll join a team building the infrastructure that makes these outcomes repeatable at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About this application</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to work at Scarlet but none of our current openings fits your experience, you can submit a general application here. Tell us what you are good at, what you could contribute and the kind of work you want to do. We'd love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Backgrounds of interest</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are particularly interested in hearing from people with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional or academic experience in a field related to Scarlet’s work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of applying skills from another industry to unfamiliar problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in medical technology, life sciences or another regulated industry</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What happens next</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will review your application against our current and planned openings. If your experience appears relevant to something we are hiring for, we will contact you to discuss it.</p><h2></h2><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/scarlet/work-at-scarlet-london-252419","tags":["Team"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"UK - London Office","created_at":1793396420},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-software-london-482428","company_name":"Comind","title":"Senior Product Manager, Software","description":"<h3><strong>Company Overview</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">At CoMind, we are developing a non-invasive neuromonitoring technology that will result in a new era of clinical brain monitoring. In joining us, you will be helping to create cutting-edge technologies that will improve how we diagnose and treat brain disorders, ultimately improving and saving the lives of patients across the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Senior Product Manager to own how our device software behaves. You'll take the product vision and turn it into features our software team can build with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is product work at the level of detail. You'll think through how features should behave in every situation, including the edge cases, and give the team clear answers. You'll also make sure that work gets delivered. That means keeping the backlog in shape, setting priorities and following features through to release. You'll start on future releases of CoMind One, our first product, and help shape CoVision as it moves towards delivery. As the team and product line grow, so does the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At CoMind, all team members work at least 4 days per week from our new Kings Cross offices, plus a flexible work-from-home day.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define how features work, step by step, including the edge cases and failure modes that matter in a clinical setting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Package features for build: what it does, why it matters, what it looks like, and the decision logic behind it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prototype flows and interactions using AI tools, so the team sees the idea before they build it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sit with the software team and make the call when a feature question comes up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the link between our commercial team and the software team, turning customer and market needs into clear requirements. Use quick prototypes to test those needs with customers and the commercial team before they reach the backlog.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the product roadmap with the Product Lead.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the software backlog in Jira: intake, triage and grooming, so it reflects real priority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write acceptance criteria and check that what ships matches what was intended.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Project Manager, who runs sprints, so sequencing and timing reflect real priority rather than convenience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep decisions and documentation in Confluence, not lost in Slack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is fundamental to our culture — it's not just a tool, but a core part of how we work, collaborate, and innovate. We expect all team members to embrace AI in their daily work and continuously find new ways to use it effectively.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Skills &amp; Experience:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable product management experience on software that runs on physical hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand the pace of regulated hardware: long development cycles and infrequent releases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of making product decisions from logic and a deep understanding of users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing requirements precise enough for engineers to build without repeated back-and-forth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable debating a feature with engineers and explaining why it matters for the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A natural translator: equally comfortable in a conversation with a non-technical stakeholder describing a problem and in a ticket-grooming session with engineers debating implementation trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI tools heavily in your day-to-day work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building interactive prototypes, using AI tools to turn an idea into something clickable that users and engineers can react to.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical device experience, or exposure to ISO 13485 or IEC 62304.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software engineering or technical background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with embedded or real-time software.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company equity plan so all employees share in the success of the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salary-sacrifice pension scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private medical, dental and vision insurance (medical history disregarded)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Group life insurance at 4x annual income</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive mental health support, including unlimited access to 1:1 sessions with trained professionals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited holiday allowance (+ bank holidays) and one week of remote working per quarter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch voucher (£10) every day for JustEat and free dinner on those days where you need to work later</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Twice weekly deliveries of fresh fruit and an extensive selection of snacks and drinks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">YuLife subscription, allowing you to turn your daily steps and meditation into discounts at a range of stores</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Disclaimer</strong> - We use Granola, an AI notetaker, throughout our interview process to help capture notes. It's used only for note-taking during the conversation. Transcripts aren't saved to shared drives or stored externally. Let us know if you'd prefer we don't.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: £80K – £110K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • Salary £80K – £110K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/comind/senior-product-manager-software-london-482428","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1793396419},{"slug":"head-of-capital-london-210390","company_name":"Relay","title":"Head of Capital","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relay is fundamentally reshaping how goods move in an online era.</strong> Backed by Europe’s largest-ever logistics Series A ($35M) led by deep-tech investors Plural, and a recently closed Series B ($95M), Relay is scaling faster than 99% of venture-backed startups. We're assembling the most talent-dense team the logistics industry has ever seen</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relay’s Mission is</strong> to <strong>free commerce from friction</strong>. Today, high delivery costs act as a hidden tax on e-commerce, quietly shaping what can be sold online and limiting who can participate. We envision a world where <strong>more goods move more freely between more people</strong>, making the online shopping experience seamless and accessible to everyone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE TEAM<br /></strong>• <strong>~160 people</strong>,  around half in engineering, product and data<br />• <strong>45+ advanced degrees</strong> across computer science, mathematics and operations research<br />• <strong>Thousands</strong> of data points captured, calculated, analysed and predicted for every single parcel we handle<br />• An intellectually vibrant culture of <strong>first‑principles thinking</strong>, tight feedback loops and relentless experimentation</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Head of Capital to run how Relay raises equity and works with its investors: the next round and the ones after it, from the investor map to the close, next to the CEO.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relay is a technology enabled parcel carrier - we deliver parcels from retailers to end customers but do it much more efficiently than incumbents. This efficiency has propelled us into one of the fastest growing companies in Europe - we have grown over 40x in the last 18 months. The capital Relay raises decides how fast the network grows and what it can promise retailers. Raising it well, from the right investors, on terms we understand, is a job in its own right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The capital we raise next decides how fast the network grows and what it can promise retailers. Our next round is planned for Q2/Q3 2027. It is for growth, from growth-stage investors, and it will be won on evidence. Today a raise runs through the CEO and the CFO alongside their day jobs. It works. It is however, not a system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the person who makes it one. You will not just be the person who holds and runs the Series C transaction, but also be the Head of the Office that will build the systems to raise multiple rounds of capital in the future. Between rounds you keep the map, the materials and the investors warm, so each raise starts from a record, not a blank page. Few roles let you own how a growing company raises the capital it runs on, from the inside, round after round.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you work with</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CEO:</strong> you report here. The CEO pitches and takes the decisions on a round.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CFO:</strong> you work together daily. The CFO owns the budget, the forecast, internal finance and any debt. You own equity, the investors behind it, and the investor-facing model built from the CFO's numbers — never a second set.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-founder and the Extended Leadership Team:</strong> the proof a round needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>External &amp; Internal Counsel:</strong> terms and the close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Board:</strong> updates between rounds and approval on the round.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Running the transaction with the CEO &amp; CFO</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the investor map: which funds, which partner at each, why each fits us, in what order we go, and the warm path to each.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The process start to close: the timeline, outreach, a brief before every meeting and notes after, investor questions answered within a day, and diligence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Put term sheets side by side and show what each costs in the round after. Draw up illustrative analysis and counsel the CEO on the right strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hold the story in one version, drafted with the CEO. The same claims and numbers across the deck, the model and the data room.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the investor-facing model: scenarios, unit economics and use of funds. Every number ties to one the CFO has signed.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Between rounds</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Refresh the deck, the KPI pack and the data room every quarter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write investor and board updates. Answer existing investors' questions. Track what we promised them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with investors so you can source your own relationships for future rounds</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read the market: who invests at our stage, on what terms, and what comparable companies showed when they raised. Put what Relay must show, and by when, to the leadership team in writing.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Across both</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agree in writing with each function what it produces for a raise and by when. Flag the proof the story needs a quarter early, not the week before.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the record: what each investor asked, what we answered, what we promised and what we learned.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>By the end of your first six months</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An investor map with a reason beside every name.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">One version of the story across the deck, the model and the data room.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A data room refreshed every quarter, never rebuilt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A written agreement with each function on what it produces for a raise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear line of sight to a closed round from a ranked list of investors.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have run a growth-stage equity round from inside a company, or worked on several from the investing side. You want to own the process, with a view to owning the pitch and fundraising function in the future as the company scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We don't ask for a set number of years or a particular firm on your CV. We ask for evidence. Be ready to walk us through specific rounds and your part in them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Round experience:</strong> you ran an equity round from inside a company, or worked on several as an investor. You can show the map you built, the order you ran it in and what you would change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Investor writing:</strong> you turn the story a founder tells in a room into a page an investor reads alone. Short, plain, in a founder's voice, with numbers that held under diligence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Modelling:</strong> you built an investor model from a company's internal forecast and defended it in diligence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Terms:</strong> you can put two term sheets side by side and say what each costs in the round after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data rooms:</strong> you built one that answered questions before they were asked. You can name the question you missed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Getting work from other teams:</strong> you got inputs from teams that did not report to you, on dates agreed in writing. You can say what arrived late and what you did about it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market knowledge:</strong> you know which funds invest at our stage and which partner leads, or can build that picture in weeks and show your working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Handling no:</strong> investors have told you no. You kept the record of why and used it the next time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in logistics, delivery, marketplaces or another operations-heavy business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time at a growth-stage fund, a tech-focused bank or a private-capital adviser before going in-house.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investor relations between rounds at a private company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The hard parts</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The CEO pitches. You are the investors' contact for everything around the room. You are judged on how the round runs, not on the pitch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The numbers come from the CFO. The proof comes from teams that do not report to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The market sets the timing, not us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investors will say no, often. The record has to stay straight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The job keeps going after the close: the map, the materials in quiet quarters and the relationships between rounds. We will agree with you what support you need to do that well.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we hire</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Talent Acquisition, 45 minutes:</strong> the job as it is, a round you ran or worked on, and how you work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An interview with our VP International: 45 minutes:</strong> how you work, the evidence and across your whole career</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The case, about a day on your own time</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case review, 75 minutes, with the CEO and CFO:</strong> you walk us through it, re-plan live when we change a condition, and take two questions the case cannot reach .</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>References and a decision within a week.</strong> An offer comes in a conversation.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tell us at any stage if you need adjustments. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who Thrives at Relay?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Aim with Precision:</strong> You define problems clearly and measure your impact meticulously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to Win:</strong> You chase bold bets, tackle the hard stuff, and view constraints as fuel, not friction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1% Better Every Day</strong>: You believe that small, consistent improvements lead to exponential growth. You move quickly, deliver results, and learn from every experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>All In, All the Time</strong>: You show up and step up. You take ownership from start to finish and do what it takes to deliver when it counts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People-Powered Greatness</strong>: You invest in your teammates. You give and receive feedback with care and candour. You build trust through high standards and shared success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow the Whole Pie</strong>: You seek out win-win solutions for merchants, couriers, and our customers, because when they thrive, so do we.<br /><br />If these resonate, and you combine strong technical fundamentals with entrepreneurial drive, let’s connect.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Relay is an <strong>equal-opportunity employer </strong>committed to diversity, inclusion, and fostering a workplace where everyone thrives.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/relay/head-of-capital-london-210390","tags":["Central Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London - On-site","created_at":1793396419},{"slug":"support-operations-analyst-united-kingdom-392059","company_name":"Aveni","title":"Support Operations Analyst","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job title: Support Operations Analyst</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reporting to: Support Lead</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: Remote (UK based)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Are you curious, analytical, and eager to grow in the world of SaaS and AI?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aveni is an award-winning technology company. We use advanced AI to enable scalable efficiency for financial services companies, combining world-leading Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Large Language Model (LLM) expertise with deep financial services domain experience to drive enterprise-wide productivity. Aveni harnesses the power of voice to drive unprecedented efficiency and oversight. We’re using the latest in AI to automate and innovate, empowering businesses to achieve exceptional productivity and compliance outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Support Operations Analyst to help us scale how customer support works through AI, automation, knowledge and strong operational processes. A core part of the role will be owning and improving our AI support experience: increasing the proportion of customer requests resolved through AI and self-service, continuously improving the content and workflows that power it, and using conversation data to identify new opportunities for automation. You’ll stay close to customers by providing second-line support when needed, while also improving our knowledge, incident and problem management practices.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Support Operations Analyst, your primary focus will be making Support more scalable, proactive and effective. You’ll take day-to-day ownership of optimising our AI support agent, Intercom Fin, using performance data and conversation reviews to improve involvement, resolution and deflection. You’ll author and test AI content, tune workflows and routing, identify knowledge and automation gaps, and implement improvements that allow more customers to get the right answer without needing a human response. Alongside this, you’ll own key parts of our customer-facing knowledge and Support operations, help ensure we’re ready for product launches, coordinate customer-impacting incidents and recurring product issues, and provide second-line customer support where human investigation is required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Second-line Customer Support – Provide hands-on support for customer requests that require human investigation or cannot be resolved through AI or self-service. Troubleshoot issues, communicate clearly with customers and use these conversations to identify opportunities to improve Fin, documentation or product experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Incident &amp; Problem Management – Act as a Support point of contact during customer-impacting incidents: triage and escalate high-priority issues, coordinate with Engineering, maintain clear stakeholder and customer communications, and contribute recommendations that improve the process. For lower-impact bugs and recurring problems, work with Product and Engineering to maintain visibility and help ensure a healthy level of customer-impacting issues is picked up through sprint planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Investigation – Diagnose and troubleshoot technical issues, gather the right evidence and work confidently with Product and Engineering when deeper investigation is required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Knowledge – Develop a strong understanding of Aveni’s products to support users effectively and confidently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch &amp; Cross-functional Collaboration – Work with Product, Marketing, Training &amp; Enablement and Engineering to ensure Help Centre and Intercom content is accurate, and that customer documentation and Support readiness are in place for new features and product launches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI Support Optimisation – Take day-to-day ownership of optimising our AI customer support experience. At Aveni we use Intercom Fin, but experience with Zendesk AI or similar platforms is equally relevant. Author, test and continuously improve the content and instructions that power Fin; tune workflows, routing and hand-off paths; review customer conversations to identify new deflection and automation opportunities; and implement improvements that allow more requests to be resolved before reaching the Support team. Own regular reporting on AI involvement, resolution and deflection rates, using the data to identify trends, prioritise experiments and demonstrate the impact of changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge Management – Maintain and improve Help Centre content, FAQs and internal Support guidance, ensuring AI and human agents have accurate, useful knowledge to work from. Identify documentation gaps through conversation reviews, support trends and AI performance, and work with Product, Marketing and Training &amp; Enablement to close them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong interest in technology, SaaS, and AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid problem-solving skills with a proactive, solutions-focused mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear and confident communication skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts in simple terms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a customer-facing or technical support role, ideally within B2B SaaS, with confidence owning customer issues from first contact through to resolution or escalation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience optimising AI customer support platforms such as Intercom Fin, Zendesk AI or similar. We’re looking for evidence that you have actively improved how an AI agent performs — for example by authoring and testing content, tuning workflows or routing, reviewing conversations for deflection opportunities, and using involvement, resolution or deflection reporting to drive measurable improvements. Direct Fin experience isn't essential; the track record matters more than the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience maintaining customer-facing knowledge bases or Help Centres and turning support trends into clear, useful documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team player who is comfortable working both remotely and independently.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous experience in a B2B SaaS or fintech environment, particularly supporting complex or regulated customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing or running experiments to improve AI agents, automation or self-service journeys in a customer support environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using support and AI metrics such as SLA, CSAT, involvement, resolution and escalation trends to identify and prioritise improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with incident and problem management practices, including escalation, stakeholder communication, root cause analysis and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with Product and Engineering during high-priority incidents and managing lower-impact bugs through a backlog or sprint-based development process.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What We Offer</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative and innovative work environment with career growth opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">34 days holiday plus your birthday off (inclusive of bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share options – we believe in shared success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skills development – continuous learning is at our core, expect the development to be front and centre of everything you do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote and flexible working – remote, co-working spaces, or a mix of both</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Life insurance, income protection and private health care</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Freebies and discounts at a range of retailers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Emotional wellbeing (Employee assistance programme provides access to 24/7 employee counselling and emotional support)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle to work scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension scheme (employer contribution matched up to 5%)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join Us in Making a Difference</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Aveni, we believe that diversity drives innovation. We're committed to building a team that reflects the diverse communities we serve and creating an inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued and empowered to contribute their best work. If you're passionate about leveraging technology to drive positive change and want to be part of a team that's shaping the future of financial services, we'd love to hear from you. We know that some people are likely to only apply where they meet 100% of requirements, but we’d like to hear from you anyway.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply now to join us on our mission to transform the financial services industry through AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/aveni/support-operations-analyst-united-kingdom-392059","tags":["Customer"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1793396418},{"slug":"customer-success-team-leader-london-281168","company_name":"Allica Bank","title":"Customer Success Team Leader","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Allica Bank</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Allica is the UK’s fastest growing company - and the fastest-growing financial technology (Fintech) firm ever. Our purpose is to help established SMEs, one of the last major underserved opportunities in Fintech.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Established SMEs are the backbone of local communities - representing over a third of our economy - yet have been largely neglected both by traditional high street banks and modern fintech providers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Description</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Customer Success Team Lead, you’ll lead a team of approximately five Customer Success Executives. Together, you’ll help qualified SME prospects move through their onboarding journey, converting leads into open, funded and actively used Allica business current accounts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll coach your team to have confident, consultative conversations with business owners and decision-makers—understanding their existing banking challenges, explaining Allica’s value proposition and supporting them as they switch to Allica.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be accountable for team performance across the full onboarding journey, while ensuring every prospective customer receives a consistently excellent experience and a strong first impression of Allica Bank.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a highly collaborative role. You’ll work closely with Relationship Management, Product, Marketing, Growth, Data, Customer Due Diligence and Operations to improve the onboarding experience, remove friction and create better outcomes for customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Principal Accountabilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with the Sales Managers of Customer Success, The Customer Success Team Leader will provide line management, capacity planning, pipeline management, coaching and development to support a team of Customer Success Executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach team members to engage SME decision-makers confidently by telephone and email, using a consultative approach to understand their needs and banking pain points.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Through close collaboration with our Customer Due Diligence, operations leaders and product teams, the Customer Success Team Leader will work to support reducing friction and improving the experience in the customer onboarding journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding our onboarding process and requirements and supporting customers and prospects through this process to open current accounts and deliver a great customer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gaining feedback from customers and prospects on potential future features they need and want from their bank and bank account and feeding these into the Product teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with our Growth, Marketing and Data teams to feedback your learnings from customer interactions, helping us to drive ever better customer outcomes, targeting, segmentation and messaging.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal Attributes &amp; Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have managed and led a team either in person or remotely to successfully achieve KPIs relating to customer and colleague experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You should have a general understanding of SME financial products (eg payments, lending, accounting, CRM), and ideally specific expertise in business current accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have a proven track record in telephone-based lead generation with established SMEs (typically 5-250 employee firms), including business development from cold prospects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have excellent interpersonal and communication skills, together with evidence of outperformance in similar roles through earning customer and colleague trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will demonstrate the ability to work collaboratively with specialist colleagues such as Relationship Managers, Operations, KYCB and underwriters, to deliver a positive outcome for our customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll have a proven track record of exceeding targets, providing excellent customer service generating new income opportunities and always considering risk and reputation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working collaboratively with specialist teams such as Relationship Managers, Operations, KYC/CDD teams and underwriters.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working at Allica Bank</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Allica Bank we want to ensure our employees have the right tools and environment in which to succeed in their role and in support of our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our employees are at the heart of everything we do, so our benefits are designed with you in mind:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full onboarding support and continued development opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Options for flexible working</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular social activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discretionary bonus scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health cover</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Life assurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Family friendly policies including enhanced Maternity &amp; Paternity leave</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Don’t tick every box?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don’t worry if you don’t have all the skills or requirements listed on the job description. If you think you’ll be a good fit, we’d still love to hear from you!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible working</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know the ‘9-to-5’ isn’t right for everyone. That’s why Allica Bank is fully committed to flexible and hybrid working. Please let us know what is best for you and, if we can, we will do our best to accommodate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a diverse bunch here at Allica, with all kinds of experiences, backgrounds and lifestyles. Our openness and differences make us stronger, and we want everybody to feel comfortable bringing as much of themselves to work with them as they like.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/allica-bank/customer-success-team-leader-london-281168","tags":["Distribution"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1793396418},{"slug":"lending-completions-officer-milton-keynes-213838","company_name":"Allica Bank","title":"Lending Completions Officer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Allica Bank</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Allica is the UK’s fastest growing company - and the fastest-growing financial technology (Fintech) firm ever. Our purpose is to help established SMEs, one of the last major underserved opportunities in Fintech.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Established SMEs are the backbone of local communities - representing over a third of our economy - yet have been largely neglected both by traditional high street banks and modern fintech providers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Description</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a key role in delivering a fast, accurate and well-controlled lending journey. You will manage a portfolio of cases from offer and post-sanction administration through to drawdown and completion, making sure every case is progressed efficiently and every condition is properly satisfied.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial mortgages will be a core part of the role, alongside other commercial lending products such as GGS loans, overdrafts, business loans, asset finance, non-property-backed lending and unsecured lending. You will work closely with Relationship Managers, Underwriting, legal and valuation partners and other teams across the bank.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Principal Accountabilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage a pipeline of lending cases from offer to completion, meeting service levels, quality standards and expected completion timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver post-sanction administration, including releasing communications, instructing legal and valuation partners and coordinating payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and satisfy Conditions Precedent and other completion requirements, escalating risks, gaps and delays early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate drawdown and completion activity accurately, ensuring the right approvals, documentation and controls are in place.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build effective working relationships with Relationship Managers, Underwriting, solicitors, valuers and other internal and external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain clear, accurate and audit-ready case records, including sanction audit trails, customer records and updates to the core banking system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate relevant information clearly so that colleagues and decision-makers understand the position, risks and actions required