ination role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver bar-raising legal engineers each quarter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own a robust, fair and fast recruiting process that is optimized to hire the best talent vs the best interviewers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Map legal talent across law firms, in-house teams, legal ops and legal tech, and build pipelines before roles open</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess what matters: legal judgment, comfort with AI and data, and the ability to work with customers and engineers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with stakeholders on how the archetype of who we hire changes as the market does</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report on your funnel every week and fix what the data shows</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><h3><strong>Essential</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of full-cycle recruiting, with at least some exposure of hiring in legal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are quick at onboarding into a new area; you are able to get a deep understanding of a new role and/or new area and quickly present yourself as a knowledgeable voice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record you can put numbers on: hires per quarter, offer acceptance, how your hires performed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most of your recent hires sourced by you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency with Ashby or a similar ATS, and real use of AI in your own workflow</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Valued</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hired for a legal tech or AI company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hired hybrid roles that blend a profession with product or engineering</p