&lt;p&gt;So we expanded into software and started building integrated, omnichannel solutions – to help sellers sell online, manage inventory, offer buy now, pay later functionality, book appointments, engage loyal buyers, and hire and pay staff. Across it all, we&#39;ve embedded financial services tools at the point of sale, so merchants can access a business loan and manage their cash flow in one place. Afterpay furthers our goal to provide omnichannel tools that unlock meaningful value and growth, enabling sellers to capture the next generation shopper, increase order sizes, and compete at a larger scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we are a partner to sellers of all sizes – large, enterprise-scale businesses with complex operations, sellers just starting, as well as merchants who began selling with Square and have grown larger over time. As our sellers grow, so do our solutions. There is a massive opportunity in front of us. We&#39;re building a significant, meaningful, and lasting business, and we are helping sellers worldwide do the same.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Square is seeking a Senior Partnerships Manager to source, negotiate, and scale partnerships that fuel Square seller acquisition, retention, and business growth across the United Kingdom. Partners include referral networks, distributors, service providers, technology platforms, and strategic ecosystems where there is mutual benefit through lead generation, co-sell, co-marketing, and product enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, hands-on role at the intersection of business development, growth, product, and go-to-market strategy. You will own the end-to-end lifecycle of strategic partnerships — from sourcing and deal structuring through to activation and ongoing optimisation — with a focus on creating partnerships that deliver incredible user experiences for Square sellers. You will work in tight collaboration with Product Marketing to shape partner narratives, positioning, and GTM motions, and partner cross-functionally to drive measurable growth outcomes for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sourcing &amp;amp; Deal Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify, evaluate, and secure high-impact partners; lead negotiations and close large-scale partnership deals and product integrations that advance Square&#39;s capabilities and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Partnership Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate closely with Product and Product Marketing to design partnership experiences that delight sellers — ensuring integrations are seamless, valuable, and well-positioned in market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver measurable results in lead generation, seller acquisition, and pipeline contribution through your portfolio of strategic partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activation &amp;amp; Scaling:&lt;/strong&gt; Launch partnerships with clear GTM plans, co-marketing &lt;br&gt;initiatives, and integrated roadmaps; work hand-in-hand with Product Marketing to bring partnerships to life for sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Relationship Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and sustain senior-level relationships with partners, ensuring long-term value creation and mutual growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Product, Product Marketing, Operations, Marketing, Sales, and Legal to ensure smooth execution and maximum impact. Bring an ownership mentality to how the team operates — actively contributing to team processes, rituals, and ways of working that make us better together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement &amp;amp; Optimisation:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and track KPIs for partnership success, adjusting strategy and tactics as needed to drive continuous growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in business development, strategic partnerships, and/or product partnerships, with demonstrated progression in scope and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience sourcing, negotiating, and closing large-scale partnerships and product integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills with Product Marketing; experience shaping partner positioning, co-marketing, and GTM narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to connect partnership strategy directly to measurable seller acquisition and revenue outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with a broad range of teams, with an ownership mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation and relationship management skills, with experience engaging at the executive level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS, fintech, or payments background strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re working to build a more inclusive economy where our customers have equal access to opportunity, and we strive to live by these same values in building our workplace. Block is a proud equal opportunity employer. We work hard to evaluate all employees and job applicants consistently, based solely on the core competencies required of the role at hand, and without regard to any legally protected class. We believe in being fair, and are committed to an inclusive interview experience, including providing reasonable accommodations to disabled applicants throughout the recruitment process. We encourage applicants to share any needed accommodations with their recruiter, who will treat these requests as confidentially as possible. &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Want to learn more about what we&#39;re doing to build an inclusive workplace? Check out our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/news/inclusion&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Inclusion &amp;amp; Diversity page&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Guidelines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may submit up to 9 active applications within a 60-day period. Reapplications to the same role are accepted 90 days after a previous application has been reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use of AI in Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We may use automated AI tools to evaluate job applications for efficiency and consistency. These tools comply with local regulations, including bias audits, and we handle all personal data in accordance with state and local privacy laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contact us &lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.block.xyz/privacyportal/form&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;with hiring practice or data usage questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Every benefit we offer is designed with one goal: empowering you to do the best work of your career while building the life you want. Remote work, medical insurance, flexible time off, retirement savings plans, and modern family planning are just some of our offering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://block.xyz/employee-benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://block.xyz/documents/benefits.pdf&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Check out our other benefits at Block.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Block, Inc. (NYSE: XYZ) builds technology to increase access to the global economy. Each of our brands unlocks different aspects of the economy for more people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Square&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;makes commerce and financial services accessible to sellers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Cash App&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the easy way to spend, send, and store money.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Afterpay&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is transforming the way customers manage their spending over time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;TIDAL&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a music platform that empowers artists to thrive as entrepreneurs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Bitkey&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a simple self-custody wallet built for bitcoin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Proto&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a suite of bitcoin mining products and services. Together, we’re helping build a financial system that is open to everyone.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://block.xyz/en/legal/applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/channel-sales-support-agent-block/senior-partnerships-manager-uk-london-482580","tags":["20244 S&M - Marketing - Square Partnerships"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793386525},{"slug":"senior-director-destination-management-supply-london-15243","company_name":"tripadvisor","title":"Senior Director, Destination Management, Supply","description":"&lt;p&gt;Senior Director, Destination Management, Supply I Tripadvisor&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tripadvisor&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Tripadvisor Group connects people to experiences worth sharing, and aims to be the world’s most trusted source for travel and experiences. We leverage our brands, technology, and capabilities to connect our global audience with partners through rich content, travel guidance, and two-sided marketplaces for experiences, accommodations, restaurants, and other travel categories. The subsidiaries of Tripadvisor, Inc. (Nasdaq: TRIP), include a portfolio of travel brands and businesses, including Tripadvisor, Viator, and TheFork.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tripadvisor Experiences is the world&#39;s leading marketplace for tours, activities, and experiences. Our mission is to bring more wonder to the world by delivering exceptional experiences to travelers wherever they are. We offer an unparalleled opportunity to be part of the future of the travel experiences industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Chief Commercial Officer, Experiences, the Senior Director of Destination Management leads Viator&#39;s global destination management team. You will bring a deep understanding of the global operator community and use it to develop strategies that solve business problems and support our mutual goal with operators: delivering exceptional experiences to travelers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an operational role. You will be expected to deliver significant business outcomes by leading and motivating a global team, with decisive leadership and a strong bias for action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Job Location: Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is a hybrid position that requires 2 to 3 days per week in our London Office.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operator Community and Destination Strategy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hold a deep, current understanding of the operator community: its needs, economics, competitive options and pain points. Use it to shape how we win and retain supply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the 3 year destination management strategy and translate it into clear regional charters and measurable KPIs, growing revenue and market share in leading destinations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop strategies that solve business problems for both operators and Viator, in support of delivering exceptional traveler experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own financial rigor: use fresh business data and pacing to steer the business, and help your team understand the financial impact of its decisions and be accountable for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team Leadership and Talent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Act as chief architect of the global destination management organization. Lead and mentor Regional Managers, and design an organization and operating model that fits the business as it evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set and hold the hiring bar, run rigorous and consistent performance management, and calibrate with peers across Supply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and retain top talent, and maintain a leadership bench and succession plan for Regional Manager roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set the standard for leadership: humble, open to feedback, and skilled at leading teams through change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be clear on what each person and region owns, and hold them accountable for it. Push decisions to the lowest appropriate level while stepping in personally on cross-regional or cross-functional problems no one else owns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data-Driven Decision Making&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set the standard for hypothesis quality and test design. Define what the team needs to learn, require evidence and experimentation over opinion, and prioritize what operators and travelers actually do over what they say.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connectivity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure industry-leading connectivity with the features and support operators need. Oversee the connectivity support team and partner with R&amp;amp;D to build enhanced connectivity features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation and AI&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive innovation by bringing in outside ideas through industry conferences, councils and competitor insight, and share what works across functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advocate for and implement AI and automation to transform productivity and quality, including rethinking roles and workflows. Scale proven wins across regions, build team AI skills, and use AI responsibly within our governance and data-privacy guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monitor competitive dynamics, regulatory environments and industry trends affecting supply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Align with Supply Sales, Marketing, R&amp;amp;D and Support, and act as an integrator on OKRs and problems that cut across functions, so operators and customers have a seamless end-to-end experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner as one team across Supply and Tripadvisor Experiences, and hold cross-functional partners accountable as well as being held accountable by them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experi&lt;/strong&gt;ence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Leadership: 10+ years leading and scaling global teams in market management, account management or a combination, including leading managers of managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operator and Marketplace Expertise: Extensive experience with two-sided marketplaces, a deep understanding of supply-side dynamics, technologies and operator communities, ideally in travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategic Thinking: A track record of setting multi-year strategy and turning it into goals, KPIs and results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operational Excellence: Data-driven operational leadership with a strong bias for action. Skilled at KPIs, pacing and scalable processes to improve global efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quality Orientation: Experience defining and enforcing quality standards across a catalog or supplier base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tech Savvy and AI Proficiency: A proven history of using AI and technology to improve business outcomes and create transformational change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commercial Acumen: Strong commercial and financial acumen, with advanced negotiation and relationship management skills to build and sustain key operator partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inspirational Leader: An authentic, humble leader who builds trust, develops talent and cultivates a winning culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation packages (routinely benchmarked against the latest industry data), including base salary and annual bonuses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;“Work your way” with flexibility to suit your lifestyle. Tripadvisor Group takes a remote-friendly approach to collaboration across a worldwide team, with the option to join on-site as often as you’d like or as required by your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible schedule. Work-life balance is ingrained in our culture by design. Trust and accountability make it work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Donation matching. Give back? Give more! We match qualifying charitable donations annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance. Want to level up your career? We love to hear it! Receive annual support for qualified programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle benefit. An annual benefit to spend on yourself. Use it on travel, wellness, or whatever suits you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel perks. We believe that travel is employee development, so we provide discounts and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee assistance program. We’re here for you with resources and programs to help you through life’s challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health benefits. We offer great coverage and competitive premiums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous referral scheme. Help us grow and be rewarded with generous awards for referring successful candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Cultural Pillars:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Traveler first&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We exist to create value for our customer, the traveler. We enable our suppliers and partners to unlock this value. Their collective behaviors and insights are what drives us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution is our edge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We act fast, experiment, learn from failure, iterate, and improve the solutions of tomorrow across every aspect of our business. Our execution is agile, data-driven, prioritised, and built to scale. We assume no problem is someone else’s problem and finish what can be done today, knowing tomorrow will bring fresh challenges.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We succeed together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best outcomes are driven by empathic, humble, and diverse subject matter experts working toward shared goals. We collaborate relentlessly, challenge assumptions, give actionable feedback, and set each other up for success through empowered teams with a clear charter. We transparently take ownership of our growth, individually and as a team. We celebrate the quality of our effort, our learnings, and our collective achievements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to create an accessible and inclusive experience for all candidates. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please make sure to reach out to your individual recruiter or our team at -----
&lt;p&gt;If you have any additional questions about careers at Tripadvisor you can email us at ----- We have all the answers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
