="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About the team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Legal team at Airwallex is a collaborative group of legal minds and risk management experts. We're passionate about safeguarding Airwallex's operations, fostering a culture of compliance and ethical conduct, and ensuring we navigate the global financial landscape with integrity. We provide expert guidance and support to all areas of the business, proactively identifying, mitigating, and managing legal and financial risks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is looking for an experienced (Senior) Counsel to support our fast growing commercial legal team across EMEA. You will support a complex set of fintech products that will challenge your problem solving and critical thinking skills. You will support a wide variety of commercial legal matters supporting Airwallex’s growing Sales team, and help us build for scale in several EMEA markets, ranging from Germany, Israel, France, the Netherlands to the UK. This is a strategic position and you will be a key advisor to Airwallex’s EMEA go-to-market Commercial team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This position is based in Amsterdam, the Netherlands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive complex deals. </strong>Personally lead negotiations on high-stakes enterprise commercial and strategic partnership deals across EMEA (with a strong emphasis on our UK, NL, and IL business), many with significant cross-border elements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build for scale. </strong>Develop and implement an innovative strategy for delivering efficient and effective commercial legal support. Drive the creation and maintenance of scalable templates, playbooks, and processes to support our rapidly growing business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a strategic partner. </strong>Act as a key advisor to our dynamic, globally distributed commercial leadership. Partner with the Commercial team to scale our go-to-market efforts and advance multi-product and multi-jurisdictional deal strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhance Efficiency</strong>. Learn from our data and operations teams to leverage technology, automation, and data-driven insights to increase the efficiency and impact of the Commercial Legal function.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborate Globally. </strong>Work closely and effectively with Airwallex’s global legal, compliance, and risk teams on deals and projects that involve multiple jurisdictions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contribute to Culture</strong>. Make a positive contribution to the culture of the Airwallex legal team, the EMEA team, and the company as a whole.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for people who meet the minimum qualifications for this role. The preferred qualifications are great to have, but are not mandatory.</p><h3><strong>Must-Haves:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring 5-8 years of legal experience, with experience in private practice at a top law firm. Additional in-house experience at a fintech is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication, drafting, negotiation, and writing skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to explain complex legal concepts to various non-legal audiences, and the ability to manage and prioritize multiple projects and deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High motivation and the ability to operate independently and pivot quickly within a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A learner’s mentality: you are consistently looking to take on new and diverse challenges and expand your knowledge beyond your current areas of expertise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative and empathetic mindset, a good sense of humor, and a keen understanding of how to work effectively with colleagues from different teams and backgrounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to translate complex legal and risk issues into clear, succinct, and actionable guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High integrity, sound judgment, and an unflappable demeanor and collaborative style of working</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-Haves:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a fintech or in the banking industry or high-growth and/or globally distributed company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience drafting and negotiating technology transactions, SaaS agreements, and other customer-facing services agreements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">French/German/Spanish language skills preferred</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Applicant Safety Policy: Fraud and Third-Party Recruiters</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To protect you from recruitment scams, please be aware that Airwallex will not ask for bank details, sensitive ID numbers (i.e. passport), or any form of payment during the application or interview process. All official communication will come from an @</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://airwallex.com"><em>airwallex.com</em></a><em> email address. Please apply only through </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://careers.airwallex.com"><em><u>careers.airwallex.com</u></em></a><em> or our official LinkedIn page.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Airwallex does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firms/recruiters.  Airwallex will not pay any fees to search firms/recruiters if a candidate is submitted by a search firm/recruiter unless an agreement has been entered into with respect to specific open position(s).  Search firms/recruiters submitting resumes to Airwallex on an unsolicited basis shall be deemed to accept this condition, regardless of any other provision to the contrary.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and anyone seeking employment at Airwallex is considered based on merit, qualifications, competence and talent. We don’t regard color, religion, race, national origin, sexual orientation, ancestry, citizenship, sex, marital or family status, disability, gender, or any other legally protected status when making our hiring decisions. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/airwallex/commercial-legal-counsel-emea-amsterdam-192379","tags":["Legal"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"NL - Amsterdam","created_at":1793137216},{"slug":"3d-packaging-engineer-delft-146296","company_name":"Quantware","title":"3D Packaging Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>About Us </strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">QuantWare is building the world’s most powerful quantum processors to solve humanity's greatest challenges. We do this with our unique VIO™ technology, the only QPU architecture that breaks the hardware barriers that have held quantum computing back, unlocking the path to MegaQubit quantum processors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With VIO, we are paving the way for the hyper-scale quantum computers that will change the world. And delivering on that vision demands people who don’t shy away from tackling the hardest challenges of our time. That’s where you come in! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>3D Packaging Engineer</strong>, you will collaborate closely with our engineering team to physically realize our VIO products. You will operate, adapt, and fine-tune high-precision assembly equipment to meet the precise tolerances required for optimal device performance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling Adaptation:</strong> Assist in modifying and calibrating high-precision assembly equipment (e.g., flip-chip bonders, die attach machines) to meet unique quantum 3D integration specifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Optimization:</strong> Help develop and refine placement and bonding processes (thermo-compression bonding, laser-assisted bonding, coldwelding) for non-standard substrates. Test adhesives, glues, and solders to determine which materials survive extreme thermal cycling and cryogenic vacuum conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3D Assembly Execution:</strong> Execute complex integration strategies, including multi-die stacking, interposer-based 3D architectures, and orthogonal (vertical) chip placement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> BS, MS, or PhD in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Physics, Materials Science, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling Experience:</strong> 3–5 years of hands-on experience operating and adjusting high-accuracy semiconductor assembly platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Precision Assembly:</strong> Demonstrated experience achieving tight placement tolerances (around 1µm) in an R&amp;D or pilot production environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3D Integration Knowledge:</strong> Solid foundational understanding of 3D integration (TSVs, micro-bumps, interposers) and how structural materials behave under thermal stress, high vacuum, or cryogenic conditions.</p></li></ul><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don't tick every box? Apply anyway! Research shows women often self-select out if they don't meet every requirement. Here's our take: nobody ticks every box. This is a description of our ideal candidate, not a filter. If most resonates and you're keen to learn the gaps, apply. We hire for trajectory, not perfection. <br /><br /><strong>What We Offer:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At QuantWare, you’ll be part of a high-performing team of world-class experts in an ambitious, fast-moving environment. From day one, you’ll have the trust, tools, and support to do your best work. Here’s what you can expect:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive salary</strong> - A salary that reflects the impact and importance of the role (and of course 8% holiday allowance)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension that’s built to last</strong> - A generous and future-proof pension plan that includes partner and dependent coverage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility built on trust</strong> - We focus on outcomes. Work flexibly, in a hybrid setup, with an open vacation policy that lets you manage your time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth</strong> - We invest in your L&amp;D, with a budget available to each team member, dependent on their individual ambitions, development needs, and performance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A connected team</strong> - We make space to celebrate wins together, with team events, offsites, and spontaneous moments that bring us closer<br /><br /><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion at QuantWare</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an ambitious company, not only for our goals but also to become an even more diverse and inclusive team. We know great candidates don't always follow a straight path, and we value diverse experience, perspectives, and ways of thinking. We know this helps us make better decisions, drives more innovation, and strengthens our culture. <br /><br /><em>As part of our recruitment process, candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening.</em></p><h2></h2><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/quantware/3d-packaging-engineer-delft-146296","tags":["Research & Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1793126439},{"slug":"rd-software-engineer-delft-423044","company_name":"Quantware","title":"R&D - Software Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>About Us </strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">QuantWare is building the world’s most powerful quantum processors to solve humanity's greatest challenges. We do this with our unique VIO™ technology, the only QPU architecture that breaks the hardware barriers that have held quantum computing back, unlocking the path to MegaQubit quantum processors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With VIO, we are paving the way for the hyper-scale quantum computers that will change the world. And delivering on that vision demands people who don’t shy away from tackling the hardest challenges of our time. That’s where you come in! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an <strong>R&amp;D Software Engineer</strong> to bring production-grade software and data practices into our R&amp;D measurement work. As we scale up VIO, our measurement data, metadata, and codebase are growing fast. You will take our existing measurement software and data practices to the next level, making them robust and maintainable, and building on how we organize data so it supports analysis, yield, and root cause investigations at scale. As channel counts grow, PCMs and test vehicles multiply, and test setups become more varied, you will standardize our experimental workflows so measurement throughput never becomes the bottleneck.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also be the link between R&amp;D, the software team in Product, and the data team in Operations, so our efforts stay aligned.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data management:</strong> Develop and maintain how R&amp;D measurement data and metadata are stored, linking each device to its related tests, components, and setup history, so cross-device comparisons and yield questions become a quick query.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement software:</strong> Turn measurement prototypes from experimental physicists and RF test engineers into robust, tested, maintainable code, and maintain the R&amp;D measurement codebase for VIO devices, their components, and PCM test vehicles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Code architecture &amp; quality:</strong> Review, refactor, and maintain modular Python code following modern software practices (automated testing with PyTest, CI/CD, documentation, version control).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work day-to-day with experimental physicists, RF test engineers and electrical engineers to improve their measurement code, and connect R&amp;D with the software team in Product to bring in best practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> Own R&amp;D software functionality through validation, review, and integration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc in Computer Science, Electrical/Computer Engineering, or similar, plus 3+ years of industry experience (must).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building software that interacts with hardware, such as in the context of manufacturing companies, test and measurement systems, lab or factory automation, or control systems (must). </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience in control of test and measurement equipment is a plus, and experience in a quantum device foundry or test facility is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python, with a track record of improving and maintaining code for data acquisition, automation, or scientific pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with databases and cloud computing suites like GCP and AWS for technical or experimental data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of best practices, including object-oriented design, Git, code review, and testing frameworks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong drive to eliminate manual measurement and analysis overhead.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in a multidisciplinary scale-up, translating between experimental hardware teams and production software, and aligning with other teams working on data and software (Ops, Product).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don't tick every box? Apply anyway! Research shows women often self-select out if they don't meet every requirement. Here's our take: nobody ticks every box. This is a description of our ideal candidate, not a filter. If most resonates and you're keen to learn the gaps, apply. We hire for trajectory, not perfection. <br /><br /><strong>What We Offer:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At QuantWare, you’ll be part of a high-performing team of world-class experts in an ambitious, fast-moving environment. From day one, you’ll have the trust, tools, and support to do your best work. Here’s what you can expect:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive salary</strong> - A salary that reflects the impact and importance of the role (and of course 8% holiday allowance)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension that’s built to last</strong> - A generous and future-proof pension plan that includes partner and dependent coverage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility built on trust</strong> - We focus on outcomes. Work flexibly, in a hybrid setup, with an open vacation policy that lets you manage your time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth</strong> - We invest in your L&amp;D, with a budget available to each team member, dependent on their individual ambitions, development needs, and performance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A connected team</strong> - We make space to celebrate wins together, with team events, offsites, and spontaneous moments that bring us closer<br /><br /><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion at QuantWare</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an ambitious company, not only for our goals but also to become an even more diverse and inclusive team. We know great candidates don't always follow a straight path, and we value diverse experience, perspectives, and ways of thinking. We know this helps us make better decisions, drives more innovation, and strengthens our culture. <br /><br /><em>As part of our recruitment process, candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening.</em></p><h2></h2><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/quantware/rd-software-engineer-delft-423044","tags":["Research & Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1793126439},{"slug":"interim-qa-specialist-utrecht-458492","company_name":"Rentman","title":"Interim QA Specialist","description":"<h1><strong>About us</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rentman is a B2B SaaS scale-up building a smart, powerful operations management platform to support event and media production teams. Our users plan everything from small shoots to massive festivals in 70+ countries, and they all rely on Rentman to keep their gear, people, and timing perfectly in sync. We’re based in Utrecht (NL) with a second office in Toronto (CA), and our 100+ team members work in a culture that’s open, flat, and inclusive, where curiosity drives us, ownership matters, and everyone has the freedom to challenge ideas and make an impact. Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://rentman.io/public-roadmap">public roadmap</a> to see what’s coming next!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/1abd1b97-44fa-4e7c-92e0-d04d95cf059f/Screenshot_2026-07-22_at_17.03.37.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Mission of this role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an interim Senior QA Specialist at Rentman, you make sure every release reaches customers without regressions. You own the test strategy across our 3 product teams and finish moving regression testing from a manual release-day cycle to an automated, shift-left E2E suite. Without this role, quality depends on manual testing on release day, bugs show up in staging or production, and the move to automated testing stalls. This is an interim position: the duration is still to be confirmed, and the role ends once the assignment is complete.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you'll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join refinement with the product teams and write Gherkin (Given/When/Then) acceptance specs that developers turn into tests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test new features on staging, going beyond the acceptance criteria to find edge cases, and file clear, reproducible bug reports in Jira</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review Playwright tests (TypeScript) in the frontend repo, and review developer-written tests in pull requests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the daily automated regression run in GitHub Actions, triage failures the same day, and fix flaky tests at the root cause</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run release-day regression and the OWASP ZAP security scan for each release, and give a clear go / no-go call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Migrate the remaining legacy tests and decide what is worth automating and what stays manual</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise cross-team QA days and coach developers so they own their tests</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/3c95dc18-9519-4446-b1af-13a805537681/Screenshot_2026-07-23_at_10.38.46.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we are looking for </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in QA on web applications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 2 years writing and maintaining UI test automation in code (Playwright, Cypress or Selenium, ideally TypeScript/JavaScript), not only record-and-play tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong manual and exploratory testing, with bug reports developers can act on without follow-up questions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have defined a test strategy (what to automate, what to test manually, coverage), not only executed test cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running automated tests in CI (GitHub Actions or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get developers to adopt new habits 